package kgen

import (
	"bytes"
	"fmt"
	"sort"
	"strings"

	"github.com/adams-shaun/gorge/dirac/kop"
)

// OPS.md: the interpreter contract for everything dirac/kgen appended to kop,
// with the pool cards that use each item (from the generated table, so it
// never drifts) ordered by the number of decks that need it.

type opsDoc struct {
	label string // usage key (see opsUsage)
	title string
	text  string
}

// opsEntries is the semantic half of OPS.md. "Gorge" names the rule or
// gorge behaviour each item mirrors.
var opsEntries = []opsDoc{
	// --- control flow ---
	{"op:SkipUnless", "OpSkipUnless (Obj -, A skip, C CondID)", "Evaluate `Table.Conds[C]` (see Conds) against the resolving entry; if FALSE skip the next `A.N` instructions. Guards exactly one effect node: gorge (Forge's AbilityUtils) skips a node whose Condition* params fail but still resolves its Sub chain, so the guarded block never covers later nodes. No decision."},
	{"op:Charm", "OpCharm (core op, kgen layout)", "Mode block header: `C` = mode index, `A.N` = block length. Targets of a mode-only slot are flagged in `Ability.TgtModes`. Decision: the controller picks `ModesPick` (CharmNum$, 1 by default) of `NModes` modes, at least `ModesPick-ModesFew` (MinCharmNum$) and closing early with a Done once that minimum is met at cast/trigger time, before targets; slots whose modes were not chosen are not targeted. A charm that may repeat a mode (CanRepeatModes$; `Ability.RepMax` > 0) keeps a COUNT per mode in the mode byte (`kop.RepeatLayout`), lowers one block per instance a mode can be chosen, and sets `C` = `kop.CharmRepeat` | shift | width<<3 | instance<<5 | mode<<9: the block runs when the mode's count exceeds its instance. A targeted mode owns one template target slot (`TgtModes`); its later instances' targets sit in overflow slots from `NTargets` up, swapped into the template slot as their block runs. A Pawprint$ budget (`RepBudget`, per-mode `RepCost`; CR 700.2i) bounds the picks."},
	{"op:Branch", "OpBranch (Obj -, A skip, C branch)", "Branch block of the preceding OpChooseBranch: if branch `C` was not the one chosen, skip the next `A.N` instructions. No decision."},
	{"op:ChooseBranch", "OpChooseBranch (Obj chooser, A n)", "Decision for player Obj: choose one of the `A.N` OpBranch blocks that follow (indices 0..n-1). Branch index n (the last block) is gorge's FallbackAbility, run when none of the n branches can be chosen. Gorge: api:GenericChoice with Defined chooser and TempRemember Chooser (inside the branches the chooser is RefEach). Perforating Artist: each opponent chooses 'sacrifice a nonland permanent' or 'discard a card'; each branch is an OpUnlessPaid that, unpaid, loses 3 life."},
	{"op:ChooseBranch.C2", "OpChooseBranch C 2 (Obj You, A 2)", "An as-enters mode election in an ETB replacement program (gorge api:GenericChoice, Defined$ You, SetChosenMode$ True; the Tarkir Dragonstorm Sieges): the entering permanent's controller picks one of two modes (a ChGenBranch decision, mode = the choice index, asked as the colour election is) and the answer is stored in the permanent's chosen byte (gorge foldChoose \"mode\": ChosenModes). ShowChoice$ ExceptSelf is descriptive. Read by ExChosenMode and Gate{CtrMode}."},
	{"op:CopySpell", "OpCopySpell (Obj spell, A n, C flags)", "Copy the spell Obj (RefTriggerObj: the instant or sorcery whose cast triggered the ability; nothing when it has left the stack) `A` times. Each copy is a new card object (not a token) on the stack, controlled and owned by the ability's controller, with the spell's targets, modes, X and kicked status, put above the spell in creation order; it is not cast. Leaving the stack it ceases to exist (CR 704.5e). Obj may also be a target spell (RefTarget: Kitsa, Twincast; gorge effCopySpellAbility's targeted arm copies the first object target). `C&1` (MayChooseTarget$): as each copy is about to resolve its controller is asked for its target declaration (TgfDecl slot) a DkTarget whose options are the copy's current targets first (kept even when illegal) then the slot's other legal targets; the answer replaces the copy's cast-time targets (CR 707.10c). Stack overflow stalls the game. Gorge: api:CopySpellAbility Defined$ TriggeredSpellAbility (effects/copy.go; rules/stack.go resolveTop -> AskCopyTargets). Not modelled: the ask for a declaration of several objects (kept without asking)."},
	{"op:Ninjutsu", "OpNinjutsu (internal: AfNinjutsu's program)", "The ninjutsu resolution (CR 702.49b; gorge zone_change.go): if the source card is still in its owner's hand it enters the battlefield (ETB triggers), then is tapped (a Tap event, \"entered tapped\"), then attacks the defender the Return pick captured when that is still legal (gorge EnteringAttackLegal: a player, or a planeswalker the opponent still controls); it was never declared, so no Attacks trigger fires."},
	{"op:Demonstrate", "OpDemonstrate (Obj spell)", "Demonstrate (CR 702.144a; gorge effects/demonstrate.go effDemonstrate): the spell Obj (RefTriggerObj: the instant or sorcery whose cast triggered the ability; nothing when it has left the stack) first asks its controller yes/no (ChGenConfirm, gorge's demonstrate election). On no, nothing. On yes the controller copies the spell (as OpCopySpell) and then each opponent still in the game copies it in turn order; every copy keeps the original's targets (gorge's StackCopy mints carry no new-target election), and in a two-player game there is no second election (gorge asks only when several opponents could). A copy is not cast. Stack overflow stalls the game. Gorge: api:Demonstrate Defined$ TriggeredSpellAbility (effects/demonstrate.go, StackCopy), from the Demonstrate keyword's appended trigger (cards/kw_demonstrate.go)."},
	{"op:PutCounterAll", "OpPutCounterAll (A n, C counter kind, F filter)", "Each battlefield permanent matching F (evaluated once, before any counter is placed) gets `A` counters of kind C, seat 0's battlefield in entry order then seat 1's; each placement is its own counter event (counter-doubling replacements apply per permanent, CounterAddedOnce fires per permanent). `A <= 0` places nothing. No decision. Gorge: api:PutCounterAll (effects/counters.go effPutCounterAll, putCounterAllSweep); its exotic shapes (Placer$, ValidCards2$, ValidZone$, targets) are refused by kgen. Finneas, Ace Archer; Oakhollow Village."},
	{"op:DealDamageFrom", "OpDealDamageFrom (Obj source, A amount, C target Ref)", "The creature Obj deals `A` damage to the permanent in Ref C (a target slot), as OpBite but with an amount other than its power; nothing when either has left the battlefield. The creature is the damage source (replacement, prevention, deathtouch, lifelink). No decision. Gorge: DealDamage with DamageSource$ (Polliwallop: twice its power). B.N = 1 is the player mode (C = RefEachOpponent): the trigger object Obj, live or its last known information (CR 113.7a, 608.2h), deals `A` damage to each opponent through the replacements, then poison (infect) or life loss and lifelink for its controller, and the damage triggers (CR 120.3, 609.7; Champion of the Path, Pyrotechnic Performer, Ingris Stingerquill). A pure plus-N competition poses gorge's no-op CR 616.1 order ask before the pass deals (replPlusSrcPass), the answer re-executing the op with the additions summed; two competing player events (RefEachPlayer), or a noncommuting candidate, still stall (StallReplPlus)."},
	{"op:UntapAll", "OpUntapAll (F filter)", "Each TAPPED battlefield permanent matching F untaps, seat 0's battlefield in entry order then seat 1's; one with a stun counter loses the counter instead (CR 122.1d). Untaps triggers fire for the permanents that untapped. No decision. Gorge: api:UntapAll (effects/combatfx.go effUntapAll). Valley Floodcaller."},
	{"op:Amass", "OpAmass (Obj player, A n, B.N override|remember<<15, C token)", "Player Obj amasses A (CR 701.47; gorge effAmass): their first battlefield permanent (list order) with the printed Army subtype -- or, with none, each Army token of card C created (token doublers apply) -- gets A +1/+1 counters (replaceable; CounterAddedOnce) and the permanent override Table.Overrides[B.N&0xfff - 1] (\"also a <Type>\"); B.N bit 15 (RememberAmass$) remembers it. No Army choice: gorge takes the first. Angrath, Captain of Chaos."},
	{"op:Empower", "OpEmpower (Obj player, A n, B.N override, C token)", "Player Obj empowers n (CR 701.71a; gorge effEmpower): one Jace token they control -- a battlefield TOKEN whose layer-aware subtypes include Table.Overrides[B.N&0xfff - 1]'s AddSub (a non-token Jace never qualifies) -- gets n LOYALTY counters as one counter event (the counter replacements, CounterAddedOnce). With no candidate the u_empower token (card C, token doublers apply) is created even when n <= 0, each mint gets the override (\"also a Jace\", named \"Jace Token\"), and the counters go on it; two or more mints ask (ChGenBolster, gorge's counter_pick). n < 0 is 0. Reality Fracture."},
	{"op:AtEOT", "OpAtEOT (Obj, C)", "An AtEOT$ rider (gorge scheduleAtEOT): if Obj is on the battlefield, at the beginning of the next end step it is sacrificed (C=0) or exiled (C=1) -- the copy-token rider's delayed action (dly). Mogg Cannon."},
	{"op:SkipNextUntap", "OpSkipNextUntap (Obj)", "Permanent Obj doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step (CR 611.2b): a one-shot perm flag (pfSkipUntap) the untap step consumes, skipping the untap (and a stun counter's removal) even when it is untapped; cleared when it leaves. Gorge: Pump KW$ HIDDEN This card doesn't untap during your next untap step. stamps Object.CantUntapNextStep at grant, rules/turn.go finishUntapStep consumes it. Frost Lynx."},
	{"op:AddMana", "OpAddMana (Obj player, A n, B.N persistent, C colour mask, F restriction)", "Player Obj adds A mana of colour mask C to their pool (the mask's last colour; no choice). `F != 0` (a loyalty ability's or a resolving DB$ Mana's RestrictValid$ Spell.<spec>, CR 106.6 / 605.1a; gorge effMana's ManaAdd restriction; a trigger's or spell's two fixed colours of one restriction float in State.rb, `genPrep.anyMultiR`) floats the units as restricted mana (`State.rb`, kind from `genPrep.restrF`, which prepareGen registers from every AddMana F) that only a spell matching F may spend; A <= 0 adds nothing, and a pool whose batches cannot hold them (every batch taken, or past 255 of a colour) stalls StallRestrSrc, never a spill to the plain pool. Chandra, Chill of Compliance; Abstract Paintmage. `B.N == 1` (PersistentUntilEndOfCombat$ True, Firebending CR 702.189a; gorge effMana) also tallies the units in `State.fbR[p]` (saturating at 255, StallFirebend): the red kept through every step boundary of the combat phase, up to the pool's remaining red (spends are ordinary-first, so the kept share is `min(fbR, pool[R])`), and dropped when the end-of-combat step ends. Fire Sages; Firebending Student; Sun Warriors. `B.N == 2` (PersistentMana$ True; gorge effMana) tallies the units per colour in `State.pm[p]` (saturating at 255, StallPersistMana) beside `pmOn`: the units kept through every step boundary and the cleanup step, up to the pool's remaining units of the colour (ordinary-first spends; with firebending red the combat units go first), zeroed with the pool at the turn change; the tally makes gorge's payment planners refuse the pool like typed mana. The same bit rides ExtManaChoice (C bit 9). Brazen Collector; Savage Ventmaw; Branch of Vitu-Ghazi. `B.N == 3` (an Effect with an UnspentMana static, ValidPlayer$ You ManaType$ Red, from a spell; gorge effEffect registers it until end of turn) adds no units: it marks the controller's red as kept (the whole red slot) at every step boundary until the cleanup step ends (`pmOn` bit 4<<p, zeroed at the turn change). The Last Agni Kai. The op also lowers from two more contexts: a DB$ Mana sub of an activated ability that is no CR 605.1a mana ability -- a loyalty ability, one with a ValidTgts$/TargetType$ anywhere in its chain, or one whose cost or chain moves a library card, which gorge resolves on the stack (cards.IsManaAbilitySA, the head-word test) -- adds to the controller as a spell's does (Quintorius Kand -6, Narset of the Ancient Way +1, Red Death, Shipwrecker); and Defined$ TriggeredPlayer under a your-Phase trigger (the active player, the controller; Hulking Raptor). Sacellum Godspeaker (a no-target, no-library-move AB$ Reveal with a DB$ Mana sub) stays refused: a mana ability by CR 605.1a that gorge puts on the stack."},
	{"op:UntapChoose", "OpUntapChoose (A n, C up-to, F filter)", "Untap n battlefield permanents matching F of any controller (gorge effUntap's UntapType$ + Amount$): the candidates are seat 0's then seat 1's matching permanents in battlefield order, tapped or not, n capped at their number; with C=1 (UntapUpTo$) or more candidates than n the controller picks one at a time (ChGenUntapPick, gorge's \"untap\" KChoose; Done ends an up-to pick), else every candidate untaps; the picks untap afterwards in pick order (a stun counter is removed instead). Snap."},
	{"op:DiscardUnless", "OpDiscardUnless (Obj player, A n, F unless filter)", "Player Obj discards A cards unless they discard one card matching F (gorge effDiscard's TgtChoose UnlessType$): with no matching card in hand it is the ordinary discard; otherwise the player is asked unless / ordinary (gorge discard_unless, ChGenDiscUnless); unless discards the one matching card, or asks which (ChDiscard, Min = Max = 1) among several; ordinary is the ordinary discard. Thirst for Discovery."},
	{"op:LookAck", "OpLookAck (Obj player)", "RevealHand Look$ True: the resolving controller acknowledges the private look at player Obj's hand (gorge poseLookAck, look_ack, one Continue option; ChGenLookAck), posed only when that hand holds a card (effReveal skips an empty pool). No other effect. Deep-Cavern Bat. C=1: the look is at the top A cards of player Obj's library (PeekAndReveal NoReveal$ without RememberPeeked$), posed when the library holds a card: Mishra's Bauble."},
	{"op:ToLibraryPair", "OpToLibraryPair (Obj target)", "ThisDefinedAndTgts$ Self on a shuffled battlefield-to-library move (gorge's object path + objectPathShuffleOwners): the target Obj and then the source go to the top of their owners' libraries, then each distinct owner's library is shuffled once, the target's owner first. Floodpits Drowner."},
	{"op:MayAsk", "OpMayAsk (A skip, C guard)", "A \"you may\" election on the next instruction (gorge effMill's mill_optional, effAttach's attach_optional: a KChoose of yes / no): the resolving controller is asked (ChGenConfirm); a no skips the next `A.N` instructions. `C` is the guard under which gorge asks (kop.MayGuard*): Mill, the next op's amount above 0; Attach, the next op's destination a battlefield permanent other than the source; Move (gorge changeZoneOptionalConfirm), the next move's Obj a live battlefield object (else it is the Origin$ skip: the move is skipped unasked); LibraryTop (gorge moveDefinedLibraryObjects), the resolving controller's library holds a card (an empty one is consumed unasked, unlike a mill's mill_optional); Draw (gorge effDraw canDraw), the next Draw's amount above 0 and the drawing player's library holding a card (failing, the Draw is skipped unasked: gorge draws nothing, no draw from an empty library); Damage (gorge damageHasRecipient), the next DealDamage's amount above 0 and its recipient a player or a live battlefield permanent. Obj, when set, names the deciding player (OptionalDecider$: Opponent, TargetedController; gorge draw_optional / dealdamage_optional); unset, the resolving controller. Stack (kop.MayGuardStackSpell; gorge changeZoneOptionalConfirm over a ChangeZone Origin$ Stack), the next OpCounter's Obj is a spell still on the stack, else the move is skipped unasked; Obj is then the target's controller (Chooser$ TargetedController; Brazen Bluff). With the guard failing nothing is asked and the next op runs (and does nothing). World Shaper, Cori-Steel Cutter, Starwinder, Vex, Requiem Monolith."},
	{"op:AtkPWGuard", "OpAtkPWGuard", "The Attacks trigger's attacker (RefTriggerObj) must be attacking a player; attacking a planeswalker or battle, or gone, the game stalls at its next step (StallDefenderPW). Gorge: DealDamage Defined$ TriggeredDefender.Opponent & Valid Planeswalker.TriggeredDefender reads the defending seat only (the planeswalker arm is an unknown predicate), so the kernel copies it only where it is the card. Raid Bombardment."},
	{"op:Connive", "OpConnive (Obj, A n)", "Permanent Obj connives n (CR 701.50; gorge effConnive): if it is still on the battlefield its controller draws n, then discards n -- the whole hand when it holds no more, else the discard ask (raDiscard, gorge KModes discard Min = Max = n); genState.conn keeps the hand's nonland count before the discard for OpConniveCounters. A.I.M. Scientists."},
	{"op:Bolster", "OpBolster (A n, C counter kind)", "The resolving controller bolsters n (CR 701.39a; gorge putCounterBolster): among the creatures they control, those with the least CURRENT toughness (layer-derived, as gorge's h.Toughness) are the candidates; one is taken unasked, a tie is asked (ChGenBolster, gorge's counter_pick), and it gets n counters of kind C (P1P1 unless CounterType$) as OpPutCounter puts them (the counter replacements, CounterAddedOnce). n <= 0 or no creature: nothing. Abzan Advantage, Dromoka Captain, Sandsteppe War Riders."},
	{"op:ClearCounters", "OpClearCounters (Obj)", "Every counter of every kind is removed from the battlefield permanent Obj: the +1/+1 count and each general slot, one removal per kind present (gorge effRemoveCounter CounterType$ All CounterNum$ All, one CounterChange per kind; excludes the internal Shield/Deathtouched markers, which the kernel never stores as counters). A Class level is not a counter. Nothing when Obj is gone or holds none. A player subject (Final Act's opponents, Suncleanser) is refused by kgen. Vampire Hexmage, Blitz Leech, Enchanted River's Grasp."},
	{"op:RemoveCounterAll", "OpRemoveCounterAll (F, A n, B.N&1 all, C counter kind)", "Each battlefield permanent matching F (seat 0's battlefield in entry order, then seat 1's) loses n counters of kind C, or with B.N&1 (AllCounters$ True) every counter of that kind it has, read first; a permanent with none of the kind is untouched. Gorge effRemoveCounterAll (ValidCards$, CounterType$, CounterNum$, AllCounters$); a line without CounterType$ (Aether Snap's AllCounterTypes$) does nothing in gorge and is refused by kgen. Heartmender, Inhumaniac, Pestilent Haze."},
	{"op:PutCountersFrom", "OpPutCountersFrom (Obj recipient, A multiplier, C source Ref)", "The battlefield permanent Obj gets, for each counter kind the object in Ref C had, that count times A counters of the kind, each put as OpPutCounter puts it (the counter replacements, CounterAddedOnce). The source is read through gorge's LKI ladder (putCounterEachFromSource, CounterType$ EachFromSource): its live counters while it is on the battlefield holding one, else the resolving entry's last-known-information snapshot of it (a dies trigger's RefTriggerObj; a cost-sacrificed RefSelf). A Class level is not a counter. Two or more kinds in a table with a counter-added trigger stall (StallCtrOrder: gorge's per-kind order is the source's insertion order). Star Pupil, Spiteful Squad, Graft Surgeon."},
	{"op:Proliferate", "OpProliferate (A n)", "The resolving controller proliferates n times (CR 701.34a; gorge effProliferate): each time an any-number pick (ChGenProlif, closed by Done; gorge's proliferate KChoose, Min 0) over the permanents with a counter (seat 0's battlefield, then seat 1's) and the players with poison or energy counters; each pick gets one more counter of each kind it has as it is answered (the regeneration shield and the deathtouch mark are not counters), and the completed action fires TrigProliferate even when nothing was eligible. A recipient with two counter kinds in a table with a counter-added trigger, or a seventeenth pick, stalls (StallProlif: gorge's per-kind event order is insertion order). Only a literal Amount$ is lowered. Atraxa, Contagion Clasp, Karn's Bastion."},
	{"trig:BecomeMonstrous", "TrigBecomeMonstrous", "Whenever a permanent matching the filter becomes monstrous (gorge Mode$ BecomeMonstrous, trigmatch monstrousMatches: the AlterAttribute event's object against ValidCard$). Fired by OpMonstrosity after the designation and with the original n. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyMonstrosity). Polukranos, World Eater; Hydra Broodmaster."},
	{"trig:DiscardedAll", "TrigDiscardedAll", "Whenever a player (Whose) discards one or more cards matching ValidCard$ (CR 603.2c; gorge Mode$ DiscardedAll, trigmatch discardedAllMatches, rules discard batch): once per discard action, amt = the cards of the batch (TriggerCount$Amount). A batch is one resolving OpDiscard, open across its player-choice suspensions and an each-player form; a cost, cleanup or cycling discard is a batch of one. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyDiscAll, trig_discardedall.go). FirstTime$, ValidCause$, Random$ refuse. Cryptcaller Chariot, Tinybones, Pocket Nuisance."},
	{"trig:TurnFaceUp", "TrigTurnFaceUp", "Whenever a permanent matching the filter is turned face up (CR 708.6; gorge Mode$ TurnFaceUp, trigmatch turnFaceUpMatches: ValidCard$ against the permanent). Fired by the turn-face-up special action after the permanent's face-up characteristics and subscriptions are restored. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyFaceDown)."},
	{"trig:Transformed", "TrigTransformed", "Whenever a permanent matching the filter transforms (CR 701.27a / 712.14a; gorge Mode$ Transformed, trigmatch transformedMatches: ValidCard$ against the object on the battlefield at match time). Fired after a battlefield transform (SetState Transform, an Incubator token, a modal flip), never on an entering-transformed flip. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyTransformed)."},
	{"trig:TokenCreated", "TrigTokenCreated (always with Tf2Batch)", "Whenever a token matching the filter is created (gorge Mode$ TokenCreatedOnce, ValidToken$ against the token, ValidPlayer$ (Whose) against its creator): once per token batch, a whole resolution; outside a resolution each token. Fired as an OpCreateToken(Ex) or amass token enters (a copy token never: gorge's CopyToken is no TokenCreate). No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyTokCr). OnlyFirst$ (Akim) refuses. Staff of the Storyteller."},
	{"trig:Scry", "TrigScry", "Whenever a player (Whose) scries (CR 701.22; gorge trigmatch scryMatches, events.Scry): once per completed scry instruction, after the arrangement is answered, and also for a scry 0 or an empty library (gorge's stand-in record). No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyScryTrig, trig_scrysurveil.go). ValidCard$, FirstTime$, ToBottom$ refuse. Matoya, Archon Elder; Proft, Consulting Detective."},
	{"trig:Surveil", "TrigSurveil", "Whenever a player (Whose) surveils (CR 701.25; gorge trigmatch surveilMatches, events.Surveil): once per surveil instruction, as it starts and before the look (so also for a surveil 0 or an empty library). No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyScryTrig, trig_scrysurveil.go). ValidCard$, FirstTime$, ToBottom$ refuse. Matoya, Archon Elder; Prudent Fateseer."},
	{"trig:Explores", "TrigExplores (Filter = the explorer, Filter2 = the revealed card)", "Whenever a creature matching ValidCard$ explores (CR 701.44a; gorge trigmatch exploresMatches on the completed events.Explore record): once per explore, after the outcome (a land in hand; a nonland's counter, then its graveyard or top answer). ValidExplored$ (Filter2) is a type-only predicate (Land, Card.nonLand), matched against the revealed card wherever it is. An empty library or a departed explorer fires nothing. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyExplEvTrig, trig_exploreevidence.go). ValidPlayer$ and other keys refuse. Merfolk Cave-Diver, Nicanzil, Current Conductor."},
	{"trig:LandPlayed", "TrigLandPlayed (Filter = the land, N = origin zone mask)", "Whenever a land matching ValidCard$ is played (CR 305.1; gorge trigmatch landPlayedMatches, rules/cast_commit.go: the land's move to the battlefield while it is a land play, a Play effect's (hideaway) too). Origin$ whitelists the zone played from as a 1<<Zone mask in Trigger.N (Hand, Graveyard, Exile, Library; Ante and Command drop out as in gorge; 0 = any). The same event as the land's ETB: the entry walk queues ETB and LandPlayed lines interleaved, per object in walk order and per line in ability order. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyLandPlayed, enterLandPlayed in trig_modes.go). ValidSA$ and other keys refuse. Shadow of the Goblin, The Endstone."},
	{"trig:SearchedLibrary", "TrigSearchedLibrary", "Whenever a player (Whose) searches their own library (gorge trigmatch cards.go, SearchOwnLibrary$ True required): one marker per hidden library search node, also when nothing is found, after the moves and before the shuffle. No slot subscription (genPrep.anyKwAct, fireKwAct in trig_modes.go). ValidCard$ and other keys refuse. Wan Shi Tong, Librarian."},
	{"trig:Forage", "TrigForage", "Whenever a player (Whose) forages (CR 701.61a; gorge trigmatch keyword_action.go, ForageAction): once per paid forage, after its moves: a cast or activation cost after every sacrifice (forageCastDone), a trigger's own cost when the either-or settles (act_forage.go). No slot subscription (genPrep.anyKwAct, fireKwAct). Corpseberry Cultivator."},
	{"trig:Discover", "TrigDiscover (amt = the discover value)", "Whenever a player (Whose) discovers (CR 701.57; gorge trigmatch cards.go, effects/discover.go emitDiscover): once per discover at completion, with the discover value as the trigger amount (TriggerCount$Amount). Fired by the OpDiscover C=1 tail (which carries the head's player and value); cascade fires none. No slot subscription (genPrep.anyKwAct, fireKwAct). ActivationLimit$ 1 lowers. Curator of Sun's Creation."},
	{"trig:ManifestDread", "TrigManifestDread (the milled card as the trigger object)", "Whenever a player (Whose) manifests dread (CR 701.62a; gorge Mode$ ManifestDread, trigmatch manifestDreadMatches on the completed events.ManifestDreadAction marker): once per manifest-dread window, after its moves, with the card the window put into its owner's graveyard as the trigger object (TriggeredCards; the one-card window's marker has an empty ID list, so none). No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyKwAct, fireKwActObj in trig_modes.go). ValidCard$ and other keys refuse. Paranormal Analyst."},
	{"trig:CollectEvidence", "TrigCollectEvidence", "Whenever a player (Whose) collects evidence (CR 701.59a; gorge trigmatch collectEvidenceMatches, events.CollectEvidenceAction): once per cost payment that exiled at least one card (a cast or activation cost, a trigger's own cost); a ward payment records no action in gorge and fires nothing. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyExplEvTrig, trig_exploreevidence.go). ValidCard$ and other keys refuse. Evidence Examiner, Surveillance Monitor."},
	{"trig:FacesDilemma", "TrigFacesDilemma", "Whenever a player (Whose) chooses one or more modes for a spell or ability (gorge trigmatch facesDilemmaMatches)."},
	{"trig:Proliferate", "TrigProliferate", "Whenever a player (Whose) proliferates (gorge trigmatch proliferateMatches, events.Proliferate): once per completed proliferate action. No slot subscription: the battlefield is scanned (genPrep.anyProlif). Ezuri, Stalker of Spheres; Scheming Aspirant."},
	{"op:ConniveCounters", "OpConniveCounters (Obj)", "Follows OpConnive: one +1/+1 counter on Obj (one counter event, replaceable; CounterAddedOnce) per nonland card its controller's hand lost to the connive's discard (gorge applyConniveDiscard). Nothing when the conniver had left."},
	{"op:Seek", "OpSeek (Obj player, A count, C flags, F filter)", "Player Obj (the controller) seeks `A` cards matching F: the eligible cards of their library, from the top, are sampled without replacement by one rng IntN(eligible) draw each, then moved to their hand in that order. Not a draw, not a search: no reveal, no shuffle. `C&1` (RememberFound$): the found cards replace the remembered set. Gorge: api:Seek (effects/zone.go effSeek); Types$, ImprintFound$, DefinedCards$ and other Defined$ are refused by kgen."},
	{"op:AttachObj", "OpAttachObj (Obj destination, B remember, C object Ref)", "The battlefield permanent in Ref C (a target slot, the trigger's object, the remembered object) becomes attached to the battlefield permanent Obj; nothing when either is not on the battlefield or they are the same permanent. A Ref C target slot holding several objects attaches each still-legal one in pick order (gorge attachObjectParentTarget: Object$ ParentTarget names the parent link's whole set; Thorin, Mountain-king). B Const 1 (RememberAttached$ True, Object$ ParentTarget only) remembers each object attached. Legality is the attachment state-based actions' (CR 704.5m/n), as gorge's Attachable is always true. No decision. Gorge: api:Attach with Object$ Targeted / ParentTarget / TriggeredCard(LKICopy) (effects/attach.go effAttach) or Object$ Remembered | Defined$ Self (attachObjectRemembered attaches EVERY remembered object, the kernel reads the one: kgen lowers it only behind a single one-object remembered writer, a constant-1 token or a one-card move, else refuses `multi-object remembered set`); Optional$, Choices$, Move$, RememberAttached$ (outside ParentTarget) and plural Object$ selectors (outside ParentTarget) are refused by kgen. Brass Squire, Sigarda's Aid; U.S.Agent, John Walker and Tony Stark (Remembered)."},
	{"op:Shuffle", "OpShuffle (Obj player)", "Player Obj shuffles their library (one rng permutation, as the kernel's searches shuffle). No decision. Gorge: api:Shuffle (effects/shuffle.go effShuffle) of the controller or one Defined$ / target player; object owners and several players are refused by kgen. Boggart Forager, Soldier of Fortune."},
	{"op:SetLife", "OpSetLife (Obj players, A amount)", "Each player in Obj (RefEachPlayer: controller first, gorge AliveFrom) has their life total become `A` (read once, before any change): a gain or a loss of the difference, firing LifeGained / LifeLost (CR 119.5). No decision. Gorge: api:SetLife (effects/life.go effSetLife); Redistribute$ is refused by kgen. Blessed Wind."},
	{"op:SkipUntap", "OpSkipUntap (Obj permanent, C form)", "A \"doesn't untap during your next untap step\" effect the controller makes: C=0 the permanent Obj (the mark leaves with it), C=1 the lands the controller controls at that step. During the controller's next untap step those permanents stay tapped (a stun counter is still removed first); the effect ends with that step. Any number of them on one permanent is one mark: gorge asks no order. No decision. Gorge: Effect Duration$ UntilTheEndOfYourNextUntap with an Event$ Untap | Layer$ CantHappen | ValidStepTurnToController$ Player.Activator replacement (rules/turn.go expireUntapStepEffects). Arbalest Elite, Bontu's Last Reckoning. C=2 and C=3 are a source-bound lock on the permanent Obj (a record of Obj, this ability's source and its controller: four at once, a fifth stalls StallUntapLock): live while that source is on the battlefield under that player, ended for good when the source changes controller or Obj leaves the battlefield (a source that leaves and returns under the same player revives it, as gorge's continuousLive reads only the source's zone and controller). C=2 holds only in Obj's controller's untap step, C=3 against every untap. Gorge: Effect Duration$ AsLongAsControl, RememberObjects$ Targeted, ForgetOnMoved$ Battlefield, an Event$ Untap | ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered | Layer$ CantHappen replacement with (C=2) or without (C=3) ValidStepTurnToController$ You. Ty Lee, Chi Blocker; Spider-Woman, Secret Agent. C=4 is the player Obj's creatures and lands (whoever cast it): the ones that player controls at their next untap step stay tapped through it, and the effect ends there. Gorge: an Effect with a StaticAbilities$ body Affected$ Creature.RememberedPlayerCtrl,Land.RememberedPlayerCtrl | AddHiddenKeyword$ This card doesn't untap during your next untap step. (an UntapDenial restriction rules/layers_restrict.go untapDenied reads) and a Phase$ Untap trigger of the remembered player exiling the Effect. Exhaustion."},
	{"op:Discover", "OpDiscover (Obj player, A value, C part)", "Discover A (CR 701.57a). C=0: the player exiles their library's cards from the top until a nonland card with mana value A or less (printed, X = 0); the others go to the bottom in a random order drawn from the engine rng (gorge's Fisher-Yates, CR 701.57a); the found card becomes the remembered set. kgen follows it with OpCastFree over it (the optional free cast, ChGenCastFree) and C=1: the remembered card still in exile goes to its owner's hand. No decision of its own. Gorge: api:Discover (effects/discover.go effDiscover, effDiscoverBottom); Defined$ is refused by kgen. Daring Discovery."},
	{"op:MoveCounter", "OpMoveCounter (Obj destination, C origin Ref, A n, B.N kind)", "Up to `A` (A < 0: all) counters of kind B.N leave the battlefield permanent in Ref C and the battlefield permanent Obj gets that many, through the counter replacements, firing its counter-added triggers; nothing when either is gone or they are the same. No decision. Gorge: api:MoveCounter (effects/counters.go effMoveCounter) with Source$ Self / ParentTarget and one destination; Any kinds, CounterNum$ Any and the sweeps are refused by kgen. Weapon Rack."},
	{"op:Rearrange", "OpRearrange (Obj player, A n, C flags)", "The controller looks at the top `A` cards of player Obj's library (at most what it holds; more than 8 stalls) and puts them back in any order: ChArrange picks over the looked-at cards, no Done, the first pick on top (gorge's KArrange ordering every card). C&1 (MayShuffle$): then the controller is asked yes/no (ChGenConfirm) whether that library is shuffled. Gorge: api:RearrangeTopOfLibrary (effects/cardflow.go effRearrangeTopOfLibrary, rearrangeMayShuffleTape); RearrangePlayer$ and a non-constant count are refused by kgen. Ponder, Portent."},
	{"op:Fog", "OpFog", "All combat damage that would be dealt this turn is prevented: the turn's combat damage passes deal nothing and pose no division ask (genState.fog, cleared as a turn begins). No decision. Gorge: api:Fog (effects/fog.go effFog, rules damageStep's fogActive). Fog, Holy Day."},
	{"op:Poison", "OpPoison (Obj players, A n)", "Each player in Obj gets `A` poison counters (CR 122.1f); a table with OpPoison checks the ten-poison state-based action (CR 704.5c) and, beside proliferate, stalls as an infect table does (StallInfect: gorge proliferates players' poison). No decision. Gorge: api:Poison (effects/counters.go effPoison). Crypt Cobra, Swamp Mosquito."},
	{"op:Blight", "OpBlight (Obj player, A n)", "Player Obj blights `A` (CR 701.68): that player chooses a creature they control and puts `A` -1/-1 counters on it (counter replacements apply, firing the creature's counter-added triggers). No creature: nothing. Exactly one candidate: the counters are placed unasked; more: ChGenBlightPick over the creatures (gorge's `blight` KChoose). Gorge: api:Blight (effects/blight.go effBlight) with Defined$ You / Opponent; other player refs and a variable Num$ are refused by kgen. Chaos Spewer, High Perfect Morcant."},
	{"op:Explore", "OpExplore (Obj explorer)", "Permanent Obj explores (CR 701.44a): its controller reveals their library's top card; a land goes to their hand; otherwise Obj gets a +1/+1 counter (counter replacements apply) and the controller chooses the card into the graveyard or back on top. Nothing when Obj left the battlefield or the library is empty. Decision: ChGenExplore over the revealed card, mode 0 graveyard (gorge's option 0) / 1 top. Gorge: api:Explore (effects/explore.go effExplore; Num$ N is N OpExplore). Merfolk Branchwalker."},
	{"op:TapOrUntap", "OpTapOrUntap (Obj permanent)", "While the permanent Obj is on the battlefield, its ability's controller chooses: tap it (Taps triggers fire) or untap it (a stun counter is removed instead, CR 122.1d); nothing to do when it is already in the chosen state. Decision: ChGenTapOrUntap over the permanent, mode 1 tap / 0 untap, the state-changing choice listed first (gorge's taporuntap KChoose \"tap\" / \"untap\"). Gorge: api:TapOrUntap (effects/taporuntap.go effTapOrUntap); Tapper$ and several-object slots are refused by kgen. Twiddle, Cloud of Faeries' kin."},
	{"op:TapAll", "OpTapAll (Obj player or none, F filter)", "Each UNTAPPED battlefield permanent matching F (only target player Obj's when Obj is set) becomes tapped, seat 0's battlefield in entry order then seat 1's; each tap fires that permanent's Taps triggers as it happens. No decision. Gorge: api:TapAll (effects/combatfx.go effTapAll; ValidCards$ default Permanent; a player ValidTgts$ is allPlayersFor's scope); Defined$, RememberTapped$ and TapperController$ are refused by kgen."},
	{"op:RepeatWhile", "OpRepeatWhile (A max, B.N body, C CondID)", "Run the next `B.N` instructions (the body) at most `A` times (evaluated once, before the first pass; 0 skips the body); after each pass evaluate `Table.Conds[C]` and stop when it is FALSE. Shares OpRepeat's two loop levels. No decision of its own. Gorge: api:Repeat with RepeatCheckSVar$/RepeatSVarCompare$ (effects/resolve.go effRepeat; the gate-governed loop, MaxRepeat$ the cap). Sphinx's Tutelage: mill two while two milled nonland cards share a colour, at most the library size times; the body mills remembering (OpMill C = MvRemember)."},
	{"op:ChooseTargets", "OpChooseTargets (C slot)", "The controller chooses target slot C now, mid-resolution (the slot carries TgfAtResolution and is skipped as the spell is cast): one object, or none for an up-to slot. Gorge asks a chain link's targets this way when the cast census cannot judge the link (rules/cast_targets.go collectSubTargetPreAsks). Fiery Annihilation: up to one target Equipment attached to the damaged creature."},
	{"op:RepeatEach", "OpRepeatEach (Obj target slot or RefNone, F filter, B.N body)", "Run the next `B.N` instructions once per card, binding RefEach (the object ref) to it. The cards are listed once before the first pass, as gorge's repeatedCards lists them: with Obj RefNone every battlefield permanent F admits (the resolving controller's first, then the other seats', each in battlefield order; RepeatCards$ <filter> with Zone$ Battlefield); with Obj a target slot that slot's legal objects in pick order (DefinedCards$ Targeted). The loop runs in one call inside one zone batch and entry hold (ChangeZoneTable$ True), so its body cannot ask: kgen lowers only a lone Role Token whose AttachedTo$ Remembered is the repeated card (a body that does ask stalls StallRoleMulti). No State of its own. Asinine Antics, Become Brutes, Twisted Sewer-Witch."},
	{"op:RepeatEachPlayer", "OpRepeatEachPlayer (Obj players, A skip)", "Run the next `A.N` instructions once per player in Obj (RefEachOpponent / RefEachPlayer), `C&1`: the resolving controller first (gorge AliveFrom), otherwise APNAP, binding RefEach to that player."},
	{"op:UnlessPaid", "OpUnlessPaid (Obj payer, A amount, B.N pips, C PayKind|skip<<4, F filter)", "Decision for the payer: pay the cost or not. If PAID, skip the next `C>>4` instructions (the effect is prevented); if not paid (or unpayable) run them. PayKind (`C&0xF`): PayMana = A generic + B.N pips (3 bits per colour, WUBRG from bit 0); PayDiscard = discard A cards (the payer chooses which); PaySac = sacrifice A permanents the payer controls matching F (payer chooses); PayLife = pay A life (only if life >= A); PaySacSelf = sacrifice the resolving ability's source (Sac<1/CARDNAME>), payable while the payer controls it, settled unasked. PayManaX (15) = a trigger's own pay-{X} cost: X is announced first (ChTrigX, 0..min(A the XMax$ cap, what the payer can produce, 64)), then the ordinary election; the paid X is the body's Count$xPaid (Shanna, Purifying Blade). PayTapX with B.N kop.PayBSubTapXVar = a trigger's own tapXType<X/Spec>: an any-number pick of untapped permanents matching F, closed by Done (none = the decline), each tapped as picked, the count tapped the body's Count$xPaid (Myr Battlesphere). Gorge: `UnlessCost$`/`UnlessPayer$` (Painful Quandary, Perforating Artist)."},
	{"op:IfPaid", "OpIfPaid (same operands as OpUnlessPaid)", "Decision for the payer: pay or not. If NOT paid skip the next `C>>4` instructions; if paid run them. Source: an AB$ with Cost$ inside a trigger body (an optional cost paid on resolution, 'you may pay {R}. If you do...'): Flamewake Phoenix (R), Frenzied Goblin (R), High-Society Hunter and Vampire Gourmand (sacrifice another creature). The skip covers the rest of the trigger's program. Frenzied Goblin's trigger is also TfOptional: gorge asks the optional-trigger question first, then the payment."},
	{"op:UnlessSwitched", "OpUnlessSwitched (same operands as OpUnlessPaid)", "Decision for the payer: pay or not. If NOT paid skip the next `C>>4` instructions; if paid run them. This is `UnlessSwitched$` (Incinerating Blast: 'you may discard a card; if you do, draw'): gorge poses it as the unless modes ask (ChGenPayMode), including at the start of a trigger, never as a trigger's own cost."},
	// --- damage ---
	{"op:DealDamageEx", "OpDealDamageEx (Obj, A amount, C DamageFlags)", "OpDealDamage plus flags. DmgTrackExcess: record the damage beyond what was lethal to the creature (toughness minus damage already marked, min 0 — CR 120.4a/702.2c excess), readable as ExExcessDamage (Goblin Negotiation's tokens). DmgExileIfDiesThisTurn: if the creature would die this turn, exile it instead (a turn-scoped replacement on that object; Fiery Annihilation). DmgMapped: part of a damage map — collect, and deal all mapped damage as ONE simultaneous event at OpResolveDamageMap (Drakuseth: 4 to one target and 3 to each of up to two others; CR 120.3 simultaneous damage, one DamageDone batch)."},
	{"op:ResolveDamageMap", "OpResolveDamageMap", "Deal all DmgMapped damage collected since the program start as one simultaneous damage event (triggers see one batch). Gorge: DealDamage DamageMap$ True + DamageResolve. A pure plus-N competition poses gorge's no-op CR 616.1 order ask before the map deals (replPlusSrcPass), the collected map surviving the pause for the answer's re-execution; two or more competing events, or a noncommuting candidate, still stall (StallReplPlus)."},
	{"op:DealDamageDivided", "OpDealDamageDivided (Obj RefTargetN, A total)", "Deal `A` damage divided among the objects chosen for target slot N as assigned at targeting (CR 601.2d: the division is chosen while casting/activating, each chosen target at least 1). The slot has Min..Max objects and `Divide` = the total. Decision sequence: choose the targets, then the division (one assignment per target). Chandra, Flameshaper -4 (8 damage, up to 8 creatures/planeswalkers). C = DmgDivideEvenly: no division is chosen, and at resolution each legal target of the slot takes A over their count, rounded down, in one damage batch (DivideEvenly$ RoundedDown; gorge effects divideEvenlyDown). Fireball."},
	// --- zones ---
	{"op:ExileEx", "OpExileEx (Obj, A counters, B.N counter kind, C MoveFlags)", "Exile Obj (from whatever zone it is in). MvRemember: the exiled objects become the remembered set (RefRemembered). A>0: the card is exiled with A counters of kind B.N (Tinybones' stash counter). MvForgetChanged: the exiled object leaves the remembered set again (ForgetChanged$ True)."},
	{"op:ReturnEx", "OpReturnEx (Obj, A counters, B.N kind, C zone|MoveFlags<<3)", "Move Obj from graveyard/exile to zone `C&7`, under its owner's control unless MvUnderYourControl (then the resolving controller's). MvTapped: enters tapped. A>0: enters with A counters of kind B.N (an as-enters modification, not an event after entering — Infernal Vessel, Valkyrie's Call, Nine-Lives Familiar). A constant A may add a second kind: A = count | (second kind + 1)<<8 (kop.RetCounterPairShift), and the permanent enters with count counters of B.N then of the second kind (WithCountersType$ with two kinds — Perennation). A following OpOverride with Obj = the same ref applies to the object it became. MvForgetChanged (ForgetChanged$ True, gorge eventForgetChanged): the returned object leaves the resolution's remembered set, order kept (after MvRemember, which would re-add it). B.N RetFromLibrary (Origin$ Library, a Defined$ library fetch): only a library card moves; B.N RetShuffleOwed (the script owes a shuffle: a preceding Shuffle$ False search deferred it, or Shuffle$ True) shuffles its owner's library after the move (gorge moveDefinedLibraryObjects: a Defined$ fetch is not a search); Guidelight Pathmaker, Archdruid's Charm. B.N RetUnderOpponent (GainControl$ ChosenPlayer after a one-opponent ChoosePlayer, CR 110.2a; never with A counters): the object enters under the resolving controller's opponent; Zuko, Conflicted. B.N RetAttachTo (AttachedTo$; never with A counters): B bits 8..10 name the bearer Ref (Self, or the target slot of ParentTarget). The returned Aura enters attached to it when it is among the Aura's legal objects to enchant, else stays in its zone (CR 303.4g); an Equipment enters, then attaches when the bearer is a creature on the battlefield; Eagle's Rescue, Magnetic Snuffler."},
	{"c:LibTopShuffle", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibTopShuffle", "The object goes on top of its owner's library, then that library is shuffled, even when the object did not move while it exists (gorge effChangeZone's object path with Shuffle$ True, objectPathShuffleOwners; CR 701.24c). Alabaster Dragon."},
	{"c:LibThird", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibThird", "The object goes into its owner's library third from the top (LibraryPosition$ 2): min(2, the other cards left) cards sit above it (gorge libraryOrderPlacementAt). Braided Quipu."},
	{"c:LibTopShuffleGrave", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibTopShuffleGrave", "LibTopShuffle for a trigger object's Origin$ Graveyard move: the card moves and the library is shuffled only if the card is still in the graveyard; exiled in response, neither happens (gorge's Origin$ precondition on the object path). Lembas."},
	{"c:LibBottomShuffle", "OpToLibrary C = kop.LibBottomShuffle", "LibTopShuffle with LibraryPosition$ -1: the object goes on the bottom of its owner's library, then that library is shuffled (gorge effChangeZone's object path). Unlucky Cabbage Merchant."},
	{"op:ToLibraryChoice", "OpToLibraryChoice (Obj)", "Decision for Obj's OWNER: top (C = kop.LibChoiceSecond: second from the top, min(1, the other cards) above it) or bottom of their library; then move it there. Uncharted Voyage (AlternativeDecider$ TargetedOwner); Temporal Cleansing (LibraryPosition$ 1)."},
	{"op:SearchEx", "OpSearchEx (Obj player, A count, C zone|SearchFlags<<3, F)", "Player searches their library for up to A cards matching F (zone Library) and puts them in zone `C&7` (Hand, Battlefield, or Library for SrThenTop), then shuffles. SrTapped: they enter tapped. SrThenTop: shuffle, then put the found card on top (Campus Guide). SrMandatory: must find one if able (gorge Mandatory$: Grim Tutor, Rune-Scarred Demon). SrRemember: the found cards join the remembered set (RememberChanged$, gorge zone_search eventRemember: Fabled Passage's untap); kgen refuses it with a library destination or SrThenTop. The shuffle is mandatory, even when nothing was found (CR 701.23, 701.24c/d; gorge): ShuffleNonMandatory$ lowers to nothing and SrShuffleOptional is retired. SrForgetChanged (B bit 1; ForgetChanged$ True): each found card that moved leaves the remembered set again (Troop of Ponies' pick). SrNoShuffle (B; Shuffle$ False): no shuffle after the moves, a library destination putting the found cards on top with the first answered on top, remembered with SrRemember (Cultivate, Flourishing Bloom-Kin). SrAltOrigin (B bit 4; OriginAlternative$): B bits 5..7 name the alternative zone (Graveyard or Hand), or SrAltGraveHand for the Graveyard,Hand pair; the searcher first elects the zones to search (ChGenKczZone: the library and the alternatives, closed by Done), the pool is the elected zones' matching cards library first, and the library is shuffled only when it was elected (Delivery Moogle, Last Light of Durin's Day; Agency Outfitter's pair with SrDifferentNames). SrAltAll (B bit 3, with SrAltOrigin and the Graveyard zone; Origin$ Library,Graveyard): the election is settled as both zones, nobody is asked, and the library is shuffled (Journey for the Elixir, Verdant Crescendo). SrSideboard (B bit 10; ChangeZone Origin$ Sideboard / Library,Sideboard, CR 400.11): the pool also holds the searcher's sideboard cards (the cards outside the game they own, object order) after the library; SrNoLibrary (B bit 11) leaves the library out (no look, no shuffle, ChGenSearch); DifferentNames$ counts the names over the whole pool. SrExactly (B bit 2; Exactly$ True): exactly A cards are found or none (Done is offered only before the first pick). SrChooserOpp (B bit 0; Chooser$ Opponent): the opponent answers the picks. A zone-none destination finds and, with SrRemember, remembers the cards where they lie (Turtles Forever's first node, North Wind Avatar). Decision: choose the cards (one pick per card, may stop early unless mandatory); the found card is revealed where the card says so (no rules effect)."},
	{"op:ChooseCard", "OpChooseCard (Obj player, F, C code)", "Player Obj chooses a card matching F (zone in the filter), stored as RefChosen; a mandatory ask is posed with one candidate too and none with no candidate. C 1: up to one (a Done beside the cards); C 2: RememberChosen$; C 3: the Peek's top-A library window. C 4 / 5 (chooseAttachPick / chooseAttachPickOpt): the object-side Attach pick, always followed by an AttachObj with C = RefChosen: the candidates are the F permanents other than that AttachObj's destination (none when the destination is gone); none: no ask, nothing chosen; C 4 (mandatory) with one candidate: taken unasked; otherwise the ask, with a Done for C 5 (Optional$ is the pick's Min 0). Gorge: effAttach with Choices$ and no Object$ (the pool of battlefieldValidTargets, destCandidatesFor, one KChoose). Zack Fair, Vow to Erebor, Winter Soldier, Icy Assassin. C 6 (choosePutCounterPick): PutCounter's Choices$ recipient pick, always followed by an OpPutCounter on RefChosen: a CounterNum$ amount <= 0 or no F permanent: no ask, nothing chosen; one candidate: taken unasked; otherwise one mandatory ask (no Done) over the F permanents, seat 0's battlefield then seat 1's. Gorge: putCounterChooseTitled (Min 1, Max 1, ResumeKind counter_pick). Aerith Rescue Mission, Wick, the Whorled Mind. C 8 (chooseCopyPick): CopyPermanent's Choices$ pick, always followed by an ExtCopyPicked on RefChosen: one mandatory ask (no Done) over the F permanents, posed with one candidate too, none with no candidate; the ask is ChGenCopyPick, whose options gorge names \"permanent\" (copypermanent_choice). Calamity, Galloping Inferno."},
	{"op:PutCounter", "OpPutCounter (Obj permanent, A n, C counter kind, B remember mode)", "The battlefield permanent Obj gets `A` counters of kind C through the counter replacements, then CounterAddedOnce. B 1 (RememberAmount$): the landed count joins the resolution's remembered count. B 2 (RememberPut$): the recipient joins the remembered set when the CounterNum$ value is > 0, read before replacements (gorge does not ask that a counter landed). Gorge: effPutCounter (effects/counters_put.go, rememberPlaced). Systems Override."},
	{"op:ChooseMove", "OpChooseMove (Obj player, A count, C zone|SearchFlags<<3, F)", "Player chooses A cards matching F from their own graveyard or hand (F.Zone; F.Ctrl = owner), or permanents from either battlefield (a zoneless F: gorge effHiddenPick's game-wide public pool, seat 0 first, or with SrOwnZone player Obj's battlefield only; they leave for C&7), and moves them to zone `C&7`. Not targeted. Inspiration from Beyond (mandatory instant or sorcery to hand). From a hand (gorge effChangeZoneHand, ChGenHandMove): SrConfirm poses gorge's Optional$ yes/no confirmation first (ChGenConfirm; no skips the move); a SrMandatory move with no more eligible cards than A takes them all unasked; SrTapped enters them tapped, SrRemember remembers them (RememberChanged$); Obj may be a target player whose hand it is (effChangeZoneHandOwners), SrChooserYou then asks the controller (Chooser$ You). SrReveal with zone none is a reveal pick (gorge effReveal: ChGenReveal, option kind reveal; nothing moves, SrRemember remembers the pick; SrConfirm then asks only when a card qualifies). Arboreal Grazer, Aether Vial, Castigate, Armored Kincaller."},
	{"op:ChangeZoneAllEx", "OpChangeZoneAllEx (Obj player or none, C zone|MoveFlags<<3, F)", "Move every card matching F (F.Zone = origin) to zone `C&7`. Obj (a target player) restricts to that player's cards (Angel of Finality: exile target player's graveyard). MvUnderYourControl: onto the battlefield under the controller's control (Rise of the Dark Realms, from all graveyards). MvEntryRiders (onto the battlefield; A = constant counter count | counter kind<<8, B = override index+1, 0 = none): each entrant, as it enters and before any of the sweep's enters checks fire, gets A counters of that kind (WithCountersType$, CR 122.6) and a permanent override record (StaticEffect$ Affected$ Card.IsRemembered, CR 603.6b; gorge applyStaticEffect per moved card). Ghost Vacuum. MvForgetOther (non-battlefield, non-library origin, ForgetOtherRemembered$): the matched set is copied out in scan order, the remembered set is cleared (both halves), then the copy moves, MvRemember re-remembering each (Random Encounter). B bit kop.CzUntilLeaves (a battlefield to exile sweep, no entry riders; Duration$ UntilHostLeavesPlay, carried in B because every MoveFlags bit is taken): nothing moves once the source has left the battlefield, and each exiled non-token permanent is linked to the source (genState.links, full table: StallLinks) so it returns, in link order, when the source leaves (Pinnacle Starcage). With MvGraveExile and B = kop.CzLibrarySideboard the origin is every library then every sideboard (Library,Sideboard, Turtles Forever's put-back): the matching cards go on top of their owner's library in sweep order (library cards first). With MvGraveExile and B = kop.CzHandGrave the origin is every seat's hand, then every seat's graveyard (Hand,Graveyard: the cards sit in the library in that move order); with B&kop.CzShuffleEach the sweep ends with both libraries shuffled, the owner of the first card moved first, then the other seat (UseAllOriginZones$ with Shuffle$ True: Echo of Eons, Timetwister)."},
	{"op:DigEx", "OpDigEx (Obj player(s), A look, B take, C zone|DigFlags<<3, F)", "Player looks at the top A cards; chooses B of them matching F (B=-1: all of them, no choice; -2: any number) for zone `C&7`; the rest go to zone `(C>>3)&7` (Library = bottom unless DigRestTop). DigOptional: may take none. DigRandomOrder: the rest go to the bottom in a random order (uses the RNG; gorge's draw order). DigTakeToTop: the taken card goes on top (Gutless Plunderer, rest to graveyard). DigRemember: moved cards become RefRemembered. DigReveal/DigRevealToCtrl: reveal (no rules effect). Obj = RefEachPlayer runs for each player, the resolving controller first (gorge AliveFrom; Etali). Decision: the chosen subset (one pick per card)."},
	{"op:DigUntil", "OpDigUntil (Obj player(s), A count, C zone|DigUntilFlags<<3, F)", "Reveal cards from the top until A cards matching F are revealed (or the library runs out). Found cards go to zone `C&7`, the other revealed cards to `(C>>3)&7`; DuRestBottom: library bottom; DuRandomOrder: random order; DuFoundWithRevealed: no separate found destination — the found card goes with the rest (gorge effects/diguntil.go: absent FoundDestination$); DuFoundAttacking: a found card put onto the battlefield enters attacking (Attacking$ True). Consuming Aberration (each opponent, until a land, all to graveyard), Spinner of Souls (until a creature: to hand, rest bottom random; the trigger is optional)."},
	{"op:Peek", "OpPeek (Obj player, A)", "Player looks at the top A cards of their library (no reveal, a look_ack first); they become the remembered set. Curator of Destinies. C=PeekPublic: a public reveal with no ask (gorge effReveal), and with PeekRemember the cards join the remembered set (RememberRevealed$). Aven Windreader. C=PeekMayReveal: the top card of player Obj's library, when it matches F, is offered to that player (gorge effReveal reveal_optional yes/no, ChGenPeekReveal); a yes reveals it and appends it to the remembered set, a no or a non-matching or absent top card remembers nothing and asks nothing. Gathering Stone."},
	{"op:TwoPiles", "OpTwoPiles (Obj separator, C zone)", "Decisions: the separator (the controller) splits the remembered cards into a face-down pile and a face-up pile (one assignment per card); the opponent chooses one pile; the chosen pile goes to zone C (Hand), the other to the graveyard. Curator of Destinies (gorge api:TwoPiles, Separator You, Chooser Opponent, FaceDown One)."},
	{"op:ChooseEachType", "OpChooseEachType (Obj players)", "Each player in Obj chooses, for each of artifact, battle, creature, enchantment, land, planeswalker, one permanent they control of that type if any (one object may satisfy several types); the chosen objects form RefChosen / F2ChosenCard. Liliana, Dreadhorde General -9 (followed by OpSacrificeAll of the opponents' nonchosen permanents)."},
	{"op:SacrificeAll", "OpSacrificeAll (F)", "Every permanent matching F is sacrificed by its controller, simultaneously. No decision."},
	{"op:CastFree", "OpCastFree (Obj cards, C zone|flags<<3, F)", "The controller may cast any number of the cards in Obj without paying their mana costs, during the resolution, in an order they choose; lands among them can't be played. Obj: RefRemembered (the remembered set), a target slot, or RefNone with F selecting cards in zone `C&7` (Exile / Hand / Graveyard, seat 0 then seat 1 in zone order). Flags: bit 3 AmountOne (close the ask after one pick), bit 4 ForgetPlayed (drop the begun card from the remembered set), bit 5 ReplaceGraveyard (exile the spell when it leaves the stack instead of the graveyard), bit 6 CopyCard (Play CopyCard$ True, CR 707.12: Obj is RefRemembered over cards in Exile; the original stays in exile and a copy is cast, an ofCopy object owned by the caster that gorge casts from its library holding zone (cast-from Library); a permanent card's copy resolves into a token (CR 707.10f), the copy ceases to exist leaving the stack (CR 704.5d); a multi-face card stalls StallCopyCast),, bit 7 Repeat (AllowRepeats$ True with Amount$ A, on a CopyCard cast: A is the copy count, evaluated at the pose; the remembered card stands A times in the offer and each pick queues one copy, so the ask can stop at any count; A below one offers nothing, more than eight copies stalls StallFree; gorge effects/play.go). Bit 8 Paid (a Play with no WithoutManaCost$, on a CopyCard cast of Obj RefSelf, the source card in exile: an exile-granted ability's 'create a copy of this card, you may cast the copy'): the copy pays its mana cost, through gorge's manual mana window with no payment plan (bflLowered); a copy whose mana cost the window cannot meet reverses there (CR 733.1), keeping the window's taps and ceasing the copy (CR 704.5d). Q, Stacking the Deck. Bloodthirsty Adversary, Reenact the Crime, Infinite Diversity. Each cast puts a spell on the stack above this ability. Decision loop: pick one of the remaining spell cards or stop (gorge offers one with no legal target too: its cast is refused and it stays exiled); targets/modes/X(=0) for each as cast. Etali, Primal Storm (P1); The Key to the Vault, Breaching Dragonstorm (P1); Daring Waverider (P2); Buster Sword, Lady Octopus (P3); Sword of Once and Future (P4)."},
	{"op:MayPlay", "OpMayPlay (Obj card, A duration, C zone)", "The controller may play Obj from zone C (cast it paying its costs, or play it as their land drop) until the duration ends: DurEOT this turn, DurYourNextTurn until the end of their next turn, DurWhileSrcMay for as long as the Effect's source stays on the battlefield (Duration$ AsLongAsControl; gorge reads the source's zone and controller, and a control change ends the grant for good: Lightning, Security Sergeant). The permission ends if the card leaves that zone. Chandra +2 / Strongbox Raider / Kellan (exiled card), Zul Ashur (target Zombie creature card in your graveyard). B bit 8 (MayPlayAdventure): the permission offers the Adventure face only (Mosswood Dreadknight)."},
	{"op:CreateEmblem", "OpCreateEmblem (Obj player, C emblem, A number)", "The player gets `Table.Emblems[C]` in the command zone: its abilities (a triggered ability with Trigger.Zone ZoneCommand, or a static) function from there for the rest of the game. A is the Effect's frozen chosen number (0 when unused): evaluated once against the resolving Effect's context and stored in `State.g.embN` (clamped to 0..255), the value an emblem static marked StEmbNum reads. Kaito -9 (whenever a player casts a spell, create a 2/1 Ninja), Vivien Reid -8 (creatures you control get +2/+2 and have vigilance, trample, indestructible). A no-RememberObjects$ `DB$ Effect` static of Mode$ ReduceCost (an EOT emblem: Goblin Maskmaker's face-down discount, which gorge never applies because it prices the face-down cast against the card in hand) or Mode$ CanAttackDefender with ValidCard$ Card.EffectSource (a WhileHost emblem, also from a triggered Effect with no Duration$: Territorial Witchstalker, Stalked Researcher, Krotiq Nestguard; CR 611.2a). When every static of the Effect is a ReduceCost whose Amount$ is the SVar Count$ChosenNumber, kgen reads SetChosenNumber$ through lc.value into A and marks those statics StEmbNum (no Static.VA): gorge evaluates the number once at resolution (effects/effect.go's state.ContinuousEffect.ChosenNumber) and the cost path reads the frozen field, so a life total that changes later in the turn does not raise the discount (Rowan, Scion of War; Will, Scion of Peace). Any other SetChosenNumber$ shape refuses. A is the frozen number only in the default case: an Emblem with CapturePlayer (an Effect's RememberObjects$ TargetedPlayer over a DamageDone trigger with ValidTarget$ Player.IsRemembered, Great Train Heist's third mode) stores the targeted player's seat + 1 in `State.g.embN`, and the DamageDone hook fires only when the damaged player is that seat.  An EOT Effect with ValidTgts$ Creature and RememberObjects$ Targeted over a DamageDone trigger whose ValidSource$ is Creature.IsRemembered sets Emblem.Capture to the chain's target slot: OpCreateEmblem stores that object + 1 in `State.g.embN` (no frozen number shares the emblem), the trigger's filter carries no Remembered flag, and the DamageDone hook fires only when the damage source is the stored object, queued with the damage dealt as TriggerAmount (gorge: Creature.IsRemembered over the delayed trigger's Remembered, TriggerCount$DamageAmount). The Inner Light's chapter II draws that many cards. An Effect that remembers its targeted creature and carries one static beside one trigger lowers in two shapes. A CantBlockBy static (ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield) beside a combat DamageDealtOnce trigger of the remembered creature is the unblockable record plus an emblem with Capture and CaptureLapse: the hook fires once per combat damage batch (the DamageDealtOnce latch) and the body's first Remembered read is the damage source (Long River Lurker's flicker). A CanAttackDefender static (ForgetOnMoved$ Battlefield) beside a DamageDone trigger whose ValidSource$ is Card.Self is a Capture emblem of that static alone, because gorge registers nothing for the Effect's own copy of the trigger (the Effect never deals damage): the static gate reads State.g.embN, so the grant reaches only the captured creature (The Pride of Hull Clade). CaptureLapse zeroes embN when the captured object leaves the battlefield (a returned object is new, CR 400.7). An EOT Effect with no RememberObjects$ whose DamageDone trigger has ValidSource$ Card.EffectSource sets Emblem.Capture to the Effect's own source object (Lyra, Tolarian Archangel's \"whenever Lyra deals combat damage to a player\"): the filter is the remembered spelling, gorge's EffectSource being the source object by id, which a source that left and returned keeps. An Effect that remembers more than the one Targeted creature lowers in three more shapes (kop.Emblem; dirac/static_emblemrem.go, trig_emblemonce.go, trig_emblemrem.go). A permanent Effect with RememberObjects$ Remembered over a one-off Phase$ Upkeep trigger, in a spell or ability whose chain wrote the remembered set (The Eagles Are Coming!): A is the set's size (RememberedCount, frozen in State.g.embN), NumAmount carries it as each trigger's amount (the body's Remembered$Amount lowers to TriggerAmount, and any other Remembered read in the body refuses) and Once drops the emblem after the trigger first fires, as gorge's one-shot delayed trigger. An end-of-turn Effect with RememberObjects$ Targeted over a ChangesZone Battlefield-to-Graveyard trigger of ValidCard$ Creature.IsRemembered, over a chain of exactly two single battlefield target slots and no ValidTgts$ of its own (T'Pring, Never Parted): Capture and Capture2 are the two slots' objects (g.embN and g.embR, object + 1), the trigger's filter carries no Remembered flag and the dies hook fires only for a remembered object, queued as the creating card's latent copy; the Effect's ConditionDefined$ Targeted | ConditionPresent$ Creature | ConditionCompare$ EQ2 gate lowers to a SkipIf over both slots (RefMatches each, a moved card read as a card in its new zone). A permanent Effect with RememberObjects$ RememberedLKI, ForgetOnMoved$ Battlefield and a Card.EffectSource leave trigger over the tokens its resolution made (Mysterio, Master of Illusion): CaptureRem stores the resolution's remembered set (up to four objects in the emblem's slots, g.embN, g.embR and g.embX; a fifth stalls StallEmbRem), CaptureLapse drops an object when it leaves the battlefield, Source fires the leave trigger for the object that made the emblem alone, and the body (exactly the exile of Remembered from the battlefield) becomes OpExt ExtExileEmbRem over the objects the trigger carries. NotHere makes the emblem only while its host is off the battlefield: gorge ends a permanent Effect registered by a battlefield permanent with that incarnation (delayedRegistrationLive, SourceBattlefield), so Mysterio's leave trigger never fires when it was on the battlefield as the Effect was made, and fires, exiling the tokens it remembered, only for a registration made while it was gone (it died with its enters trigger on the stack) when that object leaves again."},
	{"op:Override", "OpOverride (Obj, A duration, C override)", "Apply `Table.Overrides[C]` to Obj for DurEOT, DurPermanent (until it leaves the battlefield) or DurUntilYourNextTurn (until the resolving controller's next turn begins: it ends at the cleanup before that turn, gorge UntilYourNextTurn; Azure Beastbinder). Override records apply in a fixed order: set types/subtypes/colours and lose-abilities, then add types/subtypes/keywords, set P/T before counters and pumps (CR 613 layers 4/5/6/7b collapsed into a fixed order — the plan's replacement for a layer system). Grant[i] (ability index+1 of the APPLYING card) is an ability the object gains. Users: Fake Your Own Death (grant a dies trigger, EOT), Kellan (becomes Human Faerie Detective / 3/2 Rogue with double strike, permanent, after a SkipUnless on its current subtype), Mild-Mannered Librarian (becomes a Werewolf), Soulstone Sanctuary (a 3/3 creature land with vigilance and all creature types), Infernal Vessel / Valkyrie's Call (the returned card is also a Demon / an Angel with flying)."},
	{"op:ReflexiveTrigger", "OpReflexiveTrigger (A count, C ability)", "'When you do': put this card's latent ability C on the stack A times (A=0: not at all); its targets are chosen as it is put on the stack, after the current resolution step. Faebloom Trick: A = tokens created / 2 (ExTokensCreated, Div 2), then tap target creature an opponent controls. B: the value the body reads as TriggerRemembered$ (Amount / CardManaCost / GreatestCardManaCost of the remembered set), evaluated in the parent's context as the trigger is put on the stack and carried as the entry's trigger amount; the zero Const (every other reflexive trigger) carries 0. Ill-Timed Explosion (X damage to each creature, X the highest mana value among the discarded cards: its Discard<> unless-cost, B=kop.PayBRemember, remembers what it discards), The Ancient One (mill equal to the discarded card's mana value), Miasma Demon (up to that many targets). Obj (RememberObjects$ Targeted): a target ref of the parent; the target's object and ver, when it is still the chosen object on the battlefield, ride the entry as trigObj and trigAmt (B is then the zero Const), and the body's Fight Defined$ DelayTriggerRemembered fights nothing once that object's ver has moved (a zone change makes a new object, CR 400.7; gorge effImmediateTrigger), where a body Bite from it (DealDamage DamageSource$ DelayTriggerRemembered NumDmg$ TriggerRemembered$CardPower) deals the creature's last known power, snapshotted into the entry's LKI record as it is put on the stack (CR 608.2h; gorge rules rememberedPTLKI). Novel Nunchaku, Curse of the Werefox, Thorin, Mountain-king."},
	{"op:DelayedProgram", "OpDelayedProgram (Obj objects, A timing, C ability)", "Register a delayed trigger: at the beginning of the next end step (anyone's; A = 0), the next upkeep of any player (A = kop.DelayUpkeep: gorge Phase$ Upkeep, ValidPlayer$ Player, the slowtrips' NextTurn$ True) the controller's next upkeep (A = kop.DelayYourUpkeep: ValidPlayer$ You) or the next end of combat step (A = kop.DelayEndCombat: Phase$ EndCombat), after that step's Phase triggers, or the remembered object's next battlefield-to-graveyard move this turn (A = kop.DelayDiesThisTurn: gorge Mode$ ChangesZone, ValidCard$ Card.IsTriggerRemembered, ThisTurn$ True; after the move's dies/leaves triggers; one-shot, dropped at the turn change), run this card's latent ability C with RefDelayedRemembered = the objects in Obj as they are now (cards that later change zones are still found). Kykar's blink (return the exiled card), Nine-Lives Familiar (return with one fewer revival counter). B = DpTrack registers the program tracked to the resolving source's object (Decayed's end-of-combat sacrifice): it is ordered with the other due triggers and, if that object has left, resolves doing nothing. B = DpMany registers the resolution's whole remembered set (up to four objects) for a body of OpBounce with BncDelayedMany, which returns each still on the battlefield to hand (Random Encounter: ChangeZoneAll ForgetOtherRemembered$ then a RememberObjects$ Remembered delayed trigger). The same program carries a RememberedLKI target slot of several objects (Hide on the Ceiling, Temporal Tribulation, Eerie Interlude: one Exile of the slot with RememberChanged$) for a body of OpReturn with kop.RetDelayedMany (Origin$ Exile), which returns every object still the one registered to the battlefield in registration order as one entering event."},
	{"op:GiveGift", "OpGiveGift", "The controller gives a gift (CR 702.174b): fire \"whenever you give a gift\" triggers (TrigGiveGift, Jolly Gerbils). The gift itself follows as ordinary ops (the GiftAbility body: a card for the opponent, a Food, a tapped Fish), the block guarded by CondPromised at the head of an instant's or sorcery's program (gorge rules/stack.go splices the GiftAbility at the head of the spell's chain and emits events.GiveGift just before it)."},
	{"op:BecomeCopy", "OpBecomeCopy (Obj replaced, F choices, A grant override, B.N BecomeCopyCtr, C optional|override<<1)", "As-enters replacement program (an ETBReplacement keyword line): while the permanent spell is on the stack about to resolve, its controller is asked the clone choice (DkChoose ChGenClone): each battlefield permanent matching F (seat 0's battlefield, then seat 1's, in entry order; F's mana-value bound may read ExCastManaSpent), then, when C&1 (the keyword line's :Optional) or nothing matches, \"enter as itself\" (mode 1, source = the spell). A pick makes the permanent enter as a copy of it (CR 707.2, 614.1c): the copied card's copiable values (its own copy, if it is one, and its copy exceptions) with B's exceptions as copiable values (CpFlying: flying; the subtype added, CR 707.9b); its triggered abilities see it enter. Entered any other way (not cast) nothing is asked and it enters as itself. Gorge: rules/cast_etbchoice.go collectETBChoices kind copy, effects/clone.go effClone (CloneEnter.ETB). The copied card's enters-tapped property, its printed K:etbCounter counters (CR 707.5) and its enters programs apply (a choice among them is asked once it has entered, not with the clone choice). Templates are creatures and artifacts only (kgen refuses an Aura or planeswalker template). The exceptions (C>>1, an override index+1) are read through copyExceptions like CopyPermanent's: AddTypes$ lists (card types, supertypes, subtypes), AddKeywords$, SetPower$/SetToughness$, AddColors$, SetColor$, NonLegendary$ (Visage Bandit, Glasspool Mimic, Phyrexian Metamorph, Quicksilver Gargantuan); NewName$ and AddKeywords$ Changeling (a CDA, gorge clone.go L531) refuse. B.N bit BecomeCopyCtr (kop.BecomeCopyCtr): the remembered copy origin's counters ride into the entering copy as it enters (Dominion Saboteur: RememberCloneOrigin$ True then PutCounter CounterType$ EachFromSource EachFromSource$ Remembered; CR 707.9b, 614.12), folded from the whole rider chain by kgen, on top of the template's own printed counters. A (an override index+1, 0: none): AddAbilities$ (Mercurial Pretender), the named SVars lowered as latent activated abilities of the entering card, applied to the copy as a permanent override record sourced from the printed card once a template is picked (gorge clone.go folds the grant into the copy's copiable values, CR 707.9b, so a copy of the copy has it too, CR 707.3; the kernel carries the record to a later copy of the copy, copyGrantsAdd, drops it when a newer copy layer covers the copy and re-derives it on a re-base, and reads the ability from the card that made the record, grantCardAt)."},
	{"op:GainControl", "OpGainControl (Obj, A.N duration, B.N GcUntap|GcHasteEOT, C new-controller Ref)", "The new controller (C: RefNone = the resolving controller, RefOpponent/RefEachOpponent, or a player target slot) gains control of Obj (CR 613.1b layer 2). A.N: DurEOT (CR 514.2), DurPermanent, DurYourNextTurn (to the end of the effect controller's next turn), DurWhileSource (LoseControl$ LeavesPlay: while the source stays on the battlefield), DurWhileControlSource (LeavesPlay,LoseControl: and while the effect's controller controls it); a source-bound duration already over at resolution does nothing (CR 611.2b). Each effect is a timestamped control record: when records end the object goes to the newest surviving record's controller, or to the controller before the earliest record (gorge expireControl); a source-bound record is checked by the state-based check. Riders: GcUntap untaps it (a stun counter is removed instead), GcHasteEOT gives haste until end of turn. Sower of Temptation, Act of Treason variants, Donate."},
	{"op:ClassLevelUp", "OpClassLevelUp (Obj self, A level)", "The resolving ability's source Class becomes level `A` (CR 716.2a): its CtrLevel count (level-1, a kind above NumCounterKinds2 that no counter census, doubling or projection sees) is set to `A-1`, and \"when this Class becomes level N\" triggers fire (TrigCounterAddedOnce with N = CtrLevel, gated Eq on the new level). Nothing when the source has left the battlefield or is already at level `A` or more. No decision. Gorge: effects/class_level.go effClassLevelUp (a designation, not a counter)."},
	{"op:ClearRemembered", "OpClearRemembered", "Forget the resolution's remembered set (RefRemembered)."},
	{"op:ClearChosen", "OpClearChosen", "Forget the chosen card(s) (RefChosen)."},
	{"op:DoubleCounters", "OpDoubleCounters (Obj, C kind)", "Put on each object in Obj as many counters of kind C as it has (C=255: do that for every kind it has). Mossborn Hydra (+1/+1 on itself), Zimone (every kind, up to two targets)."},
	{"op:RemoveCounterRem", "OpRemoveCounterRem (Obj, A, C kind)", "Remove up to A counters of kind C from Obj; the number actually removed becomes ExRememberedCount (Fishing Pole: 'remove a bait counter. If you do, create a Fish')."},
	{"ext:EnterAttacking", "OpExt ExtEnterAttacking (Obj RefReplaced)", "Replacement program, after OpEnterTapped: the entering object enters attacking the controller's opponent (CR 508.4, 614.12; never declared, so no Attacks trigger), only in the controller's own declare attackers..end of combat. Kira Nerys, Firebrand's `R:Event$ Moved` with `IsPresent$ Creature.attacking+YouCtrl` and a `DB$ ChangeZone | Defined$ ReplacedCard | Tapped$ True | Attacking$ True` body; two or more CR 508.4 defenders stall (StallTokAtkAsk)."},
	{"op:EnterTapped", "OpEnterTapped (Obj RefReplaced)", "Replacement program: the entering object enters tapped (CR 614.1c). Used by ReplOthersEnterProgram (Authority of the Consuls); a self enters-tapped is ReplEntersTapped."},
	{"op:EnterWithCounters", "OpEnterWithCounters (Obj RefReplaced, A, C kind)", "Replacement program: the entering object enters with A counters of kind C (CR 614.1c, CR 122.6: the object enters with them). Whether CounterAddedOnce triggers (Wildwood Scourge, Exemplar of Light) see these counters: mirror gorge, the oracle decides. Conditional/X forms: Gnarlid Colony (kicked), Goblin Boarders (raid), Nine-Lives Familiar (cast by you), Wildwood Scourge (X), Banner of Kinship (count of the chosen type), Giada (other Angels, count of Angels you control)."},
	{"op:CopyAsTokenEx", "OpCopyAsTokenEx (Obj, A count, B.N CopyFlags, C exception override+1)", "The controller creates A tokens that are copies of Obj (copiable values: its card's printed characteristics, CR 707.2; a copy of a card in exile/graveyard copies the card). C names the copy exceptions (CR 707.9b) as a Table.Overrides record: set P/T (Offspring's 1/1, SetPower$/SetToughness$), added keywords (AddKeywords$: Chandra's haste; AddKeywords$ Changeling: every creature type, Dominion Infiltration), an added subtype (AddTypes$: Abyssal Harvester's Nightmare), added card types and supertypes (AddTypes$: Artifact, Creature & Balloon, Legendary; the types are ORed into the base types at layer 1), added colours (AddColors$, after any set colour), AddStaticAbilities$ naming one equip cost reduction of the copy itself (GrantStatics: an OvGate bit that switches on the reduction lowerPool adds to every pool card with an Equip ability; Firion, Wild Rose Warrior), and NonLegendary$ (the copy's type line loses Legendary, applied after the added types; the legend rule reads the derived types, so the copy and its legendary original coexist; gorge copypermanent.go removeLegendary). They are the copy's layer-1 copiable values, so a copy of the copy inherits them and a later set-P/T effect overrides the 1/1 only while it lasts. CpSacAtEnd: at the beginning of the next end step, sacrifice it (Chandra +1, Electroduplicate). CpSacAtUpkeep (both CpSacAtEndDly and CpExileAtEnd; AtEOT$ SacrificeUpkeep): the untracked one-shot sacrifice at the beginning of the next upkeep of any player (delayed.when dlyUpkeep; Firion). B.N >> CopyPumpShift: PumpKeywords$, an override record (index+1) of a permanent keyword grant on each token after it enters; it is NOT a copy exception, so a copy of the token lacks it; with CopyPumpEOT (PumpDuration$ EOT: Gray and Adira, God-Pharaoh's Gift) the grant lasts until end of turn. CpRemember: the tokens become RefRemembered. CpExileAtEnd: at the beginning of the next end step, exile it (AtEOT$ Exile: Stormsplitter, Splinter Twin; gorge scheduleAtEOT). CpTapped: the token enters tapped (TokenTapped$ True: Replicator). CopyNonRemCtrl (bit 15): the tokens are created for the opponent of the remembered permanent's last-known controller (Controller$ NonRememberedController: Fractured Identity). Users also Self-Reflection, Homunculus Horde, Extravagant Replication."},
	{"op:CreateTokenEx", "OpCreateTokenEx (Obj, A, B.N TokenFlags|(Ref<<8), C token)", "OpCreateToken with TokRemember: the number created is readable as ExTokensCreated (Faebloom Trick). TokTapped as TrTapped. TokAttach: the token enters attached to the object B.N's high byte names (RefTarget0..2 or RefSelf, kop.TokAttachDest); it is not created when that object is not on the battlefield (CR 303.4g, gorge auraTokenWithheld) or when nothing on the board can be enchanted (gorge auraTokenGate), and the attach is not checked for legality (the CR 704.5m SBA removes an illegal attachment). A Role token's attach first sweeps every other Role off the bearer (CR 303.7a, gorge's attach-time sweep; static_roletokens.go). Both TokSacAtEnd and TokExileAtEnd set: an extended AtEOT$ rider, its kind in B.N's high byte (kop.TokAtEOTDestroy: destroy the token at the beginning of the next end step, tracked, indestructible and regeneration apply; kop.TokAtEOTSacCombat: sacrifice it at this turn's end of combat, untracked; gorge effects/ateot.go; trig_tokenateot.go); never with TokAttach."},
	// --- refs ---
	{"ref:Remembered", "RefRemembered", "The resolution's remembered set: objects an op with Remember put there (ExileEx/DigEx/ChangeZone RememberChanged, CopyAsTokenEx CpRemember). Cleared by OpClearRemembered and at resolution end."},
	{"ref:DelayedRemembered", "RefDelayedRemembered", "Inside a delayed program: the objects it was registered with, followed to their current zone."},
	{"ref:Replaced", "RefReplaced", "Inside a replacement program: the object that is entering."},
	{"ref:TriggerSource", "RefTriggerSource", "The source of the damage that caused a DamageDone/DamageDealtOnce trigger (its last known information if it left): Drake Hatcher, Quilled Greatwurm put counters on it."},
	{"ref:Sacrificed", "RefSacrificed", "The permanent sacrificed to pay this ability's cost, with its last known values (Heartfire Immolator: damage equal to its power)."},
	{"ref:Host", "RefHost", "In an ability granted by a static (Static.Grant): the permanent that grants it (Fishing Pole's 'put a bait counter on Fishing Pole')."},
	{"ref:Targets01", "RefTargets01", "Every legal target of slots 0 and 1, in slot order (each slot's first object, then its others): the op runs once per object inside one batch; a destroy first drops the indestructible ones, as gorge's victim list does. Gorge: Defined$ Targeted over a SubAbility$ chain reads the union of the chain's targets (rules chainTargetUnion, effects refTargetUnion), an illegal target left out (CR 608.2b). Fumarole, Plague Spores, Boom."},
	{"ref:Targets012", "RefTargets012", "As RefTargets01 over slots 0, 1 and 2 (Boom Box, Arm the Cathars, Relive the Past)."},
	{"ref:Targets12", "RefTargets12", "As RefTargets01 over slots 1 and 2 (a charm mode's chain)."},
	{"ref:Targets0123", "RefTargets0123", "As RefTargets01 over slots 0 to 3 (Rise from the Wreck)."},
	{"ref:Discarded", "RefDiscarded", "The card the resolving spell's own Discard<1/Card> cost discarded, read where it now is (gorge refTargetsDiscarded over Ctx.Paid.Discarded, cr-discarded-cost-value-ref); a copy keeps it (CR 707.10). Recorded in the spell entry's trigObj at payment. Grab the Prize's Discarded$Valid Card.nonLand."},
	{"ref:RememberedController", "RefRememberedController", "A player ref: the first remembered object's controller; off the battlefield after a RememberLKI$ move (MvLKI), the controller its last known information holds (CR 608.2h; gorge rememberedControllersLKI). TokenOwner$ RememberedController (Unyielding Gatekeeper)."},
	{"ref:OppNonRemCtrl", "RefOppNonRemCtrl", "A player ref: the controller's opponent, unless some remembered object's controller (its RememberLKI$ capture off the battlefield, else the live one; CR 608.2h) is that opponent, then nobody. Every remembered object is tested. gorge definedSpecNonRememberedController. Momentum Breaker, Entropic Battlecruiser."},
	{"ref:Promised", "RefPromised", "A player ref: the opponent the gift was promised to (CR 702.174a; gorge Defined$ Promised, Object.GiftPromisedTo): the spell entry's election (stackEntry.grp beside sfPromised), or a permanent's gift trigger's snapshot taken as it is queued (trigPl; gorge's trigger GiftTo). None when no gift was promised. Wear Down, Valley Rally."},
	{"ref:SrcOwner", "RefSrcOwner", "A player ref: the resolving source object's owner (CR 108.3; gorge definedSpecCardOwner). Gandalf, Wandering Wizard's draw."},
	{"ref:RememberedOwner", "RefRememberedOwner", "A player ref: the remembered object's owner (CR 108.3; gorge definedSpecRememberedOwner over the source's persistent event-backed Remembered list). Lowered only inside the remembered-persist shape (card:RemPersist): the leave trigger's resolution starts with the enters trigger's kept set, and the ref names its first object's owner — an empty set names nobody (gorge manifests dread for nobody). Unidentified Hovership's leave trigger."},
	{"ref:TriggerAttackers", "RefTriggerAttackers", "An AttackersDeclared trigger's attacker group: the attackers of the DeclareAttackers event that raised it (a per-defender line: that defender's group; the batch line: the whole declaration), captured when the trigger is queued (CR 508.1m, 508.3b, 508.3d, 603.2c) and read where they are at resolution, so a creature that left the battlefield is skipped. It is the event's group, not the subset the line's ValidAttackers$ matched (that count is TriggerAmount). gorge definedSpecTriggeredAttackers reads the queue entry's Remembered. Only OpPumpUntilEOT, OpPutCounter and OpGrantKeyword run it, once per attacker, the amount read once; kgen refuses every other op. Jiang Yanggu, Alone's counters, Sabotage Strategist's -1/-0."},
	// --- values ---
	{"v:Expr", "VExpr (N = Table.Exprs index)", "Evaluate the Expr: compute Kind over its operands, then `*Mul` (0 = 1), floor `/Div` (0 = 1), `+Add`, negate if Neg. Kinds below."},
	{"ex:CountGraveyard", "ExCountGraveyard (F)", "Cards in graveyards matching F (F.Ctrl = owner)."},
	{"ex:SumPower", "ExSumPower (F)", "Total power of battlefield creatures matching F (Ghalta's reduction)."},
	{"ex:DistinctCMC", "ExDistinctCMC (F)", "Number of distinct mana values among battlefield objects matching F (Lunar Insight)."},
	{"ex:TargetPlayers", "ExTargetPlayers (Ref: a target slot)", "1 when the target slot Ref holds a player at this point of the resolution, else 0 (an unfilled optional slot, or a player no longer a legal target, CR 608.2b); gorge TargetedPlayer$Amount, which counts the resolution's player targets, over an opponents-only slot two-player. Hollow Marauder."},
	{"ex:CounterKinds", "ExCounterKinds (F)", "Number of distinct counter kinds with a positive count among battlefield objects matching F, gorge's regeneration-shield and deathtouch markers and a Class level not counted (gorge Count$DifferentCounterKinds_<spec>; only Creature.YouCtrl lowers). Hundred-Battle Veteran."},
	{"ex:Kicked", "ExKicked (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the spell (or the permanent's spell) was kicked, else Sub[1]."},
	{"ex:Sneaked", "ExSneaked (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the resolving spell was cast for its sneak cost, else Sub[1] (Count$ValidStack Card.Self+sneaked; CR 702.190a). Reads the stack entry's trigPlSneak mark; a battlefield permanent has no sneaked mark."},
	{"ex:Converge", "ExConverge", "The number of distinct colours (W U B R G) of mana spent to cast a spell (Count$Converge; gorge Object.ConvergeColours, the pay-time FlagConverged CastInfo): the per-colour pool drop of the cast's payment, a generic pip paid from a coloured unit counting toward its colour, tallied in the spell's stack entry (stackEntry.spc, saturating 2-bit counts). Read in the spell's chain and its K:etbCounter enters replacement (the resolving spell entering), or in a self-ETB trigger (Tf3ConvergeBound: bound as it triggers, 0 once the source left the battlefield). A copy and an object entering uncast read 0. Arcane Omens, Rancorous Archaic, Sundering Archaic."},
	{"ex:CastFromGrave", "ExCastFromGrave (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the resolving spell was cast from a graveyard, by a graveyard-origin cast flag (flashback, harmonize, jumpstart, escape) or its cast zone, else Sub[1] (ConditionPresent$ Card.wasCastFromGraveyard; Count$wasCastFromGraveyard.<yes>.<no>; CR 601.2a, 702.34a). Reads the stack entry's sfFlashback flag or its recorded cast zone (stackEntry.prov, genPrep.anyCastProv) and excludes a copy (CR 707.10), as gorge state.ObjectWasCastFromGraveyard does: a may-play permission cast from a graveyard reads true."},
	{"ex:FirstCast", "ExFirstCast (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the resolving spell was the first spell its controller cast this game, else Sub[1] (the static SpellCast trigger with ValidCard$ Card.Self whose DB$ StoreSVar writes Count$YouCastThisGame at cast, read by the spell's ConditionCheckSVar$ with ConditionSVarCompare$ EQ1; gorge Host.SpellsCastThisGame). The flag is stamped on the stack entry when the cast completes (CR 601.2i), so a spell cast in response after it does not take it away; a seat's earlier cast does; a stack copy keeps the original's stamp, as gorge's copy reads the original object's stored SVar. One bit per seat in genState.cast1 plus the entry's remVer bit; no counter, so only EQ1 lowers. First Contact."},
	{"ex:IfCastOwnMain", "ExIfCastOwnMain (Sub[0] yes, Sub[1] no)", "Sub[0] if the step now is a main phase, the spell\u2019s controller is the active player and the spell was cast (not a stack copy, CR 707.10), else Sub[1] (gorge Count$IfCastInOwnMainPhase.<yes>.<no>; the arms are integers). The read is live, as gorge\u2019s: a spell cast in a main phase and resolved in another step reads Sub[1]. Read in a spell ability only, at the target announcement (a TargetMax$ value) and at the resolution. dirac/value_ifcastmain.go. Return to Dust."},
	{"ex:PromisedGift", "ExPromisedGift (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the gift was promised (the entry's sfPromised flag; a permanent read as it enters: its resolving spell's), else Sub[1] (gorge Count$PromisedGift.a.b)."},
	{"ex:CommittedCrime", "ExCommittedCrime (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the controller committed a crime this turn, else Sub[1] (gorge Count$CommittedCrimeThisTurn, effects cov3BranchHoldsCommittedCrimeThisTurn; CR 700.13). Reads State.g.crime (act_commitcrime.go committedCrime); Servant of the Stinger's CheckDefinedPlayer$ You.committedCrimeThisTurn lowers to it as an intervening-if."},
	{"trig:AbilityCast", "TrigAbilityCast", "Whenever a player (Whose: You or any) activates an exhaust ability (Trigger.N 1, ValidSA$ Activated.Exhaust), a loyalty ability (2, Activated.Loyalty), or a loyalty ability an opponent of the listener's controller controls (3, Activated.Loyalty+OppCtrl); CR 602.2, 603.2; gorge Mode$ AbilityCast, trigmatch abilityCastMatches. Fired as the activation completes, after its costs are paid. No slot subscription: the battlefield, then graveyard cards (TriggerZones$ Graveyard), are scanned (genPrep.anyAbilityCast, trig_abilitycast.go). TargetsValid$, ValidCard$, ValidSAonCard$, Player.NonActive and other ValidSA$ values refuse. Afterburner Expert, Rangers' Refueler, Ajani Unrelenting, Gideon the Oathless."},
	{"trig:CommitCrime", "TrigCommitCrime", "Whenever a player (Whose) commits a crime (CR 700.13; gorge Mode$ CommitCrime, trigmatch commitCrimeMatches): once per recorded stack object whose targets include an opponent, an opponent's permanent or spell, or a card in an opponent's graveyard. No slot subscription: the battlefield, then graveyard cards (TriggerZones$ Graveyard), are scanned (act_commitcrime.go fireCrime). Spell targets are judged at the pick, abilities after payment, triggers at placement, copies at their new-target answer; a mid-resolution target is no crime (gorge)."},
	{"trig:FullyUnlock", "TrigFullyUnlock", "Whenever a player fully unlocks a Room (CR 709.5i; gorge Mode$ FullyUnlock, trigmatch fullyUnlockMatches): on the one DoorUnlock of a real locked->unlocked transition that leaves both doors unlocked. ValidCard$ is the Room (absent = Card.Room), ValidPlayer$ the unlocker (absent = any). No slot subscription: the unlock action scans battlefield listeners, then graveyard cards (TriggerZones$ Graveyard; Fear of Infinity), before the unlocked door's own UnlockDoor triggers (face_fullyunlock.go fireFullyUnlock)."},
	{"ex:Morbid", "ExMorbid (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if a creature died this turn, else Sub[1] (gorge Count$Morbid)."},
	{"ex:AttackedTurn", "ExAttackedTurn (F)", "The objects declared as attackers this turn that match F where each now is, each once (gorge Count$CreaturesAttackedThisTurn <spec>, evalCov3HeadCreaturesAttackedThisTurn, engine/effects/count_cov3.go:155-171, over AttackersDeclaredThisTurn, rules/host_turn_ledger.go:235-255): an object-width arena mask (mechAttackedObj, 0 B) set for each declared attacker after the declaration's triggers and cleared at turn start, so it follows an attacker that died or left; a battlefield object is matched as a permanent, one in another zone as a card (the spec defaults to Creature). An object put onto the battlefield attacking is not declared. dirac/value_turntallies.go. Avengers Assemble!, Thaumaton Torpedo."},
	{"ex:AttackedThisTurn", "ExAttackedThisTurn", "Number of creatures the controller declared as attackers this turn (gorge Count$AttackersDeclared; Raid tests it >= 1)."},
	{"ex:PowerOf", "ExPowerOf (Ref)", "Current power of Ref (last known if it left)."},
	{"ex:ToughnessOf", "ExToughnessOf (Ref)", "Current toughness of Ref."},
	{"ex:LifeOf", "ExLifeOf (Ref player)", "Life total of the player."},
	{"ex:LibrarySizeOf", "ExLibrarySizeOf (Ref player)", "Cards in the player's library."},
	{"ex:StartingLife", "ExStartingLife", "The controller's starting life (20), plus Add."},
	{"ex:TriggerAmount", "ExTriggerAmount", "The triggering event's amount (as VTriggerAmount), when modified."},
	{"ex:LifeGainedThisTurn", "ExLifeGainedThisTurn", "Life the controller gained this turn."},
	{"ex:OppLifeLostThisTurn", "ExOppLifeLostThisTurn", "Life the controller's opponents lost this turn."},
	{"ex:LifeLostThisTurn", "ExLifeLostThisTurn", "Life the controller lost this turn (gorge PlayerCountPropertyYou$LifeLostThisTurn)."},
	{"ex:Sum", "ExSum (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] + Sub[1]: a value modifier naming an SVar (/Plus.Y; /Minus.Y negates Sub[1])."},
	{"ex:RollResult", "ExRollResult", "The result (die + modifier) of the resolution's last OpRollDie: gorge's RollDice ResultSVar$ publication read back by a sub's bare-name amount (Num's runtimePublished fallback, after the card's own SVars)."},
	{"op:RollDie", "OpRollDie (A sides, B.N modifier)", "The controller rolls one die with `A` sides: one rng IntN(A) draw (gorge h.Rand, the engine's seeded PCG), result = draw + 1 + `B.N`, kept as ExRollResult. No decision. A ResultSubAbilities$ range table lowers to SkipIf blocks over ExRollResult, in the table's order, before the roll's SubAbility$ (gorge effRollDice resolves the range's sub inside the effect). Gorge: effects/dice.go effRollDice (one die; Amount$, IgnoreLower$, UseHighestRoll$, ChosenSVar$ refused)."},
	{"ex:CastManaSpent", "ExCastManaSpent", "The mana spent to cast the spell being resolved or entering (gorge Object.ManaSpent, Count$CastTotalManaSpent): the cast's paid mana cost, X included, recorded at payment in the spell's stack entry (histCast); 0 for a spell not cast or cast without paying. Read only by an as-enters copy's choice bound. Mockingbird."},
	{"ex:Activations", "ExActivations", "The resolving activated ability's source's non-mana activations this turn, this one included (gorge `ConditionActivationLimit$ GE<n>`, Ctx.ActivationsThisTurn), read from the object's per-turn census (object.acts, counted as the activation is pushed, CR 602.2a; zero once the source has left, CR 400.7). The census is per object, so the lowering admits only a card whose one non-mana activated ability is the counted one. Dragon Whelp."},
	{"ex:DmgAmountReceived", "ExDmgAmountReceived", "The positive damage the source object received this turn (gorge Object.DamageReceivedThisTurn, `Count$TotalDamageReceivedThisTurn`): every damage site records it in genState.dmgAmt for a card whose CardDef.DmgAmt is set, saturating at 255 and cleared at the turn change; the object keeps its record across a zone change, as gorge's does (only WasDealtDamageThisTurn clears on a re-entry). Tangled Colony."},
	{"ex:TgtSpent", "ExTgtSpent", "The mana spent to cast the spell the resolving spell targets (gorge TargetManaSpent, `Targeted$CastTotalManaSpent`), snapshotted as the resolution starts in `State.g.tgtSpent` (+1, saturating at 255; 0 with no snapshot) because a Counter later in the chain removes the target's stack entry and its recorded spend. The resolving spell must have exactly one target slot, a spell on the stack. Only a resolving spell snapshots it, and it ends with the resolution. EOE Unravel."},
	{"ex:ResolvedThisTurn", "ExResolvedThisTurn", "The times the resolving triggered ability (AfResolveCount) resolved this turn, this resolution included (gorge Count$ResolvedThisTurn, events foldResolve). Harvestrite Host."},
	{"ex:CountAtLeast", "ExCountAtLeast (F, N, Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] if the battlefield objects matching F number at least N, else Sub[1] (gorge evalCompare: Count$Compare <count SVar> GE<n>.<then>.<else>; GT n lowers as GE n+1). Dazzling Denial's unless cost: {4} if you control a Bird, else {2}."},
	{"ex:ThisTurnCastSpec", "ExThisTurnCastSpec (N CastSpec bits, F)", "The casts put on the stack this turn that match F where each object now is (gorge rules/host_cast_ledger.go spellsCastThisTurnMatching). N's bits: CastSpecYou (the spec says You: only the evaluating controller's casts), CastSpecExclude (a source-object cast is dropped: the !CastSaSource token, and always for the $CardTypes aggregate, whose gorge call passes c.Source), CastSpecHand / CastSpecNotHand (the push's origin hand bit), CastSpecTreasure (the cast spent mana from a Treasure), CastSpecGrave (the bare wasCastFromGraveyard CastFlags/latest-origin read), CastSpecExile (the push came from exile), CastSpecCtrlTrig (the object's current controller is the trigger's activating player; +ControlledBy TriggeredActivator) and CastSpecTypes (return the popcount of the matching objects' distinct card types, the count-level $CardTypes aggregate, instead of a count). Magebane Lizard, April O'Neil, Hacktivist."},
	{"ex:CountersOn", "ExCountersOn (Ref, Ctr)", "Counters of kind Ctr on Ref (last known)."},
	{"ex:CreaturesDied", "ExCreaturesDied", "Creatures put into a graveyard from the battlefield this turn (any controller)."},
	{"ex:RememberedCount", "ExRememberedCount", "Size of the remembered set / the count OpRemoveCounterRem recorded."},
	{"ex:ExcessDamage", "ExExcessDamage", "Excess damage recorded by the previous DealDamageEx with DmgTrackExcess."},
	{"ex:LastLifeLost", "ExLastLifeLost", "Total life lost to the previous OpLoseLife of this program (Exsanguinate)."},
	{"ex:TokensCreated", "ExTokensCreated", "Tokens created by the previous OpCreateTokenEx with TokRemember."},
	{"ex:Count", "ExCount (F)", "Battlefield objects matching F, when modified (Add/Mul/Neg). N 1: the distinct planeswalker subtypes printed on the matching planeswalkers (gorge `Count$Valid <spec>$PlaneswalkerType`; Tam, the Possibility)."},
	{"ex:X", "ExX", "X, when modified."},
	{"ex:HandSizeOf", "ExHandSizeOf (Ref)", "Cards in player Ref's hand. Gorge: `Count$CardsInYourHand`, `PlayerCountOpponents$HighestCardsInHand` (two players: the opponent's). Beza."},
	{"ex:CountExile", "ExCountExile (F)", "Exiled cards matching F, every player's exile (F.Owner narrows). Gorge: `Count$ValidExile`, and with ExCountGraveyard under ExSum `Count$ValidGraveyard,Exile`. Huskburster Swarm."},
	{"ex:OppsLostLife", "ExOppsLostLife (N 0 lost life, N 1 hit by a legendary creature)", "The number of the controller's opponents who lost life this turn (two players: 0 or 1). Gorge: `PlayerCountRegisteredOpponents$HasPropertyLostLifeThisTurn`. Gev. N 1 is the opponents dealt combat damage this turn by a source matching Creature.Legendary (gorge `HasPropertywasDealtCombatDamageThisTurnBy Creature.Legendary GE1`, playerCountDefinedRegistered, effects/count_player.go:350-410, over the hit ledger rules/combat.go:2531, host_turn_ledger.go:21-38): one bit per player in genState.cdLeg, set when a landed hit (after prevention, amount > 0) comes from a creature that is legendary at the hit, cleared at turn start. Only that exact spec and threshold lowers; any other refuses. dirac/value_turntallies.go. Blitzball."},
	{"ex:HighestOppPoison", "ExHighestOppPoison", "The highest poison count among the controller's living opponents, in group order (two players: the opponent's). An empty group reads 0. Gorge: `PlayerCountOpponents$HighestCounters.Poison`, playerCountExtreme's Counters.Poison arm; the ONE Corrupted statics and gates (Apostle of Invasion, Bonepicker Skirge, ...)."},
	{"ex:MVOf", "ExMVOf (Ref)", "The mana value of object Ref's card: the printed total, plus the announced X while Ref is a spell on the stack (CR 202.3e; kernel objMV). Gorge: `TriggeredCard$CardManaCost`. Jackdaw Savior, Clement, Chrome Host Seedshark."},
	{"ex:RefCount", "ExRefCount (Ref, F)", "The objects Ref names that match F where they now are (a battlefield permanent through the permanent matcher, a moved card in its new zone): gorge evalRefProperty's Valid <spec> over the live object. Lowered only for TriggeredSource$Valid in a DamageDone trigger body and for RefSacrificed + the exact Card.IsSuspected filter or Card.<creature type> / Creature.<creature type> (read from the sacrifice-time LKI snapshot's designation or derived creature-type mask, gorge sacrificedValidCount); Card.!ThisTurnEntered is 1 minus the Card.ThisTurnEntered count. Moon-Circuit Hacker, Agency Coroner, Gowron, Eager for Battle."},
	{"ex:TriggerSpellMVLKI", "ExTriggerSpellMVLKI", "The mana value of the spell that triggered this SpellCast ability, as gorge's last known information: the pre-cast card (a split card sums its halves, an announced {X} is not counted); a copied spell reads its copied face plus X. Gorge: `TriggeredSpellAbility$CardManaCostLKI`. Manaplasm, Erratic Cyclops, Kaervek the Merciless, Skittering Cicada, Hammerhead Tyrant, Prismari Apprentice."},
	{"ex:PoisonOf", "ExPoisonOf (Ref)", "Poison counters of player Ref (CR 122.1f). Gorge: `TargetedController$Counters.Poison`, evalPlayerRefProperty's Counters.Poison arm over controllersOf(the targets). Anoint with Affliction."},
	{"ex:Product", "ExProduct (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Sub[0] * Sub[1]: a /Times.Y modifier naming an SVar (gorge applyCountOpOperand resolves the operand, then applyCountOp's Times arm). Lunar Convocation."},
	{"ex:AttackersAll", "ExAttackersAll", "Attackers declared this turn by every player, summed per declaration (gorge `PlayerCountPlayers$AttackersDeclared`, Engine.AttackersThisTurn). Witchstalker Frenzy."},
	{"ex:OppsAttacked", "ExOppsAttacked", "The opponents the controller attacked this turn: the players named as defender by a declaration this turn, 0 for a controller who is not the active player (gorge `PlayerCountPropertyYou$OpponentsAttackedThisTurn`, Engine.OpponentsAttackedThisTurn); 0 or 1 with one opponent. Kurn, Son of Mogh."},
	// --- conditions ---
	{"cond:Present", "CondPresent (F, Op, A)", "The number of battlefield objects matching F (relative to the controller) compares Op with A."},
	{"cond:Value", "CondValue (A, Op, B)", "A compares Op with B."},
	{"cond:Threshold", "CondThreshold", "Seven or more cards in the controller's graveyard."},
	{"cond:YourTurn", "CondYourTurn", "It is the controller's turn."},
	{"cond:RefMatches", "CondRefMatches (Ref, F, Op, A)", "The number of objects in Ref matching F compares Op with A (Scavenging Ooze: the exiled card was a creature; Soul-Shackled Zombie: a creature card among the exiled; Nine-Lives Familiar: it was cast by you)."},
	{"cond:And", "CondAnd (Sub[0], Sub[1])", "Both Sub[0] and Sub[1] hold, re-evaluated whenever the static is read (CR 611.3a)."},
	// --- statics / repls ---
	{"stat:CDAPT", "StatCDAPT (VA, VB)", "Characteristic-defining P/T (CR 604.3, layer 7a): the source's power is VA and toughness VB in every zone. Consuming Aberration."},
	{"stat:NoMaxHandSize", "StatNoMaxHandSize", "The controller has no maximum hand size (cleanup discard skipped). A is the maximum plus one when numeric (The Ten Rings 11, Doctor Octopus 9), 0 unlimited. Niv-Mizzet."},
	{"stat:TapExtra", "StatTapExtra (Filter, A, B, StFlags)", "Whenever the controller taps a permanent matching Filter for mana, they add B mana of colour A (index W U B R G C), once per tap, beside the tapped source's own mana (CR 106.12a, 605.1b; a Mode$ TapsForMana | Static$ True trigger whose body is one literal DB$ Mana). StTapOnC: only a tap that declares {C} (Produced$ C). StTapReflect: B mana of the type the tap produced instead of colour A (a DB$ ManaReflected body over basic lands, or over artifact tokens: Roxanne, Starfall Savant, whose Meteorite's one mana of any color is the planner's n+1 mana of one colour). StTapAnyPlayer: every player's taps, the extra to the tapping player (Lavaleaper; a body adding to the tapped permanent's controller, Wild Growth). Groundchuck & Dirtbag, Badgermole Cub, Forsaken Monument. A source the extra cannot be modelled on (a colour choice beside {C}, a painful, sacrificed or restricted source) stalls (StallTapExtra)."},
	{"stat:ExtraLandPlay", "StatExtraLandPlay", "The controller may play one additional land each of their turns. Loot."},
	{"stat:MayPlayFrom", "StatMayPlayFrom (Filter, Zone, StFlags)", "The controller may play cards matching Filter from Zone (graveyard, exile, hand, library: the priority player's top card only), under Cond2. StOncePerTurn: one card per turn through this static (Muldrotha has one static per permanent type; a card of two types uses one permission of the player's choice — a decision when ambiguous). StAnyManaType: mana of any type may be spent (Tinybones). StWithoutManaCost: free (Omniscience). StFunctionsInGraveyard + StRemove6Counters: the card itself may be cast from the graveyard by also removing six counters from among creatures you control (Quilled Greatwurm; decision: which counters). StFunctionsInExile: the card itself may be cast from exile while the static functions there (Khan, Vengeful Heart). StFreeOnly: the static only waives the mana cost and opens no zone (MayPlayDontGrantZonePermissions); it joins the free flag of any permission admitting the card."},
	{"stat:MayPlayFrom+StMayRaise", "StatMayPlayFrom (StFlags StMayRaise, B)", "The permission also carries a non-mana RaiseCost$ (CR 601.2f/h; gorge mayPlayRaiseCost): Static.B is 1 + the index of a latent ability of the static's source card whose Cost is the raise: PayLife<N> (Noctis, Prince of Lucis: artifact spells from your graveyard), Discard<1/Card> (Alien Symbiosis), or PayLife<N> + Sac<1/filter> (Wickerfolk Indomitable; the life rides in Cost.Ctr beside the sacrifice's Cost.N). The cast pays it as its pick cost; an unpayable raise withholds the offer. Two granting statics that both raise stall loud (StallMayRaise)."},
	{"stat:MaxBlockers", "StatMaxBlockers (Filter, Cond2)", "Attacking creatures matching Filter can't be blocked by more than one creature while Cond2 holds (S:Mode$ MinMaxBlocker | Max$ 1, CR 509.1b): a second block on such an attacker is not offered at any pick, and an attacker whose floor (menace, Min$) exceeds the cap is never blocked. Not when the source has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/restrictions.go MinMaxBlockerBounds. Safewright Cavalry, Rope, Flopsie."},
	{"stat:UntapOther", "StatUntapOther (Filter)", "Permanents matching Filter (Card.Self, or a ValidCard$ over the controller's own permanents) untap during each other player's untap step, after that player's untap action: a stun counter is removed instead; the active player's skip-untap gates do not apply. Gorge: rules/turn.go finishUntapStep, untap.go untapOtherStaticsMatch. Bender's Waterskin, Thousand Moons Infantry, Unwinding Clock."},
	{"stat:CombatDmgToughness", "StatCombatDmgToughness (Filter, Cond2)", "Creatures matching Filter assign combat damage equal to their toughness rather than their power (CR 510.1): the attacker's assignment, the blocker's damage and the division options all read it. Gorge: rules/statics_assignment.go combatDamageAmount. Bark of Doran, Bedrock Tortoise."},
	{"stat:CantGainLife", "StatCantGainLife (Cond2)", "No player gains life while the static functions: the gain is swallowed before any gain replacement, so no LifeGained trigger and no life-gained tally (CR 119.7; gorge rules/replacement_life.go lifeGainForbidden). Giant Cindermaw, Mornsong Aria."},
	{"stat:AsIfHaste", "StatAsIfHaste (Filter, Cond2)", "The static's controller may activate abilities of battlefield creatures matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\") as though they had haste (S:Mode$ ActivateAbilityAsIfHaste, CR 302.6): every {T}/{Q} activation-sickness check, mana abilities included, exempts the creature; it is not a haste grant, so the creature still can't attack. Gorge: rules/activateasifhaste.go activatesAsIfHaste, read at pay.TapFlagsSick. Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu."},
	{"stat:CantBeSuspected", "StatCantBeSuspected (Filter, Cond2)", "A battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) can't become suspected (CR 701.60): a suspect effect skips it (an Optional$ suspect over it is still asked, as gorge's guard does not read the static, and then does nothing); a designation it already has stays (gorge rules/cantbesuspected.go gates the Suspected AlterAttribute event only). Airtight Alibi."},
	{"stat:CantDraw", "StatCantDraw (Cond2)", "No player draws a card while the static functions: the draw does not happen, no Drawn trigger and no drawn-this-turn count; an empty library still marks the CR 704.5b loss first, as gorge's drawFor does (CR 121.6; gorge rules/replacement.go, effects/cardflow.go). Mornsong Aria."},
	{"stat:CantPreventDamage", "StatCantPreventDamage (Cond2, StFlags)", "Damage can't be prevented while the static functions, printed or as an Effect's emblem (CR 615.12): protection, shield counters, the prevention sentences and keywords and the colour and scope prevention records prevent nothing. StNoPrevCombat (IsCombat$ True): combat damage only, noncombat damage is prevented as usual. A Fog or a prevent-and-mill replacement meeting it stalls (gorge still prevents there). Pyrewood Gearhulk, Impractical Joke, Frenzied Baloth. StNoPrevSpellSelf (EffectZone$ Stack | ValidSource$ Spell.Self, Cond2 the X gate): functions on the stack for the damage its own spell deals while it resolves. Banefire."},
	{"stat:CantPutCounter", "StatCantPutCounter (Filter, A, Cond2)", "No counters of kind A (A < 0: every kind) may be put on a battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) while Cond2 holds (S:Mode$ CantPutCounter, CR 122.1; gorge rules/layers_restrict.go PutCounterBlocked): the placement is swallowed before any AddCounter replacement, so no CounterChange, no CounterAddedOnce trigger and no doubling. The player form (ValidPlayer$) is refused. Blossombind, Blightbeetle, Tatterkite, Melira's Keepers, Darksteel Angel."},
	{"stat:DisableETB", "StatDisableETB (Filter)", "While the static applies, an object matching Filter (S:Mode$ DisableTriggers | ValidMode$ ChangesZone,ChangesZoneAll | Destination$ Battlefield | ValidCause$ F, CR 603.2g) entering the battlefield causes no ability to trigger: the battlefield, graveyard and emblem enters listeners are all skipped. Not when the source has lost its abilities; a batch event with no single object is not suppressed. Gorge: rules/disable_triggers.go disableTriggersExcludes. Torpor Orb, Karn Argent Defender, Doorkeeper Thrull."},
	{"stat:FbGrant", "StatFbGrant (Filter, Cond2, StFbOwnCost GrantCost)", "Each card in its controller's graveyard matching Filter has flashback while Cond2 holds (Condition$ PlayerTurn: their turn), read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card: at the card's mana cost, or GrantCost under StFbOwnCost (CR 702.34a; gorge legal_walk_alt.go flashback walk, cast_altcost.go flashbackCost). Iroh, Grand Lotus."},
	{"stat:WarpGrant", "StatWarpGrant (Filter, GrantCost)", "Each artifact or creature card in its controller's hand matching Filter has warp at GrantCost, read live from the battlefield, never stamped on the card (CR 702.185a; gorge rules warp_grant.go grantedWarpCosts): the hand offers each warp instance gorge does not drop as dominated (the printed one first, then the grant's; AltCostIndex rides the action target), a grant-cost cast marks its entry trigPlWarpG for the cost builder, and the end-step exile and the recast from exile run as for printed warp. Tannuk, Steadfast Second."},
	{"stat:BeamGrant", "StatBeamGrant (the granter's FbCost the return)", "During its controller's main phase each instant and sorcery card in their graveyard has beam me up at its mana cost (gorge beamMeUpInstances)."},
	{"stat:CantBeBeamedUp", "StatCantBeBeamedUp (Filter)", "Permanents matching Filter can't be returned to pay beam me up (gorge matchesBeamReturn)."},
	{"stat:CantBeCast", "StatCantBeCast (Filter, StFlags, Cond2)", "Spells matching Filter can't be cast (gorge castRestricted): StRaiseYou only by the controller, StRaiseOpp only by its opponents (Caster$), under Cond2 (Condition$ PlayerTurn: the controller's turn). The hand, flashback, play-permission and free-cast offers are withheld. Dragonlord Dromoka. A self static (Zone = Command; ValidCard$ Card.Self | EffectZone$ All) binds only the card itself, in any zone, with its owner as \"you\"; StCasterActive: only while the caster is the active player (Caster$ Player.Active). Jace Reawakened, Proft. A > 0: NumLimitEachTurn$ A, the static binds only once the caster has cast A spells this turn (unfiltered ValidCard$ only; gorge castLimitBinds). High Noon. B&CantCastNamed (ValidCard$ Card.NamedCard beside an as-enters NameCard): only a spell whose card is the source's chosen name (ExtChooseName); Alhammarret, High Arbiter."},
	{"stat:Goad", "StatGoad (Filter, Cond2)", "Creatures matching Filter are goaded while the static applies (a Continuous static's Goad$ True beside its pump, CR 701.15b; gorge's static goad route): they attack each combat if able and attack a player rather than a planeswalker or battle (act_goad.go goadedAt). Koloth, Tribble Hunter."},
	{"stat:CantTarget", "StatCantTarget (Filter, Filter2, StFlags, A, Cond2)", "A battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source as Self) can't be the target of a spell or ability whose source matches Filter2 (0 = any; the spell card, or the permanent that has the ability), whose kind is in A (CantTgtSpell, CantTgtActivated, CantTgtTriggered; 0 = every kind) and whose controller StFlags names (StRaiseOpp the static controller's opponents, StRaiseYou the controller) (S:Mode$ CantTarget, CR 115.4; gorge cantTargetBlocks). Read at the target offer, the feasibility probe and the resolution recheck (tgt_canttarget.go). Species 8472, Thrun, Breaker of Silence."},
	{"stat:AnyTypeCreatures", "StatAnyTypeCreatures (no operands)", "Its controller may spend mana as though it were mana of any type to cast creature spells (S:Mode$ ManaConvert | ValidPlayer$ You | ValidCard$ Creature.YouCtrl | ValidSA$ Spell | ManaConversion$ AnyType->AnyType; CR 609.4b; gorge rules/mana_convert.go manaConversionParts): a creature spell's pips take any mana, exact colours first. Vizier of the Menagerie."},
	{"stat:CantPhaseIn", "StatCantPhaseIn (no operands)", "While its source is on the battlefield and keeps its abilities, no permanent phases in (S:Mode$ CantPhaseIn | ValidCard$ Card.phasedOutPermanent, CR 702.26; gorge rules/cantphase.go phaseBlocked): the untap step's phase-in scan skips every phased-out permanent, indirect ones included, since they phase in with their host. Only the blanket ValidCard$ is lowered. The City on the Edge of Forever's Human token."},
	{"stat:CantSacrifice", "StatCantSacrifice (Filter)", "No battlefield permanent matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\") can be sacrificed, for a cost or by an effect (S:Mode$ CantSacrifice, CR 701.21a; gorge rules/layers_restrict.go sacrificeBlocked): it is no sacrifice candidate, a self-sacrifice cost of it can't be paid, a mana ability that sacrifices it is no mana source, and a delayed or Saga sacrifice leaves it. ValidCause$ and ForCost$ lines are refused. Quark, Humble Proprietor."},
	{"stat:CantActivate", "StatCantActivate (Filter, StFlags, Cond2, A)", "Activated abilities of battlefield permanents matching Filter (read with the static's controller as \"you\" and its source's host as EnchantedBy) can't be activated (S:Mode$ CantBeActivated, CR 602.5; gorge abilityRestricted): StRaiseOpp only by the controller's opponents, StRaiseYou only by the controller (Activator$), under Cond2 (Condition$ PlayerTurn). A = 1 (ValidSA$ Activated.!ManaAbility) spares mana abilities; A = 2 (ValidSA$ Activated.Loyalty) reaches loyalty abilities only (The Immortal Sun); otherwise a matching mana source is no mana source in the planner. Clarion Conqueror, Grand Abolisher, Petrify."},
	{"stat:Override", "StatOverride (Filter, Override)", "Objects matching Filter (Witness Protection / Imprisoned in the Moon: the enchanted creature) get `Table.Overrides[Override-1]` while the static applies (see OpOverride for the order). An override with RemoveCreatureSub (RemoveCreatureTypes$ without RemoveCardTypes$: Noggle the Mind, Honest Work) first drops the creature subtypes (genPrep.creatSub) and the all-creature-types mark, keeps the rest, then adds AddSub (gorge applyTypeEffect). A HasTypes or HasSub replacement leaves KeepTypes and KeepSub, the subtypes of a card type the effect adds (CR 205.1a; RemoveCardTypes$ with AddType$ Land leaves a land's land types, which grant no mana ability back: the ability is the card's, and LoseAbilities still takes it)."},
	{"repl:EntersProgram", "ReplEntersProgram (Prog, Cond)", "As this object enters the battlefield (CR 614.1c/614.12), if Cond holds, run the ability's program: OpEnterTapped / OpEnterWithCounters / OpChooseColor / OpChooseType (the choice is stored on the permanent: F2ChosenColor/F2ChosenType, AfManaChosen)."},
	{"repl:OthersEnterProgram", "ReplOthersEnterProgram (Filter, Prog)", "While the source is on the battlefield: as another object matching Filter enters, run the program on it (RefReplaced). Authority of the Consuls (opponents' creatures enter tapped), Giada (other Angels enter with extra +1/+1 counters)."},
	{"repl:TurnUpProgram", "ReplTurnUpProgram (Prog)", "As this face-down permanent is turned face up (CR 702.37e/702.168c, R:Event$ TurnFaceUp ValidCard$ Card.Self), after the cost is paid and before it turns up, run the program on it (RefReplaced: one PutCounter, the count read as it is turned up). gorge applyTurnFaceUpReplacements runs the body before the turn-up event folds; the permanent still holds its face-down characteristics. Bubble Smuggler, Crowd-Control Warden."},
	{"repl:SpellsCantBeCountered", "ReplSpellsCantBeCountered (Filter)", "While the source is on the battlefield, a spell its controller controls that matches Filter (the spell's type words; YouCtrl is structural: the spell's controller is the source's) can't be countered (Layer$ CantHappen, no ReplaceWith$): gorge counterReplacementMatchesAll stops the Counter effect's event, so OpCounter skips it and the spell stays on the stack. Ward, bounce and fizzling are not Counter events. Chimil, the Inner Sun, Sphinx of the Final Word."},
	{"repl:CantTurnUp", "ReplCantTurnUp (Filter, Cond)", "While the source is on the battlefield and Cond holds (PlayerTurn$ True: the source's controller is the active player), a permanent matching Filter (read in the source's frame: OppCtrl, EnchantedBy) can't be turned face up (Layer$ CantHappen, CR 614.17a): gorge turnFaceUpCantHappen makes the special action illegal, so it is never offered and nothing is paid. Karlov Watchdog, Unable to Scream."},
	{"repl:OnePoison", "ReplOnePoison", "If the controller would get one or more poison counters, they get one instead and can't get additional poison counters this turn (gorge's ReplaceCounter Amount$ 1 then an ImmediateTrigger's CantPutCounter POISON Effect). Melira, the Living Cure."},
	{"repl:DoubleCountersYou", "ReplDoubleCountersYou (Cond)", "While Cond holds (a Class's ClassBand$ level), counters the controller would put on a permanent or player are doubled. The putter is gorge's in-flight counter adder: the entrant's controller for entry counters, the Saga's controller for its turn-based lore counter, the damage source's controller for infect -1/-1 counters and poison, else the resolving (or paying) entry's controller; none known: not doubled. Innkeeper's Talent."},
	{"repl:DrawMore", "ReplDrawMore (A cards, C&ReplDrawNotFirst, Cond)", "If the controller would draw a card, they draw A cards instead (R:Event$ Draw | ReplaceWith$ DB$ Draw | Defined$ You | NumCards$ A); C&1 exempts the first card of their own draw step (NotFirstCardInDrawStep$ True); Cond is a granted max-speed gate. Only a draw that takes a card from a non-empty library is replaced. The A draws are new draws that meet every draw replacement but the ones already applied to the lineage (CR 614.5, gorge replDrawChain); two matching one draw stall (StallDrawRepl: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order). Mr. Spock, Alhammarret's Archive, Bard, Vnwxt."},
	{"repl:RewriteTokens", "ReplRewriteTokens (C pool token index; remapped per matchup)", "While the source is on the battlefield, every token its controller would create is the token of card C instead, the same number (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidToken$ Permanent.YouCtrl | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ ReplaceToken | TokenScript$; gorge applyTokenReplacementToPlan, mint by mint, CR 614.1a). The CreateToken ops and the mint sites that make the card they were given (amass, incubate, empower, endure, recruit, the copy sites) read it (replTokensCard); a Role mint (TokAttach: gorge mints the rewriter's card as a plain script mint, no host sought) stalls (StallTokRewrite). A second matching token replacement of the same token, a multiplier or another rewriter, is gorge's CR 616.1 order ask: a CreateToken op poses it token by token to the creator (repl_tokorder.go), the other mint sites stall on it (StallTokRewrite). Holo-Engineer."},
	{"repl:CantLoseGame", "ReplCantLoseGame", "The controller can't lose the game (SBA losses and 'loses the game' effects do nothing). C == kop.CantLoseLife stops only the loss for 0 or less life (poison, an empty-library draw and 'loses the game' effects still lose). Herald of Eternal Dawn, Georgiou, Terran Emperor."},
	{"repl:OppsCantWinGame", "ReplOppsCantWinGame", "The controller's opponents can't win the game. Herald of Eternal Dawn."},
	{"stat:ReduceAbility", "StatReduceAbility (Filter, A/VA, B, Cond2)", "Activated abilities of battlefield permanents matching Filter (controlled by the static's controller) cost A (VA when dynamic) generic less, floored at zero after each static, after the ability's own ReduceCost$ (CR 601.2f, 602.2b; gorge costModifiersCompose). B bit 0: Exhaust abilities only. B bit 2 (kop.ReduceAbPowerUp): Power-up abilities only (Hulk, Gamma Goliath's ValidSpell$ Activated.PowerUp; a Power-up ability is matched by kop.CostPowerUp). B bit 3 (kop.ReduceAbEquip): Equip abilities only (kop.AfEquip; ValidSpell$ Activated.Equip: Auriok Steelshaper), and with StTargetsFilter2 only an equip whose target matches Filter2 read with the static's source as Self (Cloud, Planet's Champion's ValidTarget$ Card.Self): the offer prices the cheapest legal target, the CR 601.2c target menu keeps the candidates whose own price is payable, the charge prices the chosen target. B bits 4..7: the MinMana$ floor (gorge pay.ApplyTo: caps this reduction at min(floor, the cost's mana before it), never raises; Agatha of the Vile Cauldron, Forensic Gadgeteer). Priced at the battlefield offer and the activation charge (kernel abReduced); B bit 1 (kop.ReduceAbUnlock) is Inquisitive Glimmer's ValidSpell$ Static.Unlock arm instead: the same static lowers the Room unlock special action's generic cost at the offer and the charge (kernel unlockReduced, CR 601.2f); a mana ability is an activated ability, so a filter land's fee is priced after the reduction (filtFee; a fee taken to nothing makes the source's own gated-choice view, mana_filterfree.go), while any other mana ability with a mana cost the reduction would lower is not priced and a matchup holding one refuses (cardset.AbReduceRefusal: a MinMana$ floor at the cost, or a filter naming no type the card has, lowers nothing). Mutagen Man, Blossoming Tortoise, Boom Scholar."},
	{"stat:PlayerHexproof", "StatPlayerHexproof", "The controller has hexproof: spells and abilities its opponents control can't target that player (CR 702.11b). A == 1 also protects it from damage dealt by its opponents' sources (protection from each opponent, CR 702.16; Absolute Virtue). Crystal Barricade."},
	{"stat:CanAttackDefender", "StatCanAttackDefender (Filter), under Cond", "A Defender creature matching Filter (the card itself, or a ValidCard$ over its controller's creatures such as Ghalta the Immovable) can attack as though it didn't have defender while the static's Cond holds (CR 702.3b; gorge combat.AttackAllowedThroughDefender; the condition is the shared Condition$/CheckSVar$/IsPresent$ gate). Mechan Shieldmate, Shipwreck Sentry, Demon Wall, Bristlepack Sentry, Platypus-Bear, Ghalta the Immovable. The Effect-delivered form and ValidAttacked$ stay refused."},
	{"stat:Panharmonicon", "StatPanharmonicon (Filter)", "A triggered ability of a printed, non-granted trigger line whose source object matches Filter (relative to the static's controller; Other is relative to the static's own permanent) triggers an additional time: one extra pending placement per matching live static, queued right after the original (CR 603.2d; gorge panharmoniconEchoes). A granted trigger and a copy of the placement are not doubled. A == PanhModeLifeGained or PanhModeDrawn (ValidMode$ LifeGained or Drawn alone) echoes only a trigger of that player event, whose player must match B (a Whose, ValidPlayer$) relative to the static's controller (Dr. Beverly Crusher). Delney, Streetwise Lookout; Twinflame Travelers."},
	{"stat:HexproofOwnColors", "StatHexproofOwnColors (Filter)", "The objects matching Filter have hexproof from each of their own CURRENT colours (CR 702.11d; a Continuous static's AddKeyword$ Hexproof:CardColors, the one Affected$ shape Creature.Other+YouCtrl). A layer-6 grant: it does not survive a later loss of the recipient's abilities. The target's colours are read live, so a colour-changing effect makes it hexproof from every colour it has then; a colourless source is never stopped. Tam, Mindful First-Year."},
	{"stat:StackKw", "StatStackKw (Filter, A = keyword code: 1 Improvise, 2 Casualty, 3 Cascade, 4 Lifelink, 5 Storm, 6 Split second, 7 Convoke, 8 Conspire, 9 Delve; B = casualty threshold; Zone = ZoneHand for wasCastFromYourHand)", "The spells the static's controller casts that match Filter carry a keyword for the cast-time readers (AffectedZone$ Stack AddKeyword$ Cascade, Improvise, Casualty:<n>; gorge keywordmay.go stackKeywordPossibleH): one more cascade trigger per granting static, live at the moment the cast trigger queues; a granted Improvise reads wherever the printed Convoke/Improvise does (kernel tapPays / isImprovise), a granted Casualty:<n> wherever the printed one does (kernel casualtyN); all through kernel stackKwN (a carrier spell still on the stack grants too, gorge stackSelfStaticOK). a granted Lifelink is read at damage time off the resolving spell (kernel srcKw, stackLifelinkKw). Affinity grants lower to an ordinary ReduceCost instead. Quandrix, the Proof; Sami, Wildcat Captain and Witherbloom, the Balancer (affinity); Ironheart, Clever Champion and Inspiring Statuary (improvise); Chief Engineer, We Ride at Dawn and Invasion of Segovia (convoke: a granted Convoke reads the same paths as the printed one, kernel tapPays; a spell with both Convoke and Improvise, or an {X} cost, poses gorge's one mixed announcement, kernel convokeOptions; only a Harmonize or alternative-cost route stalls unmodelled, StallStackKwGrant); Silverquill, the Disputant (casualty); Heartflame Duelist and Lo and Li, Twin Tutors (lifelink); Prismari, the Inspiration and the Ral, Crackling Wit emblem (storm: a kernel-native cast trigger, one per spell however many statics grant it, copying the spell once per spell cast before it this turn by either player, new targets allowed; kernel queueStorm); Raiding Schemes (conspire: a conspired cast, AkCastConspire, offered beside the plain cast at no extra mana while two untapped creatures share a colour with the spell; it taps two of them (ChGenConspire, forced with exactly two) and queues one copy trigger per paid cast however many statics grant it (an unpaid cast queues nothing, matching the printed CheckSVar$ Count$Conspired gate), new targets allowed; kernel kw_conspire.go); Teval, Arbiter of Virtue (delve: the cast is offered on its graveyard credit, min(generic, graveyard size), and announces graveyard cards to exile after X, one pick at a time; the cards move to exile once the mana is paid; kernel kw_delve.go; the printed keyword lowers too)."},
	{"stat:Control", "StatControl (Filter)", "The source's controller controls the permanent the source is attached to while Filter matches it (an Aura's \"You control enchanted creature\", CR 613.1b): the state-based check registers a control record when the static applies and the controller differs, and ends it when the static stops applying (source gone, lost its abilities, moved, or changed controller), as gorge's reconcileControlStatics. Control Magic, Mind Control, Kitnap."},
	{"repl:DoubleDamageToOpps", "ReplDoubleDamageToOpps", "Damage a source the controller controls would deal to an opponent or a permanent an opponent controls is doubled, once per such permanent (CR 614.1a). Applies at every damage site (spell, fight, divided, combat) before prevention. Twinflame Tyrant. With Repl.Filter/Repl.C set (kop.ReplDmg* bits, ReplDmgSrcInPlay): only a source matching Filter its controller controls, to a recipient in C (Gratuitous Violence, Neriv, Trance Kuja; dirac/repl_multipliers.go)."},
	{"repl:DamagePlus", "ReplDamagePlus (Filter source, A plus, C recipients)", "Damage a source matching `Filter` (relative to the replacement's controller) would deal to a recipient in `C` (ReplDmgOppPlayer / OppPerm / Player / Perm, ReplDmgNonCombat) is that much plus `A` instead (ReplaceCount$DamageAmount/Plus.N). Applies at every damage site before doubling. With another damage replacement matching the same event gorge asks for their order (CR 616.1), which changes the amount: the kernel stalls (StallReplPlus). Valley Flamecaller. ReplDmgRaise (C): instead of adding, damage below the host's current power becomes that power (DamageAmount$ LTX, VarValue$ Count$CardPower; a candidate only while below it): Ojer Axonil. ReplDmgCtrHost: Repl.A is a counter kind on the host, its live count added (Fated Firepower). ReplDmgPowHost: the host's live power added (Count$CardPower; a negative power stalls StallReplPlus): Hawkeye, Young Avenger. A nonzero Repl.Cond gates the replacement on its host (a max-speed grant, the controller's speed >= 4: Far Fortune, End Boss). A pure plus-N competition (two or more on one event, no other damage replacement kind) poses gorge's no-op CR 616.1 order ask at the dealHits batch and the direct replDamage sites (OpDealDamageFrom's player mode, OpResolveDamageMap, a one-target divided batch): the op parks and the answer re-executes it with the additions summed; more than one competing event in one pass, or a noncommuting candidate (a raise, a doubling, a prevention), still stalls (StallReplPlus; a dealHits batch with two competing hits, or a competing hit after an earlier one, is the named capacity StallReplPlusBatch)."},
	{"repl:PreventNoncombatToOthers", "ReplPreventNoncombatToOthers", "Noncombat damage that would be dealt to another creature the controller controls is prevented (CR 615): no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger for it. Applied after the amount replacements (the fixed order). Crystal Barricade."},
	{"repl:AddToken", "ReplAddToken (C pool token index, remapped per matchup; Filter the tokens it matches)", "While the source is on the battlefield, a creation of one or more tokens matching Filter under its controller's control also creates one token of card C, once per creation event: a CreateToken op makes it after the op's own tokens, plain and untapped (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidPlayer$ You | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ AddToken | Amount$ 1 | TokenScript$; gorge applyTokenReplacementToPlan, a fixed Amount$ block claimed once per Token resolution). An adder beside another matching token replacement (gorge's CR 616.1 order ask), a CreateToken op with riders (tapped, remembered, attached...) and every other mint site (amass, incubate, the copy sites...) stall (StallTokRewrite). Worldwalker Helm."},
	{"repl:CopyFirstToken", "ReplCopyFirstToken (Cond: no token its controller owns has entered this turn)", "While the source is attached to a permanent and no token its controller owns has entered the battlefield this turn (Repl.Cond, gorge's per-add zone-entry list), the controller's creation of a token may instead make it a copy of that permanent: an election, decline first (R:Event$ CreateToken | ValidPlayer$ You | Optional$ True | Layer$ Copy | CheckSVar$ X | SVarCompare$ EQ0 | ReplaceWith$ DB$ ReplaceToken | Type$ ReplaceToken | ValidChoices$ Card.EquippedBy or Card.EnchantedBy | TokenScript$ Chosen; gorge poseChosenTokenReplacement). gorge asks per token, so the first token of a creation is the one the election covers and the gate closes behind it. A plain CreateToken op asks and makes the copy as an untapped, non-attacking token (copyTokenEnterFrom); the ops with riders, every other mint site (amass, incubate, the copy sites...), a second matching token replacement (gorge's CR 616.1 order ask), a copy of an Aura, a face-down or as-enters-choice permanent stall (StallTokRewrite). Mirrormind Crown, Moonlit Meditation."},
	{"repl:PreventMillOpps", "ReplPreventMillOpps", "Damage a source the controller controls would deal to an opponent is prevented and that opponent mills that many cards instead, once per damage event (combat: once per attacker), at the point the damage would be dealt: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger. Beside a damage doubler, a plus-N or a colour prevention gorge asks the CR 616.1 order, which changes the mill: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus). The Mindskinner."},
	{"repl:PreventDamageCounters", "ReplPreventDamageCounters", "Damage that would be dealt to this permanent is prevented and that many +1/+1 counters are put on it instead (the counter replacements apply to the placement), once per damage event (combat: once per source), after protection: no damage, no lifelink, no damage trigger. Under a can't-prevent static the counters are put and the damage is dealt (CR 615.12). Beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus). Anti-Venom, Horrifying Healer."},
	{"repl:DamageHealFirst", "ReplDamageHealFirst", "Damage that would be dealt to this permanent is dealt, but the damage already marked on it (and its deathtouch mark) is healed first, once per damage event: lifelink and damage triggers see the damage. A second combat damage event to it in one pass (it would heal the first) stalls (StallReplPlus); beside another damage replacement gorge asks the CR 616.1 order: the pair is refused (StallReplPlus). Wolverine, Fierce Fighter."},
	{"repl:DoubleTokens", "ReplDoubleTokens", "An effect that would create tokens under the controller's control creates twice that many, once per such permanent. Doubling Season. Repl.A > 2 multiplies by A instead (Ojer Taq: 3); Repl.Filter restricts it to the tokens matching it (Ojer Taq: creature tokens)."},
	{"repl:DoubleCounters", "ReplDoubleCounters", "An effect that would put counters on a permanent the controller controls puts twice that many, once per such permanent; counters put as a cost are not doubled (EffectOnly). Doubling Season."},
	{"repl:GraveToLibrary", "ReplGraveToLibrary", "Works from every zone: if this card would be put into a graveyard from anywhere it is put into its owner's library instead and that library is shuffled (no dies trigger: it never reaches the graveyard). Progenitus."},
	{"repl:PayBeforeETB", "ReplPayBeforeETB (Prog)", "This permanent spell would enter: its controller may discard a land card from their hand instead (an optional discard, run as the spell resolves, the discarded card remembered); if they did the card enters the battlefield, otherwise it goes to its owner's graveyard (Mox Diamond; gorge's Moved replacement chain of Discard, two ChangeZone and Cleanup). The card entering by any route but its cast resolution stalls (StallPayETB)."},
	{"repl:DiscardOppToBattlefield", "ReplDiscardOppToBattlefield", "This card in its owner's hand, discarded by a spell or ability an opponent of the owner controls, enters the battlefield under its owner's control instead of going to the graveyard. Cost discards (cycling, Discard<> costs), cleanup discards and the owner's own effects keep the graveyard. Wilt-Leaf Liege, Obstinate Baloth, Loxodon Smiter."},
	{"repl:ExileOnLeave", "ReplExileOnLeave (Filter, C)", "A permanent matching `Filter` that would be put into a graveyard from the battlefield is exiled instead (no dies trigger; leaves triggers still fire). C = 1: from every zone, so a card matching `Filter` moving to a graveyard from the stack (a resolved or countered spell), hand (discard), library (mill) or exile goes to exile instead and no graveyard trigger fires for it (Rest in Peace, Leyline of the Void, Dryad Militant). Two matching sources, or one beside Progenitus's redirect, pose gorge's CR 616.1 order ask: the kernel stalls (StallReplLeave)."},
	// --- preds / keywords / counters / costs ---
	{"pred:CMCEQ", "PredCMCEQ (PredN)", "Mana value == PredN."},
	{"pred:CMCLEV", "PredCMCLEV (PredV)", "Mana value <= the value PredV evaluated for the resolving ability (Alesha: its power; Fiendish Panda: the dead Panda's power; Genesis Wave / Fiend Artisan: X; Loot: lands you control); == it when PredN is 1 (Repurposing Bay: the sacrificed artifact's mana value plus 1)."},
	{"pred:CountersGE", "PredCountersGE (PredN = n<<8 | kind)", "At least n counters of the kind."},
	{"pred:ToughnessGE", "PredToughnessGE (PredN)", "Toughness >= PredN (current on the battlefield; printed or CDA off it). Gorge `toughnessGE<n>`. Repel Calamity."},
	{"pred:HasXCost", "PredHasXCost", "The printed mana cost has {X}. Gorge `hasXCost` (effects/filter.go). Helga's mana restriction."},
	{"pred:PowerLTToughness", "PredPowerLTToughness", "Power < toughness. Gorge `powerLTtoughness`. Fecund Greenshell."},
	{"pred:MultiColor", "PredMultiColor", "Two or more colours (current on the battlefield, printed off it). Gorge `wordMultiColor`."},
	{"pred:TypesAllCMCLE", "PredTypesAllCMCLE (PredN = the conjunction, PredV = the constant mana-value bound)", "Has every card type in PredN and a mana value at most PredV.N: kgen's cmcLE/cmcLT beside an all-of type conjunction, LT lowering the bound by one. The battlefield arm reads the derived types and the current mana value; the card arm the printed types and mana value (a split card off the stack sums its halves, CR 709.4b; a face-down card has none, CR 708.4). Resistance Is Futile."},
	{"pred:Historic", "PredHistoric (PredN = Saga subtype index+1)", "Artifact, legendary or Saga. Gorge `historicMatches`."},
	{"pred:Equipped", "PredEquipped", "A battlefield permanent with an Equipment attached. Gorge `equipped` (hasAttachmentOfKind)."},
	{"pred:Modified", "PredModified", "Modified (CR 700.9): a battlefield permanent with one or more counters (any kind the kernel stores as a counter: CtrLevel is a Class's level, not a counter; the regeneration shield and the deathtouch mark are flags), an Equipment attached, or an Aura its controller controls attached. Off the battlefield nothing is modified. Gorge `modifiedPermanent` (the internal Shield/Deathtouched markers excluded). Orochi Merge-Keeper, Kami's Flare, Ambitious Assault."},
	{"pred:Monstrous", "PredMonstrous", "IsMonstrous: the battlefield permanent's CR 701.37b monstrous designation (gorge wordIsMonstrous, Object.Monstrous). Off the battlefield nothing matches. Fleecemane Lion, Hundred-Handed One."},
	{"pred:NoCounters", "PredNoCounters", "!HasCounters: a battlefield permanent with no counter of any kind (PredHasCounters negated: the regeneration shield and the deathtouch mark count as counters, as gorge stores them). Off the battlefield every card matches (gorge's '!' over hasCounters of a card with none). Unstoppable Slasher's dies trigger."},
	{"pred:LacksKeyword", "PredLacksKeyword (N)", "!with<Keyword>: the object does not have keyword bit N (PredHasKeyword negated; gorge's '!' over objectHasKeyword). Surge Engine."},
	{"pred:Outlaw", "PredOutlaw (N)", "Outlaw: the object has one of the creature types Assassin, Mercenary, Pirate, Rogue, Warlock (gorge outlawMatches, the layer-aware type read; a changeling has them all). N = 1 negates (!Outlaw). Shoot the Sheriff."},
	{"pred:SameNameT0", "PredSameNameT0", "The resolving ability's target 0 or an object sharing its name, lowered whole. On the battlefield: a permanent, the target still there at its chosen version (a face-down permanent has no name, CR 708.2): gorge's \"TargetedCard.Self,Permanent.NotDefinedTargeted+sharesNameWith Targeted\" (Maelstrom Pulse). Off it: a card, the target a graveyard card legal as the resolution started, matched by name even after the sweep has moved it (gorge's referent keeps its ObjID): ChangeZoneAll Origin$ Graveyard Defined$ You \"TargetedCard.Self,Card.NotDefinedTargeted+sharesNameWith Targeted\" as a Card.YouOwn clause (Rat King, Verminister)."},
	{"pred:ToughnessLEV", "PredToughnessLEV (PredV)", "A battlefield permanent whose current toughness (layers applied) is <= the value PredV evaluated for the resolving ability. Gorge `toughnessLE<X>` / `toughnessLT<X>` (LT lowers the bound by one). Zero Point Ballad's \"creatures with toughness X or less\". PredN 3: toughness >= PredV, a toughness > a value lowered as >= value+1 (a battlefield permanent's, or off the battlefield the printed toughness, a face-down card a 2/2, or a departed trigger object's last known toughness): Hulkling, Burgeoning Bruiser's toughnessGTZ."},
	{"pred:CountersLT", "PredCountersLT (PredN = n<<8 | kind)", "Fewer than n counters of the kind (gorge counters_LTn / LE(n-1) / EQ0); off the battlefield every card has none. Reckoner Bankbuster's \"if there are no charge counters\"."},
	{"pred:TotalPT", "PredTotalPT (PredN = DmgGate(cmp, n))", "A battlefield permanent whose current power plus toughness passes the comparison (gorge totalPT_<cmp><n>, cr-totalpt-filter). Cut Down."},
	{"pred:TriggerObj", "PredTriggerObj", "The resolving trigger's object, wherever it is now (gorge TriggerContext.TriggeredCards, bound from the firing event's ID list; the kernel entry's trigObj): ChooseFromDefined$ TriggeredCards' pool membership. The ManifestDread marker's milled card; the one-card window's empty marker matches nothing. Paranormal Analyst."},
	{"pred:ExiledWith", "PredExiledWith (PredN 0 filter / 1 Defined$)", "ExiledWithSource: the card was exiled with the resolving entry's source (gorge exiledBySourceAt): the reverse link Object.ExiledWith held live for the source's incarnation (the same ver; one ver on once the source has left the battlefield; PredN 1, a resolving trigger's fire ver), or the forward ExiledCards entry a ChangeZone / ChangeZoneAll / search exile writes (cleared when the source enters other than from the stack). genState.exw records them for a CardDef.ExiledWith card's resolutions only (a cost exile carries no source). Read in resolution-time movers, and by a printed Mode$ Continuous static as the FExiledWith filter flag, which takes the static's own object as the source: Keen-Eyed Curator, Dawnhand Dissident, Maralen. A target, a cost, an emblem/Effect static or a granted ability is refused. Ghost Vacuum, Northampton Farm, The Princess Takes Flight."},
	{"pred:WasCastEnter", "PredWasCastEnter (PredN 0 wasCast / 1 wasCastFromGraveyard / 2 wasCastFromYourHandByYou / 3 wasCastFromYourGraveyard / 8 CastSa Spell.ManaSpent EQ0 / 16 webSlinged, +4 negated)", "The permanent entering is the spell resolving right now, read inside the enter (gorge WasCast / ObjectWasCastFromGraveyard; a copy and any other arrival read not cast, CR 707.10): s.res.e is the provenance record, its cast zone in stackEntry.prov (genPrep.anyCastProv). Lowered only in a battlefield-entering ChangesZone / ChangesZoneAll ValidCard(s)$ (wasCast, !wasCast, wasCastFromGraveyard, wasCastFromYourGraveyard) and in a self enters replacement's CheckSVar$ Count$wasCastFromYourHandByYou.1.0. Doomsday Excruciator, Patched Plaything, Myojin of Night's Reach, Twilight Diviner, Satoru, the Infiltrator, Rocket-Powered Goblin Glider. adds bit 8, CastSa Spell.ManaSpent EQ0: the entering object was the resolving spell and its recorded total spend is 0 (gorge castSaTokenHolds, tag -1; a cheated-in object has no cast window and reads false; spentOfSpell, prep keeps the spend: anySpent/anyHist). Satoru, the Infiltrator's second alternative. Bit 16, webSlinged: the resolving spell entry carries the web-slinging mark (trigPl == trigPlWebSling, kw_websling.go; a stack copy's is cleared, CR 707.10; gorge webSlingedAdmits); refused on a spell and outside a battlefield-entering trigger. Spiders-Man, Heroic Horde."},
	{"pred:WasCastSpell", "PredWasCastSpell (PredN 0 wasCast / 1 wasCastFromYourHand / 2 wasCastFromYourHandByYou / 3 wasCastFromExile / 4 wasCast+!wasCastFromYourHand / 5 CastSa Spell.MayPlaySource / 6 CastSa Spell.Mayhem, +16 negated)", "The spell on the stack, or resolving right now, was cast from the origin (gorge WasCast / WasCastFromHand / WasCastFromHandByYou / WasCastFromExile; a stack copy was never cast, CR 707.10, so a negated read holds for it): its stack entry is the provenance record, the cast zone in stackEntry.prov (genPrep.anyCastProv). The bare wasCastFromYourHand is a hand cast by any caster, ByYou adds the reading player as the caster. Lowered only in a SpellCast ValidCard$ and in a spell ability's ConditionDefined$ Self + ConditionPresent$ (the condition is matched on the spell, ZoneStack); a mana ability's Spell.<word> spend restriction (Mm'menon's granted !wasCastFromYourHand; read with the cast's origin, kernel cast_wascastrestrict.go: an offer reads the object's current zone and the hand family denies, the payment reads the pushed entry) lowers too, and a CantBeCast ValidCard$ lowers the hand (1), exile (3) and cast-not-from-hand (4) families, wasCastFromTheirHand included as the same predicate as wasCastFromYourHand (gorge: a cast from a hand, any caster): the cast offer has no stack entry, so the kernel reads the candidate's current zone as the origin (matchSpellCardOffer, cast_cantbecastorigin.go; ByYou, MayPlaySource, Mayhem and bare wasCast refuse there). Any other filter refuses. Avatar's Wrath, Drannith Magistrate. Vega the Watcher, Keeper of Secrets, Memory Worm, Kami of Celebration, Otterball Antics, Antiquities on the Loose; Mm'menon, the Right Hand. adds code 6, CastSa Spell.Mayhem and its !CastSa Spell.Mayhem: the spell entry was cast for its mayhem cost (stackEntry.trigPl == trigPlMayhem; gorge FlagMayhem, a stack copy reads false). Sandman's Quicksand's two PumpAll conditions."},
	{"pred:TrigPlayerCtrl", "PredTrigPlayerCtrl", "A battlefield permanent controlled by the current trigger entry's trigger player: the player a damage trigger's damage was dealt to, at any seat count (gorge ControlledBy TriggeredTarget, read at targeting and rechecked on resolution, CR 608.2b); false off the battlefield or with no trigger entry. Trygon Predator, Dreadmaw's Ire."},
	{"pred:Suspected", "PredSuspected (PredN 1 / 0)", "PredN 1: a suspected battlefield permanent; PredN 0: anything not suspected, off the battlefield too (gorge IsSuspected / !IsSuspected: Object.Suspected, false off the battlefield). The designation is the arena bit mechSuspected set by OpExt ExtSuspect. adds the sacrifice-time snapshot: lkiRec.bits bit 1 keeps the designation a sacrificed cost object had, and the exact Sacrificed$Valid Card.IsSuspected head reads it (Agency Coroner). Clandestine Meddler, Deadly Complication, Rubblebelt Braggart."},
	{"f2:CrewedSrc", "FilterFlags2 F2CrewedSrc (CrewedThisTurn / SaddledThisTurn, and Count$CrewSize)", "The candidate crewed (or saddled) the filter's source this turn: the source-mark record noteCrew writes when a Crew/Saddle pick taps it (gorge CrewedVehicles/CrewedTurn, foldCrew); the mark ends as the turn begins or the crewer leaves (CR 702.122). lowers Count$CrewSize (gorge count_body_simple.go evalCountBodyCostCrewSize) to the ordinary battlefield Count$Valid over Creature+F2CrewedSrc relative to the source, so a permanent's attack trigger counts its crewers. A card whose ability reads the word records its crews (genPrep.crewBy, through an instruction filter or a ValueRef expression). Leisure Bicycle, Subterranean Schooner, Luxurious Locomotive."},
	{"pred:Solved", "PredSolved (PredN 1 / 0)", "PredN 1: a battlefield permanent that is a solved Case; PredN 0: anything not solved, off the battlefield too (gorge IsSolved / !IsSolved: Object.Solved, CR 719.3b). The designation is OpSaddle with C = 1 (AlterAttribute Solved), the saddled bit, never cleared as a turn begins. Activation$ Solved reads it on the source. Case of the Crimson Pulse."},
	{"pred:PermMark", "PredPermMark (PredN: mark 0-3 | 16 negated)", "attackedThisTurn (0: declared an attacker this turn, not a creature put onto the battlefield attacking), dealtDamageThisTurn (1: the permanent as SOURCE dealt damage this turn, after prevention, to anything), dealtDamagetoAny (2) and dealtCombatDamagetoAny (3): the same, game-long since it entered; PredN bit 4 is the ! form. False off the battlefield, so a negated word is true there (gorge AttackedTurn, DamageDealtThisTurn, DealtDamageToAnyGame, DealtCombatDamageToAnyGame). The marks are arena slot bits (mechAttacked, mechDealtTurn, mechDealtAny, mechDealtCombat); the first two end with the turn. The Lunar Whale, Hexhaven Dueling Arena, Treacherous Greed, Red Guardian Super-Soldier, Karakyk Guardian, Ruric Thar the Unbowed."},
	{"pred:FaceDown", "PredFaceDown", "faceDown: a face-down battlefield permanent (CR 708.2; gorge wordFaceDown is Object.FaceDown on the battlefield, so a face-down spell or exile card never matches). Read live by the filter (s.faceDown), also in a ThisTurnEntered count over the entered ring, which reads each entry where it lives now. Cryptid Inspector, Threats Around Every Corner, Tunnel Tipster."},
	{"pred:PowerGTBase", "PredPowerGTBase", "powerGTbasePower: a battlefield permanent whose current power exceeds its base power (layer 7b, before 7c effects and 7d counters; CR 613.4; gorge filter_value.go numericPred). Nothing off the battlefield matches. Kutzil, Malamet Exemplar."},
	{"pred:Word7", "PredWord7 (PredN sub-kind)", "noName (face-down, or a Room with no door unlocked; gorge hasNoName), greatestPower (a battlefield creature no other battlefield creature out-powers, ties match), attackingAlone (attacking, and exactly one attacker), inZone<Z> (the object's current zone). Pompous Gadabout, Getaway Glamer, Crowd of True Believers, Dread Summons, Take It Back. adds six: 5 faceUp (not face down, any zone; gorge wordFaceUp), 6 IsNotChosenType (a chosen type exists and the object lacks it; fails closed with no choice), 7 attacking Opponent (attacking a player other than the evaluating controller; a planeswalker defender matches nothing), 8 EnchantedBy Aura.YouCtrl (an Aura the evaluating controller controls is attached to it), 9 doesNotShareNameWith OtherYourBattlefield (no other permanent its controller controls shares its name), 10 sharesNameWith Valid Permanent.Legendary (another legendary battlefield permanent shares its name; a trailing +YouCtrl is the outer filter's). Oviya Automech Artisan, Archon of the Wild Rose, Yenna Redtooth Regent, Key to the Side-Door, Kindred Judgment. adds 12 greatestPowerControlledByTargeted (a battlefield creature controlled by a player target of the current stack entry that no other such creature out-powers; ties match; no player target matches nothing; gorge controlReferentPlayers Targeted skips object targets) and 13 CrewedBySourceThisTurn (the filter's source crewed the candidate Vehicle this turn, read off the crew source marks reversed; no source matches nothing; the crewer's card records its crews, genPrep.crewerRec); adds 11 withWarp (gorge's printed-keyword read: the card's printed CardDef.HasWarp in any zone, face down or not; a battlefield permanent that is face down or lost all abilities has none; only that spelling, withoutWarp and hasKeywordWarp stay refused); a TgtCard slot whose filter zone is exile walks both players' exile lists in order (State.exileCardCands). Blade of the Swarm. adds 14 NoAbilities (the card's printed face has no keyword, static, replacement, trigger, activated or extra spell ability, CardDef.NoAbilities from gorge FaceHasNoAbilities; read off the battlefield only, where kgen refuses it). Fang-Druid Summoner, Rise from the Wreck. adds 22 withDisguise (the card printed with Disguise, CardDef.MorphFamily, in any zone; a battlefield permanent that is face down or lost all abilities has none; only that spelling, withoutDisguise and hasKeywordDisguise stay refused). 26 withFlashback (the same printed-keyword read for Flashback, CardDef.Keywords&KwFlashback; only that spelling). Sorceress's Schemes. 27 !hasKeywordLandwalk:Island (the permanent has no Landwalk naming Island among the permanent's printed landwalk, unless it lost its abilities, or a Continuous static's granted landwalk; only that spelling). Stormtide Leviathan. 23 is the pair faceUp+withDisguise in one clause (not face down and printed with Disguise). Expose the Culprit. Consumed by Greed, Balthier, Fran and Blade of the Swarm. adds 20, the pair doesNotShareNameWith YourGraveyard+doesNotShareNameWith OtherYourBattlefield in one clause (no other permanent its controller controls and no card in the evaluating controller's graveyard shares its name; Guardian Project). adds 24 ThisTurnEnteredFrom_Battlefield (the card's latest arrival into its current zone came from the battlefield this turn, read off the entered ledger; a table whose filter carries it records the ledger; off the battlefield only, where kgen refuses it on a permanent and every other origin zone). Assimilate the Wounded, Ezri Dax Newly Joined."},
	{"pred:AdventureCard", "PredAdventureCard", "AdventureCard: the object's own card has the Adventure layout (CR 715.1; gorge wordAdventureCard reads the card, not the current face), so it holds in every zone, on the stack as the Adventure half is cast, on an adventure in exile, and for the permanent on the battlefield. A layer-1 copy reads its own card. Beluna Grandsquall, Edgewall Inn, Howling Galefang."},
	{"pred:Blocked", "PredBlocked", "A battlefield permanent that is attacking with a blocker recorded, kept after the blocker leaves combat (pfBlocked; gorge \"blocked\", cr-blocked-filter). Tactical Advantage."},
	{"pred:MonoColor", "PredMonoColor", "MonoColor: exactly one current colour (gorge wordMonoColor; a colourless or face-down object is not monocoloured). Guardian of the Guildpact's protection quality."},
	{"pred:HasCounters", "PredHasCounters", "HasCounters: a battlefield permanent with one or more counters of any kind (CtrLevel is a Class level, not a counter), the regeneration shield and the deathtouch mark included as gorge stores them as Shield/Deathtouched counters. Off the battlefield nothing matches. Gorge `wordHasCounters` (hasCounters, not hasRealCounters) (C8)."},
	{"cost:SubAmong", "CostSubAmong (N, Ctr, Filter)", "Remove N counters of kind Ctr from among the permanents matching Filter the payer controls, one counter per pick (gorge RemoveAnyCounter<N/Kind/Filter>, rules amongCounterAsk: a lone candidate takes the unit unasked); an activated ability's own cost only. Hopeful Initiate."},
	{"trig:Training", "Trigger.N TrigNTraining", "Attacks, the source itself: fires only when it attacks with another attacker of strictly greater power, the whole declaration counted (CR 702.149a; gorge trigmatch AttacksMatches). Hopeful Initiate."},
	{"trig:TeamworkTap", "Trigger.N TrigNTeamworkTap", "Taps, the source itself: fires only for a tap paying a teamwork additional cost (Teamwork$ True; gorge trigmatch/tap.go:41, the tap reason events.TapTeamworkCounter of pay/paidcost.go). Agent Maria Hill."},
	{"trig:GameOnce", "Tf3GameOnce", "A battlefield trigger line that triggers once per source object (GameActivationLimit$ 1; gorge trigger_match.go triggerGameActivationLimitAllows, the count committed as the trigger is queued and reset when the source changes zones, CR 400.7). Acrobatic Cheerleader."},
	{"cost:OncePerTurn", "CostOncePerTurn", "Activate only once each turn (gorge AB ActivationLimit$ 1; printed battlefield abilities with index < 8 only). Hired Claw."},
	{"ab:ActCond", "Ability.Trig.Cond on an AbActivated", "Activate only if the condition holds (CR 602.5b; gorge CheckSVar$/SVarCompare$, IsPresent$/PresentCompare$ on the battlefield, Activation$ Threshold), checked by canActivate; printed battlefield abilities only. Hired Claw, Thought Shucker."},
	{"dig:Tapped", "DigTapped / DuFoundTapped", "A Dig's taken card / a DigUntil's found card put onto the battlefield enters tapped (Tapped$). DigUntil's battlefield destination is lowered for a Valid$ that cannot admit an Aura (typed, no Enchantment). Fecund Greenshell, Clifftop Lookout."},
	{"dig:ExileFaceDown", "DigFaceDown", "A Dig into exile with ExileFaceDown$ True and WithMayLook$ True: each taken card is exiled face down and the resolving controller may look at it (gorge applyMoveFaceDown zone_change.go:1286-1335; fold apply_zone.go:222-240). The mark rides the exiled-with link pool (exwFace), ends when the card leaves exile, and is projected as FFaceDown. ExileFaceDown$ without WithMayLook$ is read only as the blind exile whose look the following Effect's MayLookAt$ static delivers (lower_blinddig.go): the exiler is the controller (Defined$ Targeted) or, with DefinedExiler$ Targeted and ForceReveal$ Targeted over Defined$ You, the target opponent (DigExilerOther: the looker bit is that seat's); the Effect's MayPlay is then the exiler's (MayPlayOpponent). Any other ExileFaceDown$ / WithMayLook$ combination refuses `Dig ExileFaceDown$ shape`. Outrageous Robbery, Decadent Dragon, Black Cat Cunning Thief; Vulcan Mind-Meld."},
	{"kw:HexproofFromInstants", "KwHexproofFromInstants", "Can't be the target of instant spells opponents control (Elenda)."},
	{"kw:ProtBlack", "KwProtBlack", "Protection from black (CR 702.16: DEBT). Akroma's Memorial."},
	{"kw:ProtRed", "KwProtRed", "Protection from red. Akroma's Memorial."},
	{"kw:PreventCombatDamageFrom", "KwPreventCombatDamageFrom", "Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by this creature (an EOT grant: an Effect's bodyless Prevent$ True IsCombat$ True ValidSource$ Card.IsRemembered replacement, gorge effects/effect.go; Maze of Ith). Applied with the recipient's prevention (preventCombatGen); not offered as a candidate in the replacement-order ask."},
	{"kw:PreventCombatDamageTo", "KwPreventCombatDamageTo", "Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to this creature (Fleeting Flight, EOT grant)."},
	{"kw:Wither", "KwWither", "A GRANTED wither (CR 702.80; Pump KW$ Wither, a static AddKeyword$ Wither, an override AddKw): damage to a creature is -1/-1 counters. Printed wither stays CardDef.Wither. Read by kernel witherKw / srcWither (genPrep.anyWitherGrant). Barbed Bloodletter."},
	{"kw:FlashbackOwnCost", "KwFlashbackOwnCost", "A graveyard instant/sorcery gains flashback with a cost equal to its mana cost until end of turn (Sphinx of Forgotten Lore)."},
	{"kw:Unblockable", "KwUnblockable (core bit, kgen use)", "Granted until end of turn for gorge's Effect 'can't be blocked this turn' (Rogue's Passage, Kaito +1, Vampire Gourmand)."},
	{"kw:CantBlock", "KwCantBlock (core bit, kgen use)", "Granted until end of turn for 'target creature can't block this turn' (Frenzied Goblin, Sower of Chaos)."},
	{"ctr:Shield", "CtrShield", "The SHIELD counter (CR 122.1c; shield): damage that would be dealt to the permanent is prevented and one counter removed (combat events one at a time in assignment order; protection prevents first), and a destroy effect removes one instead (after regeneration, NoRegen$ too; gorge's SBA lethal-damage destruction does not read it). Another damage replacement matching the same event stalls (StallShield). Rhox Pummeler, Boon of Safety."},
	{"ctr:Unfeat", "CtrCharge, CtrOil, CtrSpore, CtrQuest, CtrVerse, CtrGrowth, CtrFuse, CtrStory", "Named counters with no inherent rules meaning, numbered above CtrLevel: kept in the same sparse perm slots, outside the frozen feature layout (FeatCtrKinds), compared against gorge per kind through ProjObj.CountersX (kcounters)."},
	{"ctr:New", "CtrIncubation, CtrBait, CtrSoul, CtrFellowship, CtrRevival, CtrStash", "Named counters with no inherent rules meaning; above NumCounterKinds (the kernel's counter array is NumCounterKinds2 wide)."},
	{"cost:PayEnergy", "CostPayEnergy (N energy)", "Pay `N` energy counters (CR 107.14): payable when the controller has `N` (canActivate / pickCostPayable through costObjPayable), paid with the ability's other non-mana costs (payAbilityCosts). An activated non-mana ability's cost only; kgen refuses it elsewhere and PayEnergy<X>. Gorge: rules/cost Energy, rules/pay EnergyPayable."},
	{"cost:Twobrid", "ManaCost.Tb (kop.HybTwobrid)", "A monocoloured hybrid symbol `{2/W}` (CR 107.4e, Forge `2W`) in a single-face card's printed mana cost: each pip is announced as its colour or two generic (CR 601.2b, gorge pay.AnnouncePip), mana value 2 per pip (CR 202.3f). Up to five pips. kgen refuses it in every other cost, beside hybrid, {X}, an alternative or additional cost, or a second face. A cost reduction or increase composes on the announced faces (CR 601.2b, then 601.2f), and the offer gate prices the faces that make it payable. Gorge prices no twobrid cast but a floating pool's (pay.PlanCostDetail: cost:twobrid)."},
	{"cost:Behold", "CardDef.BeholdN, BeholdF, BeholdExile", "Part one of a spell's either-or additional cost is `Behold<1/Type>:<mana>` (CR 701.4a, 601.2b; gorge beholdCostAsk): behold a permanent you control or a card in your hand (the cast spell excepted) matching BeholdF, or pay the other part. Beholding moves and marks nothing. After the either-or answer picks part one, in the cost-pick stage (before blight): no candidate reverses the cast, exactly one is taken unasked, more pose ChCostBehold over the battlefield candidates then the hand ones. Part one is payable only with a candidate. Table data, not a CostFlags bit. Kinsbaile Aspirant, Mudbutton Cursetosser, Silvergill Mentor, Caustic Exhale. BeholdExile (`S:Mode$ RaiseCost | ValidCard$ Card.Self | Cost$ BeholdExile<1/Type>`, gorge foldRaiseExtra / EmitChoiceCosts) is the same ask as a mandatory part of the spell\u2019s own cost, owed whatever the either-or says (no HasAltAdd): the pick is recorded (pkBeholdEx, the lone candidate too), exiled at payment after the discards and before the taps and sacrifices (a permanent through leave, a hand card through detach/placeFrom), and linked to the spell as a reverse exiled-with record (exwPut, stamped with the ver the permanent will have) that the card\u2019s leaves trigger\u2019s Defined$ ExiledWith reads. The cast is offered only with a candidate (spellCostsFeasible) and is no planned cast (plannedCastCost). Champion of the Clachan, Champions of the Perfect, Champions of the Shoal."},
	{"cost:ExileSelf", "CostExileSelf", "Exile this permanent as part of the cost (gorge Exile<1/CARDNAME>: exAsk takes the source unasked; payCast moves it to exile). Paid after the mana when the source could tap for mana itself (paySacsGen, as a sacrifice-this); its leaves-the-battlefield triggers fire, no Sacrificed trigger. An activated non-mana ability with only mana and {T} beside it; kgen refuses the rest."},
	{"cost:ReturnSelf", "CostReturnSelf", "Return this permanent to its owner's hand as part of the cost (gorge Return<1/CARDNAME>: returnAsk takes the source unasked; payCast moves it before the sacrifices and the tap). Paid after the mana when the source could tap for mana itself (paySacsGen, as a sacrifice-this). An activated non-mana ability with only mana and {T} beside it; kgen refuses the rest. The resolution form (UnlessCost$ / an AB$ cost in a trigger) is PayKind PayReturn: one permanent matching F the payer controls, picked (ChGenPayReturn, gorge returncost) and returned to its owner's hand."},
	{"cost:Return", "CostReturn (N, Filter)", "Return `N` permanents you control matching Filter to their owners' hands, chosen at payment after the mana (bsCosts; gorge returnAsk: one KChoose of N there, one ChCostReturn pick per permanent here, asked even with one candidate) and returned after the mana sources are tapped, before the sacrifices (paySacsGen; gorge payCast). Payable with N candidates (costObjPayable). The only counted part of an activated non-mana ability's cost; kgen refuses it on spells and beside another counted part."},
	{"cost:ExileHand", "Cost.ExileHand (with CostExileGrave)", "ExileFromHand<1/Card> (CR 118.3, 602.2b; gorge exAsk over the hand zone): the CostExileGrave part exiles Cost.N cards matching Cost.Filter from the payer's hand instead of their graveyard, each a pick (ChCostExile, one per card, asked even when only one card can pay, in hand order). A table byte, not a CostFlags bit (the words are full). Only the cost of an exile-granted ability (ExtGrantExile) lowers it. Q, Stacking the Deck."},
	{"cost:ExileBf", "Cost.ExileBf (with CostSac)", "Exile<N/Spec> from the battlefield (CR 118.3, 602.2b; gorge cost.parse's exileBattlefieldCost part): the CostSac part's N permanents the payer controls matching Cost.Filter move to exile at payment instead of being sacrificed, each a pick (ChCostSacrifice, asked even when only one can pay). No Sacrificed trigger fires and a CantSacrifice static withholds no candidate. A table byte, not a CostFlags bit (the words are full). A printed activated ability's or a permanent spell's additional cost. Fear of Abduction, The Soul Stone."},
	{"cost:HostExile", "Cost.Host = CostHostExile", "Exile<1/OriginalHost> (CR 118.3, 602.2b; gorge bindGrantedCostReferents): the granted ability exiles the Equipment or Aura that granted it, the one candidate settled unasked; the host must be the payer's own permanent on the battlefield. Not sacrificed: no Sacrificed trigger. The Dominion Bracelet."},
	{"cost:DiscardHand", "Cost.DiscardHand", "Discard<N/Hand> as an activated non-mana ability's own cost (CR 118.3, 602.2b; Reverberating Summons): the whole hand is discarded, in hand order, with the other non-mana cost picks and before the source's own sacrifice (the kernel's activation cost payer runs before the mana; gorge pay.DiscardCandidates' whole-hand spec and pay.PayDiscardCost's one discard action). No choice is asked and an empty hand pays with nothing, so there is no offer gate. The ignored count spells both 0 and 1. A table byte, not a CostFlags bit (the words are full); Discard<N/Random> stays an unless-cost selection method and keeps refusing."},
	{"cost:PutLibSelf", "Cost.PutLibSelf", "PutCardToLibFromGrave<1/-1/CARDNAME> (CR 118.3, 602.2b; Daniels, Temporal Agent): the source card in its owner's graveyard goes to the bottom of that library as the ability's cost. gorge putToLibAsk asks a puttolibcost KChoose even with the source as the only candidate, so the kernel poses the one-option ChCostPutToLib pick (pkPutLib) and moves it at payment. A table byte, not a CostFlags bit (the words are full); only a graveyard activated ability's own cost, alone beside its mana. It is no effect, so the library is not shuffled."},
	{"cost:ExileGSelf", "Cost.ExileGSelf (with CostExileGrave)", "ExileFromGrave<1/CARDNAME> then ExileFromGrave<N/Spec> of the other cards (CR 118.3, 602.2b; Say Its Name): the source card in the payer's graveyard is exiled as the first exile pick, unasked (gorge exAsk's CARDNAME singleton), then Cost.N cards matching Cost.Filter (which excludes the source) are picked one at a time (ChCostExile, as one KChoose of N there). A table byte, not a CostFlags bit (the words are full). A graveyard activated ability's own cost; three parts, the self part second and an unexcluding spec stay refused."},
	{"op:GainEnergy", "OpGainEnergy (Obj player(s), A n)", "Player(s) Obj get `A` energy counters (CR 122.1), kept per player in State (saturating at 255). No decision, no trigger. Gorge: PutCounter Defined$ <player> CounterType$ ENERGY."},
	{"op:OverrideAll", "OpOverrideAll (F filter, A duration, C override)", "Each battlefield permanent matching F (evaluated once, at resolution: CR 611.2c) gets `Table.Overrides[C]` for duration `A.N` (DurEOT / DurPermanent), seat 0's battlefield in entry order then seat 1's, as OpOverride does for one object (one override record each; a full pool stalls). No decision. Gorge: api:AnimateAll (effects/combatfx.go effAnimateAll, registerAnimateEffects per object). A non-RefNone Obj (a player-kind ValidTgts$, `targetPlayerKindScope`) limits the sweep to that player's permanents; an unresolvable player sweeps nothing. RemoveKeywords$ / RemoveAllAbilities$ ride the override record. A PTDelta record (kop.Override.PTDelta; PumpAll Duration$ UntilYourNextTurn with constant NumAtt$/NumDef$, ValPT's PA/TA) is a +N/+M pump, not a base P/T: ptGen adds it with the counters (CR 613.4c), once per merged application, until the resolving controller's next turn (DurUntilYourNextTurn); it adds no state beyond the record's own p, t. V'Ger, the Intruder. Armed and Armored, Natural Affinity, Thelonite Druid; Quick Draw, Curious Colossus, Spectacular Pileup."},
	{"cost:TapPower", "CostTapPower (N floor, Filter)", "Tap any number of other untapped creatures you control matching Filter with total power N or greater (Crew CR 702.122a, Saddle CR 702.171a; gorge tapXType<Any/Creature.Other+withTotalPowerGE<N>>, CostPart.MinPower). Payable with at least one candidate and the candidates' summed current power >= N (canActivate). Paid at bsTapCost by an any-number pick (ChCostTap, gorge's KChoose \"tapcost\" Min 1 MinSum N): each candidate whose pick keeps the floor reachable, and Done once one is picked and the total reaches N; picking the last candidate ends it. The picks tap with the cost (payPicks). An activated ability's whole cost only; kgen refuses it beside any other part. Crew and Saddle Vehicles and Mounts, Mossbridge Troll."},
	{"op:Prepare", "OpPrepare (Obj)", "The battlefield permanent Obj becomes prepared (CR 722.3a; gorge effAlterAttribute Prepared, events apply_player.go): if it is a preparation front (FacePrepare, Face 0) and not already prepared, a DurPrepared play record is armed and its exile copy is minted at the end of its controller's exile (CR 722.3c, gorge grantPreparedCopy: a new object, no zone-change event, no trigger). A second grant on a prepared permanent does nothing; a source off the battlefield is untouched. Lowered from AB/DB$ AlterAttribute Attributes$ Prepared on the card itself (no Defined$ or Self), and from the Updated K:ETBReplacement:Other body (Obj RefReplaced). dirac/face_prepare.go. Also lowered with a ValidTgts$ battlefield target or Defined$ Enchanted (any permanent: one with no prepare spell, or already prepared, is a no-op, as gorge); C=1: unprepare (Activate$ False), which clears the designation and unlinks the copy (kernel face_prepare.go; a non-battlefield referent is untouched). kgen refuses any other Defined$ and any other Activate$ value."},
	{"ex:Void", "ExVoid (Sub[0] yes, Sub[1] no)", "Sub[0] if Edge of Eternities' Void holds, else Sub[1] (gorge Count$Void.<yes>.<no>, cov3BranchHoldsVoid; the arms are integers). Void: a nonland permanent left the battlefield this turn (any player's, to any zone; the zone-add ring's battlefield departures, each object read where it now lives, CR 400.7: gorge never deletes an object, so a token that ceased still counts) or a spell was cast for its warp cost this turn by either player (castProv bit castWarpPush, per push: gorge strips the CastSa Spell.Warp token from each cast's own pay-time flags, so a warp spell since countered still counts). No filter. Both rings record only for a table with the kind (a 25th zone add stalls StallEntered, the 6th cast per player StallCastRing). dirac/value_void.go. Decode Transmissions, Elegy Acolyte, Hylderblade, Hymn of the Faller, Insatiable Skittermaw, Interceptor Mechan, Kavaron Skywarden, Plasma Bolt, Roving Actuator, Temporal Intervention, Tragic Trajectory, Voidforged Titan."},
	{"ex:Revolt", "ExRevolt", "1 if a permanent that left the battlefield this turn is controlled by the controller NOW, else 0 (CR 207.2c ability word; gorge revoltThisTurn, trigger Revolt$ True, an intervening-if re-checked on resolution, CR 603.4). gorge reads Object.Controller after the move, and foldMoveZone resets Controller to the owner on every move off the battlefield (engine/events/apply_zone.go:712, :819), so an object that is not on the battlefield answers with its OWNER (a stolen permanent that died counts for its owner) and one that returned answers with its controller now; the kernel copies that. Tokens count (CR 400.7). Records only for a table with the kind (a 25th zone add stalls StallEntered). dirac/zone_leftzonering.go. Foot Mystic, Insectoid Exterminator, Lord Dregg, Michelangelo, Pizza Face, West Wind Avatar."},
	{"ex:ChosenMode", "ExChosenMode", "The evaluating source permanent's chosen mode index (gorge Card.ChosenMode<X>, effects/filter.go: the permanent's ChosenModes holds X, set by an as-enters GenericChoice with SetChosenMode$ True; the kernel keeps it in the permanent's chosen byte), 255 off the battlefield or unanswered. A Siege's AddStaticAbility$ mode grant is the inner static ANDed with `ExChosenMode == index`; its AddTrigger$ grant is a Gate{CtrMode, index} trigger. Barrensteppe, Glacierwood, Citadel, Palace, Outpost Siege, Battle of Hoover Dam, The Marvelous Scientist; Frostcliff (gorge fires its granted combat-damage batch trigger per damage event), Hollowmurk and Windcrag stay refused."},
	{"ex:ChosenNumber", "ExChosenNumber", "The number the evaluating source permanent chose as it entered (gorge Object.ChosenNumber, which a filter bound \"Chosen\" reads through specCtx's Resolve), kept in the permanent's chosen byte by ExtChooseNumber; 0 when none was chosen or the source is off the battlefield (gorge's zero value). A battlefield SpellCast trigger's ValidCard$ bound only, evaluated with the trigger's source as the context: Nyota Uhura, Communications' cmcEQChosen."},
	{"ex:UnlockedDoors", "ExUnlockedDoors", "Unlocked Room doors among battlefield permanents the controller controls: 1 for a partly unlocked Room, 2 for a fully unlocked one (CR 709.5j; gorge unlockdoor.go countUnlockedDoors). Rampaging Soulrager."},
	{"ex:CastBattlefield", "ExCastBattlefield", "The battlefield permanents matching the card's CastBF as the spell was cast (Count$LastStateBattlefieldWithFallback <spec>; CR 601.2a, gorge castBattlefieldEvent: frozen the moment the spell reaches the stack, before targets, divisions and costs, so a permanent a cost then sacrifices still counts): beginCast freezes the count into the spell entry's trigMV (the byte a spell entry otherwise never uses; a trigger entry's is the trigger-spell MV) and the resolution reads it; a stack copy inherits the entry. gorge's fallback for an uncast source is the live battlefield (engine/effects/count_cast_battlefield.go), the kernel's for a non-spell entry; kgen lowers the head only in a spell's own program, one filter per card (CardDef.CastBF), and the cast-time count reads the live layers (gorge reads the frozen printed types plus the live host's derived ones: equal for the carriers unless a type is granted or lost between cast and resolution). dirac/value_castbattlefield.go. Steer Clear (Mounts), Faerie Fencing (Faeries)."},
	{"ex:CtrAdded", "ExCtrAdded (N kind class | object form << 2)", "1 if the reading controller put a matching counter this turn, else 0: gorge Count$CountersAddedThisTurn <Any|P1P1|LORE> You <Creature|Card.Self> read under CheckSVar$ X (>= 1; kgen refuses any other comparison, the layout keeps presence, not amounts). Creature: a counter on a creature at placement; Self: a counter on the reading source, keyed by object so a flickered source keeps its record. Records only for a table with the kind (prep.anyCtrAdded) and, for Self, a flagged card. dirac/ctr_addedthisturn.go. Lasting Tarfire, Beast Erudite Aerialist, Fractal Tender."},
	{"ex:LeftZone", "ExLeftZone (N origin zone, Filter)", "The number of DISTINCT objects among this turn's zone-add entries whose origin is N (Graveyard) that match Filter where they now live (gorge Count$LeftGraveyardThisTurn, evalCov3HeadLeftZoneThisTurn: counted once per object, so a card that left the graveyard twice counts once). Records only for a table with the kind. dirac/zone_leftzonering.go. Living History, Primary Research, Wilt in the Heat. N Battlefield: Count$LeftBattlefieldThisTurn (Kutzil's Flanker)."},
	{"ex:Mod", "ExMod (Sub[0], N)", "Sub[0] % N, the remainder with the dividend's sign (gorge count_operand.go applyCountOp Mod.N; Forge doXMath). Sab-Sunen, Luxa Embodied."},
	{"ex:Pow", "ExPow (Sub[0] base, Sub[1] exponent)", "Sub[0] raised to Sub[1], a saturating integer power clamped at +-32767 at each multiply (gorge count_operand.go applyCountOp `Pow.`: logarithmic exponentiation; a negative exponent fails closed there, which the kernel answers 0). Lowered from a Trailing value modifier /Pow.<operand>, the operand a non-negative literal or an SVar that lowers (Mathemagics' Number$2/Pow.X with X = Count$xPaid). dirac/value_countheads.go."},
	{"ex:RedNCDmg", "ExRedNCDmg", "The noncombat damage dealt this turn by sources the controller controlled that were red when the damage landed, to any recipient, after replacement and prevention (gorge Count$NonCombatDamageThisTurn Card.Red+YouCtrl Any; genState.redNC, saturating, kept only when a table reads it; replDamage taxes every noncombat hit). Temple of Power."},
	{"ex:SacrificedThisTurn", "ExSacrificedThisTurn (N 0 permanents, N 1 artifact cards, N 2 Food cards)", "The permanents the reading controller sacrificed this turn (gorge PlayerCountPropertyYou$SacrificedThisTurn <Permanent|Artifact>, sacrificedThisTurn, engine/effects/count_cov3.go:282-308): N 0 every one, N 1 the artifact cards among them (the printed type, as gorge matches the card where it went). Counted per sacrifice event for the player who controlled the permanent when it was sacrificed, not its owner (CR 701.21a); a token copy is skipped (CR 707.10h, filter.go matchesZoneSpecCtx rejects an IsCopy object off the stack/battlefield). N 2 is the Food cards (the printed subtype, tokens included; a `/Times.N` suffix applies to the count (Bonecache Overseer); Elanor Gardner). Three per-player tallies in State, written at the one sacrifice choke point (fireSac and the simultaneous fireSacAll, listener or not), saturating at 255, zeroed at turn start. dirac/value_sacrificedthisturn.go. Detective's Satchel, Furtive Courier, Obsessive Pursuit, Sawblade Skinripper, Suspicious Detonation."},
	{"ex:DiscardedThisTurn", "ExDiscardedThisTurn", "The cards the reading controller discarded this turn (gorge PlayerCountPropertyYou$CardsDiscardedThisTurn, CardsDiscardedThisTurn, engine/rules/host_turn_ledger.go): one per-player tally in State (player.disc), bumped at the two hand-to-graveyard discard placements (discardObj, cycleDiscard) for the discarded card's OWNER (a cost discard is paid from the payer's own hand, CR 118.2a), saturating at 255, zeroed at turn start. A madness discard (exile) is NOT counted: gorge rewrites its move Text to \"discarded (madness exile)\" (replacement.go:156), which events.IsDiscard rejects. dirac/value_discardedthisturn.go. Green Goblin, Revenant; Misty Knight, Hero for Hire."},
	{"ex:DilemmasFaced", "ExDilemmasFaced", "The times the reading controller chose modes this turn (gorge Count$YouFaceDilemmaThisTurn)."},
	{"ex:ScriedThisTurn", "ExScriedThisTurn (N 0 scry, N 1 surveil)", "The scry (N 0) or surveil (N 1) instructions the reading controller performed this turn (gorge Count$YouScryThisTurn / Count$YouSurveilThisTurn, engine/effects/count_body_paid.go; rules/scry_surveil_this_turn.go ScriedThisTurn / SurveilledThisTurn fold the log's events.Scry / events.Surveil records since the last TurnChange). Counted at the moments TrigScry / TrigSurveil fire: a surveil as it starts, before the look (also on an empty library); a scry once its arrangement is answered, or at once with no ask (an empty library); a scry or surveil of 0 is none (CR 701.22b, 701.25c). Two nibbles per player in State (genPrep.anyScryTally gates the writes), a sixteenth instruction of one kind in a turn a loud StallTables, zeroed at turn start. dirac/value_scrytally.go. Desperate Futurescribe, Proctor of Potential, Surveillance Phantasm."},
	{"ex:RemLKIPT", "ExRemLKIPT (N 0 power, 1 toughness, 2 countered mana value, 3 sacrificed mana value)", "RememberedLKI$CardPower / $CardToughness over the set a Sacrifice RememberSacrificed$ took: the sum of the power or toughness the sacrificed creatures had just before they left (gorge count_ref_property.go sacrificedInfoFor, CR 608.2g/h), accumulated by sacRemember into resCtx.remLK (the Sacrifice B.N bit 2 power, bit 4 toughness; kgen admits one characteristic per program). Tribute to Hunger. N 2 reads the same accumulator after an OpCounter with CtrRemMV (Hurl into History). N 3 is Sacrificed$CardManaCost: the sacrificed card's printed mana value (gorge SacrificedInfo.ManaValue), accumulated by the same remLKAdd from an OpSacrifice or a printed trigger's own OpIfPaid Sacrifice cost (B.N bit 8, kop.SacSumMV); the writer is one per program. Venom, Lethal Protector; Bolg of the North captures the sum into its reflexive trigger's amount (Spawner>Sacrificed$CardPower; the capture reads the power the creature had when sacrificed, which gorge reads, CR 608.2h)."},
	{"ex:ExiledWithN", "ExExiledWithN (N 0 count, N 1 summed mana value)", "The cards in every seat's exile zone exiled with the reading source (gorge exiledWithSet, Count$ExiledWith$Amount; the same link as pred:ExiledWith, PredN 1). N 1 sums their printed mana values (gorge count_ref_property.go CardManaCost over the same set; kernel exwMVSum). Veteran Survivor; Jadeheart Attendant."},
	{"ex:YourSpeed", "ExYourSpeed (N=1: at max speed)", "N 0: the controller's speed (gorge Count$YourSpeed). N 1: 1 when the controller's speed is at the maximum, 4, else 0 (gorge PlayerCountPropertyYou$HasPropertyMaxSpeed, playerMaxSpeedProperty): Hazoret, Godseeker."},
	{"ex:YourTurns", "ExYourTurns (N=1: is it your turn)", "N 0: the turns begun with the controller as the active player, the current one included (gorge Count$YourTurns, Host.TurnsTaken; genState.yourTurns, counted only when a table reads it); N 1: 1 while it is the controller's turn, else 0 (gorge PlayerCountPropertyYou$HasPropertyActive); N 2: 1 during the controller's own main phase (Count$InOwnMainPhase). Starting Town, Sarkhan's Scorn."},
	{"ex:YourExtraTurns", "ExYourExtraTurns", "1 if the controller has begun an extra turn this game, else 0 (gorge Count$YourExtraTurns, Host.ExtraTurnsBegun: one per extra turn actually begun with the player active, CR 500.7, not per grant). genState.extraTurnBegun is the per-seat bit set when an extra turn's TurnChange fires. H.M.S. Bounty, Unlikely Timeship."},
	{"ex:LowestLife", "ExLowestLife", "The lowest CURRENT life total among the living players (CR 119.3; gorge PlayerCountPlayers$LowestLifeTotal, lifeExtreme over AliveFrom: in two players min(life[0], life[1]), read as the replacement applies). The DSK \"enters tapped unless a player has 13 or less life\" lands' ConditionCheckSVar$ X with ConditionSVarCompare$ GT13 (CR 614.1c). dirac/value_lowestlife.go. Abandoned Campground and kin."},
	{"ex:SelfPrepared", "ExSelfPrepared (N=1 negates)", "1 if the evaluating source is prepared (CR 722.3a: a live DurPrepared record names it), else 0; N=1 negates (gorge evalCountValidSelf over Card.IsPrepared / Card.!IsPrepared). Woodwork Prodigy, Paradox Shaper, Stingerquill Voxmancer."},
	{"ex:ThisTurnActGrave", "ExThisTurnActGrave", "Abilities the evaluating controller activated this turn (one per stack push, mana abilities never reach the stack) whose source object now sits in a graveyard (gorge AbilitiesActivatedThisTurnMatching over Activated.YouCtrl+inZoneGraveyard: matchesSpec reads the source's CURRENT zone, and an ObjID survives zone changes). Recorded in a bounded per-player ring only for tables with this expression; a ninth activation by one player in a turn stalls (StallActRing). A token that left the game does not count. Laboratory Drudge."},
	{"op:DigCounters", "OpDigCounters (A n, C kind)", "A > 0: the card the next OpDigEx puts onto the battlefield enters with A counters of kind C (genState.enterCtr; Dig's WithCounters$ / WithCountersAmount$, one-card takes only); A = 0 clears it, emitted right after the Dig. gorge effDig reads neither parameter (cr-dig-withcounters): the kernel plays the card text. The Undercity's Throne of the Dead Three."},
	{"ext:SearchCounters", "OpExt ExtSearchCounters (B amount, C kind)", "B > 0: the next card a library search puts onto the battlefield enters with B counters of kind C (genState.enterCtr; a ChangeZone search's WithCountersType$ / WithCountersAmount$, one-card takes only). kgen emits the arm before the Search and B = 0 after it. The entering card consumes it in enter, as a graveyard pick's rider does. dirac/ctr_search.go. Captain Jean-Luc Picard."},
	{"op:TakeInitiative", "OpTakeInitiative (Obj player, C dungeon card)", "Player Obj takes the initiative (CR 726.3: one holder, genState.initH) and ventures into the dungeon card C (Undercity, CR 726.2; gorge effTakeInitiative then effVenture Dungeon$ Undercity): no dungeon -- a command-zone dungeon object is created with the marker on the top room; else the marker follows the room's one arrow, or the controller picks between two (ChRoom, gorge's \"room\" KChoose in printed order); from the bottommost room the dungeon is completed and a new one begins (CR 701.49c). The room entered queues its latent ability as a trigger the dungeon's owner controls (CR 309.4c). The holder ventures at their upkeep and a player whose creatures deal combat damage to the holder takes it (source-less triggers). dirac/act_initiative.go. Avenging Hunter."},
	{"op:Ext", "OpExt (A = Const(sub-op))", "The extension op, the last high slot: A.N names an ExtOp sub-op (kop/ext.go), numbered from 1 and append-only, the instruction's other fields being the sub-op's own; the kernel dispatches it in a cold file (execExt). New families take a sub-op here instead of an op: the op space is full."},
	{"ext:UnlockDoor", "OpExt ExtUnlockDoor (Obj, C)", "DB$ UnlockDoor (CR 709.5f-g; gorge effects/unlockdoor.go effUnlockDoor) over one target slot (ValidTgts$ Room.YouCtrl, TargetMin 0/1, TargetMax 1): C 0 (Mode$ Unlock) unlocks a locked door; C 1 (Mode$ LockOrUnlock) first asks the controller \"Lock or unlock a door?\" (ChRoomDoorHalf, option 0 = unlock), then picks a door when both qualify (ChRoomDoor, face order, gorge's \"Choose a Room door\"), swaps the Room permanent's state def without paying, and fires the unlocked door's UnlockDoor triggers and the fully-unlock watchers on an unlock (a lock fires nothing; gorge DoorLock). dirac/face_unlockdoor.go. Ghostly Keybearer, Keys to the House, Marina Vendrell."},
	{"op:Unearth", "OpUnearth", "After its unearth ability's Return of itself from the graveyard (CR 702.84a; gorge kwUnearth's expansion, rules/unearth.go unearthEnter): the source gains haste until end of turn and is exiled at the beginning of the next end step (a delayed record whose act is OpUnearth, ordered with the other end-step triggers even when stale, as Warp's); while that record is live the permanent leaving the battlefield for any zone goes to exile instead (genPrep.anyUnearth leave hook). A high op (kop/ops.go). Yotian Frontliner."},
	{"ext:TurnFaceUp", "OpExt ExtTurnFaceUp (Obj, C, F)", "SetState Mode$ TurnFaceUp (CR 708.6; gorge effSetState's turnUp arm): an effect turns a face-down battlefield permanent face up with no cost; its turn-up replacements run and its turned-face-up triggers fire, as the special action's turn-up does after payment (no Megamorph counter). A permanent no longer face down, or whose printed face is an instant or sorcery (gorge setStateTurnUpVerdict), is left alone. C 0: the target in Obj (ValidTgts$; Expose the Culprit). C 1: Choices$ (Optional$ or not): the resolving controller picks up to one battlefield permanent matching F that would turn up, seat 0's first in battlefield order, or Done (ChGenTurnUpPick, gorge setStateChoose's \"setstate_pick\" Min 0 Max 1); none asks nothing. dirac/face_turnupeffect.go. Expose the Culprit, Hustle // Bustle."},
	{"ext:PutCounterExisting", "OpExt ExtPutCounterExisting (Obj, B)", "CounterType$ ExistingCounter (gorge putCounterExisting): the controller chooses a kind of counter already on the object in Obj (kernel kind order, the Glissa kind ask, the oracle compares by kind) and puts B more of it on it; no kind does nothing, a single kind is put unasked. The put is an ordinary OpPutCounter of the pick: replacements, the CR 616.1 order ask and the counter-added triggers run. dirac/ctr_putexisting.go. Dathon, His Heart Open."},
	{"ext:RemoveCounterAny", "OpExt ExtRemoveCounterAny (Obj, B, C)", "Remove up to B counters from the object in Obj, its controller picking the kind of each (kinds still present, kernel kind order; the oracle compares by kind), C&1 (UpTo$) offering Done at every step, a single kind without UpTo$ taken unasked; the picks are removed together at the end (gorge removeCounterAny, cr-removecounter-any-upto). Glissa Sunslayer."},
	{"ext:ChooseColorRes", "OpExt ExtChooseColorRes", "The resolving controller chooses a colour (ChGenColor, all five), kept in res.chosen for the ExtColorGrant that follow (gorge effChooseColor Defined$ You; Skrelv, Defector Mite)."},
	{"ext:ChooseNumber", "OpExt ExtChooseNumber (B lowest, C highest)", "An as-enters number choice, the first instruction of an enters program (CR 614.12; gorge's ETB ChooseNumber, Defined$ You, its options from effects.ETBNumberChoices): the entering permanent's controller chooses a number from B to C (a ChGenNumber decision, mode = the number), asked as the colour choice is, and the answer is kept in the permanent's chosen byte, read by ExChosenNumber. Literal Min$/Max$ only; without Max$ the offer ends at 12, and a bound gorge cannot honour falls back to 0..12 as gorge does."},
	{"ext:ExileEmbRem", "OpExt ExtExileEmbRem (no operands)", "The body of a remembering emblem's leave trigger (kop.Emblem.CaptureRem; Mysterio, Master of Illusion's \"exile those tokens when it leaves\"): every object the firing trigger carries (trigObj, trigAmt, x and trigMV, the emblem's remembered set when the trigger was queued, with the versions stamped as it went on the stack) that is still the object it was and on the battlefield is exiled, in the order the emblem remembered them; one that has left since is skipped (CR 400.7). An empty set does nothing. dirac/trig_emblemrem.go."},
	{"ext:SacDelayed", "OpExt ExtSacDelayed (Obj RefDelayedRemembered)", "Mobilize's end-step body (CR 702.181a; gorge Sacrifice Defined$ DelayTriggerRememberedLKI): the group program's remembered tokens (trigObj and the second packed in trigAmt) still on the battlefield are sacrificed as one batch (fireSacAll, leaveAll); none left does nothing; a member another player controls stalls StallSacOther (gorge checks no controller, CR 701.21a). OpDelayedProgram B = DpGroup registers the whole remembered set (up to two; more stalls StallDProg). Mobilize 1-2."},
	{"ext:ExileExMark", "OpExt ExtExileExMark (Obj, C the Fight fighter's ref or 0)", "A Pump or Fight's ReplaceDyingDefined$ Targeted (gorge effects/damage.go registerReplaceDying over the pump's affected or the fight's targeted objects; CR 614.1a, 614.9): the object in Obj (RefTarget runs once per object of a multi-object slot) still on the battlefield takes the turn-scoped exile-instead mark (markExileEx), so it is exiled instead of dying this turn, whether or not it took damage. A second mark on one creature stalls StallReplLeave (CR 616.1). C != 0 is a Fight: the mark lands only while the fighter C and the object are both creatures on the battlefield (gorge fightPairs drops the pair, and registerReplaceDying then registers nothing, when either left). Emitted right after the pump or fight. Gnashing of Teeth, Faunsbane Troll."},
	{"ext:ExHaste", "OpExt ExtExHaste (Obj, C bits 0-7)", "Until the cleanup step the object Obj can't be blocked except by creatures with haste (gorge Effect Mode$ CantBlockBy | ValidAttacker$ Card.IsRemembered | ValidBlocker$ Creature.withoutHaste; CR 509.1b, 702.10a): canBlock refuses a blocker whose CURRENT keywords lack haste. C bit 0 is the power form (Cavern Stomper, Cheeky House-Mouse: ValidBlocker$ Creature.power<op><N>, N 0..15): C bits 1-3 hold the comparison (kop.CmpOp), bits 4-7 the constant, and canBlock refuses a blocker whose CURRENT power satisfies it (gorge matches ValidBlocker$ at block declaration, CR 509.1b, 611.2c); a haste record and a power record of one attacker are separate records. A record in genState.exH (a seventeenth stalls StallExHaste), not a keyword, so it survives a loss of all abilities and is no projected keyword. A record ends with its own permanent, whichever others the effect named (ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield, CR 611.2c). Any other ValidBlocker$ is refused. Agility Bobblehead; Cavern Stomper, Cheeky House-Mouse."},
	{"ext:ColorGrant", "OpExt ExtColorGrant (Obj, B, C)", "Until the cleanup step, the object Obj has, for res.chosen's colour, hexproof from it (C bit 0), toxic B (summed with its printed toxic) and \"can't be blocked by creatures of that colour\" (C bit 1); a grant of the same object and colour merges, a fourth record stalls StallColGrant (gorge definedKWGrant and the CantBlockBy Effect's freezeChosenColor, cr-pump-definedkw-chosencolor). genState.colG. Skrelv, Defector Mite."},
	{"ext:BreachChoose", "OpExt ExtBreachChoose", "For each player (the resolving controller first, then the other), the controller chooses a creature or planeswalker card in that player's graveyard (a mandatory ChGenChooseCard ask, also posed with one candidate, none when there is no candidate) and imprints it: the picks accumulate in the chosen set in pick order (gorge RepeatEach Player over ChooseCard Defined$ You ChoiceZone$ Graveyard ImprintChosen$ True). Breach the Multiverse."},
	{"ext:BreachReturn", "OpExt ExtBreachReturn", "Every card of the chosen set still in a graveyard enters the battlefield under the resolving controller's control, in pick order, as one entering event (gorge ChangeZone Defined$ Imprinted GainControl$ True Origin$ Graveyard Destination$ Battlefield). Breach the Multiverse."},
	{"ext:ExileLandChoose", "OpExt ExtExileLandChoose", "The resolving controller chooses a land card the other player (the one opponent of a two-seat game) owns among the remembered cards in exile (a mandatory ChGenChooseCard ask, also posed with one candidate, none when there is no candidate) and imprints it: the chosen set (gorge RepeatEach Opponent over ChooseCard Defined$ You ChoiceZone$ Exile ImprintChosen$ True); OpMayPlay over RefChosen then grants the controller a permission to play each chosen card while it remains exiled. Ensign Pavel Chekov."},
	{"ext:Phases", "OpExt ExtPhases (Obj)", "The permanent Obj names (RefSelf, or a target slot run once per object) phases out (CR 702.26a; gorge effPhases without PhaseInOrOut$): it and every permanent attached to it, recursively, indirectly (CR 702.26g, gorge foldPhaseOut), leave every battlefield walk -- they keep their slots and are on no slot mask, their object zone is ZonePhased (direct) or ZonePhasedInd -- and leave combat; nothing enters or leaves (CR 702.26d, no version bump). The direct ones phase in at their controller's untap step, before it untaps, in battlefield-list order; an indirect one phases in with the permanent it is attached to and stays attached (CR 702.26h). Cleanup ends damage and until-end-of-turn effects on them too. Cold: guarded by prep.phasing (a table with this program): the slot allocator, the untap and cleanup steps, a host's departure and the projection. Obj RefNone with F (AllValid$ <filter>): every battlefield permanent matching F phases out, one at a time in gorge's object order (effPhases' arena walk; the kernel's Obj order), one already phased out by an earlier host's attachment sweep skipped (The City on the Edge of Forever). Spectral Adversary; the toggle, Phaseout$, RememberAffected$, WontPhaseInNormal$ and K:Phasing are refused."},
	{"ext:GrantPanharm", "OpExt ExtGrantPanharm (Obj target)", "The target gains \"if a triggered ability of this permanent triggers, that ability triggers an additional time\" (CR 603.2d) for as long as the ability's source stays a tapped permanent and the target stays on the battlefield (gorge Effect Mode$ Panharmonicon | ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered, Duration$ UntilUntaps, ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield; CR 611.2b). Nothing is granted when the source is not a tapped permanent as this resolves. One record per grant (host, target) in genState.pgT / pgH, dropped at the host's first untap or departure and at the target's departure, and counted by the Panharmonicon echo walk beside the printed statics: two grants on one creature echo twice. Four grants at once stall StallPanharmGrant. Lwaxana Troi, Charming Guest."},
	{"ext:GrantExile", "OpExt ExtGrantExile (Obj RefRemembered, C ability)", "Every remembered card in exile gains the resolving ability's card's latent activated ability C (its ActZone is Exile) for as long as it stays exiled (gorge Animate Abilities$ with Duration$ Permanent: a layer-6 AddAbilities effect that effectMoveSweep ends when the card leaves exile). One record per granted card (the card, its version and the host object whose ability it is) in genState.qgO / qgV / qgH, three bytes of each of eight slots; a record is live while the card is in exile at the recorded version (CR 400.7). A ninth live grant stalls StallExileGrant. The card's owner is offered the ability as AkActivate{source: the exiled card, target: the host, mode: 0x80|ability} on their own turn (the ability's PlayerTurn$ gate, Trig.Cond) while a hand card can pay its cost, in exile order beside the other granted abilities (dirac/cast_exilegrant.go). Q, Stacking the Deck."},
	{"ext:LockActs", "OpExt ExtLockActs (Obj target)", "The target, when tapped as this resolves, cannot have any activated ability activated (mana abilities included) until its first untap or departure; the source leaving changes nothing (gorge Effect Mode$ CantBeActivated, ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered, ValidSA$ Activated, Duration$ UntilTargetedUntaps). Eight locks at once (nlA, nlB, nlC) stall StallNetLock; a locked card with a mana ability that does not tap stalls StallNetMana. Braided Net."},
	{"ext:BlocksIfAble", "OpExt ExtBlocksIfAble (Obj)", "The battlefield permanent Obj (the Effect's target) blocks this turn if able (CR 509.1c; gorge Effect StaticAbilities$ Mode$ MustBlock | ValidCreature$ Card.IsRemembered over RememberObjects$ Targeted or ThisTargetedCard, ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield, read by combat.MustBlockCandidates): the arena slot bit mechBlocksIfAble, no State byte, cleared as the next turn begins and when the permanent leaves. A blocker requirement in the same maximum-requirements count as the must-be-blocked and Lure ones: one unit per marked blocker that blocks; a pair is offered only while the maximum stays reachable and Done only once it is met. A target no longer on the battlefield does nothing; a Duration$ refuses. Culvert Ambusher, Courtly Provocateur, Hustle // Bustle."},
	{"ext:AegisClone", "OpExt ExtAegisClone", "Resolution of a TrigAttached trigger: the controller picks the creature card exiled with the attachment's incarnation (the OpExileUntilLeaves link; gorge's clone_choice KChoose, posed with one option too, ChGenChooseCard on the Hideaway ask code) and the bearer (RefTriggerObj) becomes a copy of it until the attachment is unattached or leaves (genState.linkAeg; the live attachment with the latest layer timestamp wins; a bearer that is a copy already stalls StallAegis). Assimilation Aegis."},
	{"ext:SweepFrom", "OpExt ExtSweepFrom (Obj the source's target slot, B the amount, F the creature filter, C&1 = the source's own slot excluded)", "DamageAll DamageSource$ ParentTarget over <spec>.NotDefinedTargeted (CR 120.3; gorge effDamageAll with damageSourceParam): the target creature in Obj deals B damage (read once) to every battlefield creature matching F (seat 0 first, entry order; not Obj's own slot when C&1) in one damage batch whose hits all name the source, so its deathtouch, lifelink (one gain per batch), infect and wither apply. A source that left deals from the resolving spell. Two competing damage replacements on a hit stall (StallReplPlus). dirac/act_sweepdamage.go. Waltz of Rage, Nibelheim Aflame."},
	{"ext:ChangeTargets", "OpExt ExtChangeTargets (Obj a TgtStackObj slot with TgfSingleTgt, or RefTriggerObj; C bit 0: Optional$)", "Change the targets of the spell or ability on the stack that Obj names (CR 115.7; gorge effChangeTargets): a slot target is a spell or ability holding exactly one target, chain links counted (TargetType$ SpellAbility.singleTarget, ValidTgts$ Card,Emblem), RefTriggerObj the spell whose cast fired the trigger (Defined$ TriggeredSpellAbility in a SpellCast trigger, Speedball). The redirect's controller answers one ask per declaration, the root's and then each announced SubAbility$ link's, over the slot's legal targets judged as the redirected entry; a charm's head names none, so no ask. Without Optional$ (115.7a) the current targets are not offered and, unless every declaration has enough others, nothing moves. With it (115.7d) they are, Done keeps the rest, and a pick already a target stays in place. Every answer is written after the last ask, and each target that became one is reported as targeted. More than 8 answers stalls (StallMultiRetarget). Chooser$, DefinedMagnet$, RandomTarget$, ChangeSingleTarget$ and TargetRestriction$ refuse (unread params). dirac/act_stackrewrite.go. Bolt Bend, Redirect Lightning, Untimely Malfunction, Speedball, New Warrior."},
	{"ext:CounterAll", "OpExt ExtCounterAll (no operands)", "Counter every spell and ability an opponent of the resolving controller controls (CR 701.5; gorge effCounter over Defined$ ValidStack Spell.OppCtrl,Activated.OppCtrl,Triggered.OppCtrl, the stack bottom first): an uncounterable spell is skipped (gorge CounterAllowed), a spell goes to its graveyard, an ability is removed with no card move. RememberCounteredSA$ True: each countered entry adds one to the resolution's remembered count (genState.remCnt, the channel ExRememberedCount sums), which the following Count$RememberedSize reads. Any other ValidStack spec refuses. dirac/act_stackrewrite.go. Glen Elendra's Answer."},
	{"tgf:SingleTgt", "TgfSingleTgt", "A TgtStackObj slot admits only a spell or an ability whose targets are exactly one distinct target (gorge TargetType$ SpellAbility.singleTarget, the singleTarget property: kernel singleTargetOK over the entry's chain). Bolt Bend, Redirect Lightning, Untimely Malfunction."},
	{"ext:Airbend", "OpExt ExtAirbend (Obj, or F with Obj RefNone and C = 1+excluded target slot)", "Airbend (CR 701.65a; gorge effAirbend): exile the battlefield permanent Obj (a target slot), or every battlefield permanent matching F (Defined$ Valid, seat 0 first; a trailing .NotDefinedTargeted becomes the C exclusion of the ability's one target), through the ordinary leave path, and give each card that reached exile its owner's DurAirbend record: the owner may cast it from exile for {2} (AkCast mode castAirbend, the card's own timing, the floating pool alone paying; a cast marks the stack entry trigPlAirbend and buildCostGen charges {2}); a token ceases to exist in exile and gets none. A spell-target airbend (TgtZone$, a filter with no permanent type) and every param beyond the subject refuse. dirac/act_airbend.go. Aang the Last Airbender, Aang Swift Savior, Airbender Ascension, Airbender's Reversal, Airbending Lesson, Appa Loyal Sky Bison, Avatar's Wrath, Glider Staff."},
	{"ext:EffEtbCtr", "OpExt ExtEffEtbCtr (B count)", "A SpellCast trigger's `DB$ Effect | RememberObjects$ TriggeredCard | SetChosenNumber$ N | ExileOnMoved$ Stack` whose one `Event$ Moved | ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered | Destination$ Battlefield | ReplacementResult$ Updated` replacement puts `DB$ PutCounter | Defined$ ReplacedCard | CounterType$ P1P1 | ETB$ True | CounterNum$ Count$ChosenNumber` (gorge effects/effect.go:583-636 registers it with the frozen ChosenNumber; rules/replacement.go:1180-1231 applies the move, ends the effect, runs the body, then matches the entry's triggers). B (max 0) is evaluated once as the Effect resolves and added to the triggering spell's stack entry (stackEntry.spc bits 11-15, more than 31 stalls StallEffEtbCtr); the permanent enters with that many more +1/+1 counters through the counter replacements, after its printed enters-with counters and before its ETB triggers. The effect ends when the spell leaves the stack, so a spell already gone gets nothing, and a stack copy has none. Torgal, A Fine Hound; Wildgrowth Archaic; Mikey & Don, Party Planners and Undead Sprinter's constant-CounterNum$ 1 bodies."},
	{"ext:StackExileMark", "OpExt ExtStackExileMark (C kop.StackExile* bits)", "An Effect's `Event$ Moved | Origin$ Stack | Destination$ Graveyard | ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered` replacement whose body exiles the ReplacedCard (gorge effects/effect.go registers it with ExileOnMoved$ Stack, ending it as the spell leaves the stack). Trigger form (a SpellCast trigger, RememberObjects$ TriggeredCard, ConditionPresent$ on the stack, ValidCard$ ...+YouOwn): the triggering spell, if still on the stack, gets stackEntry.remVer bit 4 (a second replacement on one spell stalls StallExileOnMoved), so a resolved, fizzled, countered or held exit sends it to exile (stackEntry.exilesOnLeave); with the plot rider (remVer bit 5) the exiled card becomes plotted (kw_plot.go plotOne). A dream counter (Goliath Daydreamer) stalls. Grant form (RememberObjects$ Remembered after an exile, Nita, Forum Conciliator): each remembered exiled card's may-play record gets until bit 6 and the cast that spends it carries the mark; a capped record stalls. A stack copy has no mark. Lilah, Undefeated Slickshot; Nita, Forum Conciliator."},
	{"ext:FinalityCtr", "OpExt ExtFinalityCtr (Obj the triggering spell)", "A Static$ True SpellCast trigger's `DB$ Effect | RememberObjects$ TriggeredCard` (or `ExileOnMoved$ Stack` with ValidCard$ Card.EffectSource) whose one `Event$ Moved | Origin$ Stack | ValidCard$ Card.IsRemembered | Destination$ Battlefield | ReplacementResult$ Updated` replacement puts `DB$ PutCounter | Defined$ ReplacedCard | CounterType$ FINALITY | ETB$ True | CounterNum$ 1 | SubAbility$ <ChangeZone Self Command Exile>`, or the same body with no SubAbility$ (gorge ends that Effect when its remembered spell leaves the stack, CR 400.7): the trigger resolves off the stack, before the CR 603.3b ordering ask (gorge static_trigger.go, Tf3Static), and the cast spell's stack entry gains one FINALITY rider (stackEntry.sid bits 6-7, a 2-bit count: two grants can cover one cast; a fourth stalls StallFinality). The permanent enters with that many FINALITY counters through the counter replacements, one per grant, after its printed enters-with counters and before its ETB triggers; dieZone's finality exile is armed. Intrepid Paleontologist, Leonardo Sewer Samurai, Osteomancer Adept; Storied Veteran, Overflow Submatrix."},
	{"ext:CopyAbility", "OpExt ExtCopyAbility (B amount, C&1 MayChooseTarget$, C>>1 target slot)", "Copy the activated or triggered ability on the stack named by target slot C>>1 (a TgtCopyAb or TgtCopyTrig slot: an ability its chooser controls, of a source whose card types match the slot's Filter; the resolving entry is never a candidate, CR 115.5), B times (Amount$, read once; 0 or less copies nothing, the count capped at 255). Each copy is an ordinary stack entry minted below the resolving one: same source, ability, X, mode, targets and trigger context, the resolving controller as its controller, no cast provenance. It is not activated or cast (CR 707.10), so no cost is paid and no activation limit or tally moves. A target gone from the stack, or an ability marked ab:CantCopy, copies nothing. C&1: as each copy is about to resolve its controller is asked (in gorge's order: mint, ask, mint, ask) for the ability's first target slot, as OpCopySpell's election is (gorge AskCopyTargets); an ability with more than one target slot stalls StallTables. Stack overflow stalls StallStack. Peter Parker's Camera, Echo Perceptive Prodigy, Scientist Supreme of A.I.M., Kirol Attentive First-Year, Gogo Master of Mimicry (Amount$ X), Mister Fantastic (Amount$ 2)."},
	{"ext:ToGraveyard", "OpExt ExtToGraveyard (Obj)", "Move the object Obj names to its owner's graveyard (a ChangeZone move, not the mill keyword action: no mill replacement, no MvMayMill). With Obj RefLibTop it is gorge's `ChangeZone Defined$ TopOfLibrary Origin$ Library Destination$ Graveyard Optional$ True` under an OpMayAsk MayGuardLibraryTop (moveDefinedLibraryObjects: a position read, no shuffle). Gathering Stone, Traveling Botanist and kin."},
	{"ext:Suspect", "OpExt ExtSuspect (Obj, or F with Obj RefNone; C bit 0 = remove)", "The battlefield permanent Obj, or every battlefield permanent matching F (Defined$ Valid, read once, seat 0 first), becomes suspected (CR 701.60; gorge effAlterAttribute Attributes$ Suspected), or with C bit 0 (Activate$ False) no longer suspected: the arena slot bit mechSuspected, no State byte. A suspected creature has menace (a base keyword, so a lose-all effect removes it) and can't block; the designation ends when it leaves the battlefield and at any control change, an end-of-turn revert included. Optional$ True rides an OpMayAsk with MayGuardSuspect (posed only when some object would flip, gorge alterAttributeWouldChange). A target no longer on the battlefield does nothing. RememberAltered$ refuses. Barbed Servitor, Caught Red-Handed, Absolving Lammasu, Rubblebelt Braggart."},
	{"ext:SpellToLib", "OpExt ExtSpellToLib", "The resolving spell moves from the stack to the top of its owner's library, then that library is shuffled (CR 608.2n; gorge effChangeZone Origin$ Stack, Destination$ Library, Shuffle$ True over Defined$ Parent): it goes to no graveyard. A spell copy is ceased by the finish and the library is shuffled all the same. Blue Sun's Zenith and the other Zenith spells."},
	{"ext:AttacksIfAble", "OpExt ExtAttacksIfAble (Obj)", "The battlefield permanent Obj (the Effect's target) attacks this turn if able (CR 508.1d; gorge Effect StaticAbilities$ Mode$ MustAttack | ValidCreature$ Card.IsRemembered over RememberObjects$ Targeted or ThisTargetedCard, ExileOnMoved$ Battlefield): the arena slot bit mechAttacksIfAble, no State byte, cleared as the next turn begins and when the permanent leaves. Read wherever the MustAttack static is (declareMustAttack's auto-declaration, mustAttackLeft under Config.GorgeMustAttack, State.MustAttack); the duty sits on the Effect, so losing its abilities keeps it. A target no longer on the battlefield does nothing; a Duration$, a MustAttack$ defender and a player-scoped ValidCreature$ refuse. Heckling Fiends, Incite, Courtly Provocateur."},
	{"ext:MustBeBlocked", "OpExt ExtMustBeBlocked (Obj, or F with Obj RefNone)", "The battlefield permanent Obj, or every battlefield permanent matching F (PumpAll ValidCards$, read once, seat 0 first), must be blocked this turn if able (CR 509.1c; gorge Pump / PumpAll KW$ HIDDEN CARDNAME must be blocked if able., an Animate's HiddenKeywords$ CARDNAME must be blocked if able., the hidden keyword MustBlock read layer-derived per attacker): the arena slot bit mechMustBlocked, no State byte, cleared as the next turn begins and when the permanent leaves. It counts as the printed keyword does (CardDef.MustBeBlocked) unless the permanent has lost its abilities. A target no longer on the battlefield does nothing; an Animate with a Duration$, or without one object (AnimateAll), and a PumpAll with a ValidTgts$ player scope refuse. Joraga Invocation, Magitek Scythe, Disturbed Slumber."},
	{"ext:CloneCopy", "OpExt ExtCloneCopy (Obj becomer or RefNone with F its Valid set, B.N kop.Clone* flags, C copy exceptions)", "DB$ Clone on the battlefield: the becomer (Obj: the source or a target slot; or, with Obj RefNone, every battlefield permanent matching F, seat 0 first, entry order, less the template when B.N&CloneExclTmpl) becomes a copy of the template permanent (CR 707.2, 613.2a): the steps of OpBecomeCopy's entry (unsubscribe the old card, the copied card's characteristics, subscribe it, the template's copy exceptions then the op's, C = override index+1, NonLegendary$ and AddKeywords$ only; CR 707.9b). The template is target slot B.N>>CloneTmplShift&3, or, with CloneTmplPick, the Choices$ pick (chosen[0]); it must still be on the battlefield, else nothing happens. B.N&CloneEOT (Duration$ UntilEndOfTurn): the becomer gets an fxCopyEOT record (once); no Duration$ (or Permanent) records the source in an fxCopyPerm record. The cleanup step (CR 514.2) returns each recorded becomer to its printed card and re-bases it on its newest permanent copy's source as that source is then, as gorge settleExpiredClones does. Both end when the becomer leaves (CR 400.7). With B.N&ClonePick the op is only the Choices$ pick (the controller picks among the battlefield permanents matching F; nothing is asked with none); an Optional$ copy puts OpMayAsk MayGuardCloneCopy before the copy op (asked only when a template and a becomer are live, gorge's pairs). With B.N&CloneBatch (with ClonePick, then CloneTmplPick) the pool is the resolving trigger's batch members (a one-or-more exile trigger's moved set, trig_batchmembers.go) still in exile and matching F, each player's exile in zone order, and the copy is of the picked card as printed (it must still be in exile); Obj is the becomer target. A becomer that is its own template is an ordinary copy layer (CR 707.2): it copies its own copiable values, its current copy exceptions among them (CR 707.9b), held beside the layer so a re-base restores them; on an Aegis bearer the new copy covers the Aegis copy, which the cleanup step gives back (copy_aegisunder.go). Kaya, Spirits' Justice. Fleeting Reflection, Shuri, Deepfathom Echo, Oko the Ringleader, Silent Hallcreeper, Naga Fleshcrafter."},
	{"ext:CopyExiledWith", "OpExt ExtCopyExiledWith (F, B.N CopyFlags, C copy exceptions override+1)", "CopyPermanent Defined$ ExiledWith (The Cloning of Shredder's chapters II and III): for each card in any seat's exile zone exiled with the resolving source (gorge exiledWithSet: seat 0 first, exile order), create a token that's a copy of it under the resolving controller's control. F is the exiled-with filter in the predicate form (PredExiledWith, PredN 1), so a resolving trigger's fire incarnation counts, as gorge's read passes it. As gorge's CopyPermanent Defined arm does, every source's copy count is sized through the CreateToken replacements first, then the copies are minted source by source and enter together (CR 603.6a). B.N and C are OpCopyAsTokenEx's copy riders and copy exceptions (CR 707.9b; NonLegendary$, AddTypes$). An exiled card is not a permanent, so the copy has no template slot. A copy whose as-enters choice or Aura host parks is resumed by the ordinary copy ask when no later copy remains; a later exiled card would mint out of the answer's order, so that shape stalls StallCopyAllAsk. A Choices$ pool stays unread and refuses by name (gorge asks the controller to pick one of the set)."},
	{"ext:CopyAllEach", "OpExt ExtCopyAllEach (F, C copy exceptions)", "For each battlefield permanent matching F (Defined$ Valid <filter>, the set read once at resolution, seat 0 first, entry order), create a token that's a copy of it under the resolving controller's control (CR 707.2, 111.10). As gorge's CopyPermanent Defined arm does, every source's copy count is sized through the CreateToken replacements first, then the copies are minted source by source; a source gone mid-sweep mints nothing. C (index+1) is the copy exceptions' override (CR 707.9b; NonLegendary$). A copied Aura with two or more legal hosts poses the host ask (CR 303.4f), and a copy with an as-enters choice poses that choice; either parks the sweep (genState.sweep): the answer enters the waiting copy and the sweep resumes with the remaining copies (raGenTokChoice / raGenEnchant, copy_allpark.go). Gorge's zone batch spans the park, so the sweep's enters checks are held across it and fire once, in entry order, when the sweep ends (CR 603.6a). A copy of a copy (copyTokenBasis) and an Aura with several hosts and an as-enters choice still stall StallCopyAllAsk. Multiversal Incursion; its Animate sibling (Sita Varma, Masked Racer) is an OpOverrideAll over the same set behind OpMayAsk MayGuardAnimateAll (asked only when the set has a battlefield hit)."},
	{"ext:AddPhase", "OpExt ExtAddPhase (B count, C kind | splice point << 4)", "Queue B extra phases (gorge effAddPhase, DB$ AddPhase; none for a count of 0 or less): kind Combat (BeginCombat..EndCombat), Upkeep or End, spliced after the step in C's high nibble (EndCombat, End). The kernel keeps gorge's pending queue run-length coded in genState.xph (four distinct entries, StallAddPhase past that; Obeka's N upkeeps are one entry) and advance enters the most recently created pending entry's first step on leaving its splice point, resuming at the splice point's successor when the last one completes (gorge rules/turn.go extraPhaseBoundary, CR 500.8). The jumps outside advance (declare attackers with no attacker, regular damage to end of combat) skip it, as gorge's do. Kind CombatMain (C = 3, FollowedBy$ Main2 behind ConditionPhases$ Main1,Main2; the splice point is the main phase it resolves in) is an extra combat then an additional main phase: cast in the second main phase the walk resumes at it, cast in the first it enters the second main phase and then the ordinary combat (gorge extraPhaseBoundary, followedByMainBeforeCombat); the queue holds that one entry alone, any other grant beside it a StallAddPhase. Aurelia the Warleader, Full Throttle, Obeka Splitter of Seconds, Y'shtola Rhul, Great Train Heist, Relentless Assault."},
	{"ext:SkipPhase", "OpExt ExtSkipPhase (Obj the player)", "The player Obj skips every combat phase of their next turn (gorge effSkipPhase, DB$ SkipPhase with Phase$ BeginCombat, Start$ FromNext, Duration$ UntilTheEndOfTargetedNextTurn; CR 614.10): genState.cskip holds a pending bit until that player's next turn begins and a live bit through it, and advance enters the postcombat main phase instead of the beginning of combat on a live turn, so no combat step, beginning-of-combat trigger or combat ledger entry happens; an extra combat granted to that player is consumed and completed at once. False Peace, Empty City Ruse."},
	{"ex:Adamant", "ExAdamant (N)", "Sub[0] when at least n mana of one colour was spent to cast the source, else Sub[1] (CastSA>Count$Adamant_<n>.<Colour>.<yes>.<no>; gorge effects/count_body_heads.go evalAdamantBranch). N packs the colour index (bits 0-2, W U B R G) and n (bits 3-4, 0-3: the per-colour spend counts saturate at 3). Lowered only in a self-ETB trigger's CheckSVar$ (any other site refuses): as the trigger is queued the spell's count is read from the resolving entry (stackEntry.spc) and bound into the pending trigger's x; the resolution recheck reads gorge's: the bound cast-time value while the source is off the battlefield (the departure snapshot, CR 113.7a/608.2h) or the same object on it, 0 for a new object (leaving wiped the live spend, CR 400.7). Catharsis, Deceit, Emptiness, Vibrance, Wistfulness."},
	{"ex:NotOwnLibMV", "ExNotOwnLibMV", "Inside a RepeatEach over players: the mana values summed of the library cards in the resolution's remembered set that the repeated player does not own, a face-down one skipped (gorge Count$ValidLibrary Card.IsRemembered+!RememberedPlayerOwn$CardManaCost). Parker Luck."},
	{"ex:OppExtreme", "ExOppExtreme (N figure, F)", "A figure over the controller's living opponents in seat order: N's low byte OppExtAmount counts them, OppExtLife / OppExtHand / OppExtGrave / OppExtValid take the highest (OppExtLowest in N: the lowest) life total, hand size, graveyard card count, or count of battlefield permanents matching F read from that opponent's side. An empty group reads 0. Gorge: `PlayerCountOpponents$Amount`, `$Highest|LowestLifeTotal`, `$Highest|LowestCardsInHand`, `$HighestCardsInGraveyard`, `$Highest|LowestValid <spec>` (opponentGroup, playerGroupCount, lifeExtreme, playerCountExtreme). Bloodghast, Joined Researchers, Claim Jumper, Vault of Champions."},
	{"ex:StepIn", "ExStepIn (N step bits)", "1 while the game's current step is one of the kop.Step bits in N, else 0 (gorge ConditionPhases$ <list>, conditions.go: the ONE phase-name parser engine/state.ParsePhases maps the named gorge steps onto the kernel's numbering; a gorge combat-damage step sets the kernel's first-strike and regular damage bits because gorge models one combat-damage step). kgen also lowers it beside ConditionPlayerTurn$ (the conjunction of a turn test and this step test), with no third Condition*$ key. Great Train Heist."},
	{"ex:PhaseCount", "ExPhaseCount (N)", "The turn's phase ledger (gorge CombatsThisTurn, EndStepsThisTurn, counted as each BeginCombat / End step is entered): N 0 the combats begun, N 1 the finished end steps (Count$FinishedEndOfTurnsThisTurn: begun, less the one being run while in the end step). FirstCombat$ True is N 0 == 1."},
	{"trig:FirstAttack", "Tf3FirstAttack", "An Attacks trigger that fires only for an attacker not yet declared this turn (gorge FirstAttack$ True, trigmatch firstAttackOK: AttacksThisTurn == 1 at the fire): the attackers-declared mark (mechAttackedObj) is read before the declaration sets it. Aurelia the Warleader, Fear of Missing Out."},
	{"ext:PlotGrant", "OpExt ExtPlotGrant (Obj Remembered)", "Every object in the resolution's remembered set that is in exile becomes plotted (CR 702.170b-d; gorge effAlterAttribute Attributes$ Plotted, zone gate ZExile, the fold stamping PlottedTurn): a DurPlot genState.may record stamped with the current turn (StallMayPlay past maxMay), so offerPlotCasts offers its free sorcery-speed cast from exile on a later turn whether or not the card has plot, then the card's own BecomesPlotted triggers. Any other zone is a no-op. Kellan Joins Up."},
	{"ext:Hideaway", "OpExt ExtHideaway (B, C)", "C 0 (Hideaway N, CR 702.75a): the controller looks at the top B cards of their library (all of it when shorter), is asked which to exile face down (ChHideaway, gorge's KChoose hideaway_pick, library order) and puts the rest on the bottom in a random order (backward Fisher-Yates, Rand(i+1); none for one card); the exiled card is linked to the source's incarnation (genState.links with the linkHide bit; a full table first drops the links of departed sources, StallLinks). C 1 (Defined$ ExiledWith, Optional$, WithoutManaCost$): the linked card is offered as a free cast (ChGenCastFree); a land is played at once if its controller is the active player with a land play left (gorge effPlay, beginPlay). gorge keys the link on the object id alone, so a source that left and returned still sees the card; the kernel follows CR 400.7. Collector's Cage."},
	{"ext:CounterLose", "OpExt ExtCounterLose (Obj, C)", "Counter the stack ability in target slot Obj; if its source is still the same artifact, creature or planeswalker on the battlefield it loses all abilities (host-bound LoseAbilities override C) for as long as the resolving source stays on the battlefield (gorge Counter RememberCountered$ + Effect RemoveAllAbilities$ AsLongAsInPlay). Tishana's Tidebinder."},
	{"ext:TwoPilesSac", "OpExt ExtTwoPilesSac (Obj, F)", "The resolving controller separates the battlefield permanents matching F that the player Obj controls into two piles (ChGenPileSplit: a permanent per pick, AkDone-closed, picking them all ends it; a one-permanent pool poses no split), that player picks one (ChGenPileChoose: 0 the picks, 1 the rest) and sacrifices it (fireSacAll, leaveAll; gorge effTwoPiles battlefield arm + SacrificeAll IsRemembered, cr-twopiles-battlefield-validcards). Pile A rides genState.sacM. Liliana of the Veil."},
	{"ext:Endure", "OpExt ExtEndure (Obj, B, C)", "The object Obj endures N, N the PA of override C read once (N <= 0 does nothing, CR 701.63b): on the battlefield its controller chooses (ChGenEndure: 0 N +1/+1 counters through the AddCounter replacements, 1 a w_x_x_spirit token B for them set to N/N by override C, permanently); gone, the resolving controller gets the Spirit with no ask. More than one mint (a token doubler) stalls StallEndureN (gorge effEndure, CR 701.63a). The TDM Endure carriers."},
	{"ext:DistCounters", "OpExt ExtDistCounters (B total, F pool)", "Distribute B +1/+1 counters (the dying source's last-known counters) among creatures the resolving controller picks, no targets (gorge putCounterPickDistribute; Vastwood Hydra): one pick at a time from the pool matching F (seat 0 first, entry order), at least one and at most min(B, pool size), Done after the first; the counters then go round-robin in pick order, the earlier picks taking the remainder. A pool of one takes all B unasked, an empty pool or B of 0 asks nothing; a window past 24 stalls StallLook. dirac/ctr_distpick.go."},
	{"ext:DividedCounters", "OpExt ExtDividedCounters (C target slot N)", "Put the triggering source's last-known +1/+1 counters (X, the trigger entry's LKI) on the objects of target slot N as the controller divided them while putting the trigger on the stack: the slot (TargetSpec.Divide = DivLKIP1P1) takes 0..X targets, each at least 1, the division asked after the targets when there are two or more (more than eight stalls StallXTgt); one target takes all X unasked; a target illegal at resolution loses its share (gorge cr-dies-trigger-divided-counters-lki; CR 601.2d, 603.10a). Quirion Beastcaller. Constant-total form: the slot has Divide = N (a literal 2..8) and 1..N targets; the total is N, divided the same way, one target takes all N (Biogenic Upgrade, Glint Weaver). Any-number forms: TargetMin$ 0 makes the literal-N slot 0..N (no target is castable and resolves putting nothing; Picnic Ruiner's Stolen Goodies), and a spell's paid {X} (CounterNum$, TargetMax$ and DividedAsYouChoose$ all one SVar Count$xPaid, P1P1) lowers a TgfBoundsV 0..X slot with Divide = kop.DivMaxV (254): the total is the slot's evaluated maximum, more than eight stalls StallXTgt (Elusive Otter's Grove's Bounty; the literal carriers are Storm the Seedcore, Verdurous Gearhulk, Jugan, the Rising Star and Myojin of Towering Might). Only a root target declaration is lifted: the ability chain's head at depth 1, or the chosen mode's head (Abzan Charm), because gorge divides at announcement and a `SubAbility$` body divides at resolution, so Rhino, Terrible Trampler's enters trigger stays refused."},
	{"ext:ManaChoice", "OpExt ExtManaChoice (B amount, C colour mask | 0x100 for Any, F restriction)", "A loyalty ability's resolving Mana effect over a colour choice (CR 605.1a; gorge effects.askManaChoice): Produced$ Combo <colours> with a constant Amount$ N asks the controller one colour per mana (ChGenManaChoice, mode = W U B R G = 0..4; gorge poses one multi-select of N over the colours repeated per unit), Produced$ Any asks one colour for all N (C bit 8). Each pick adds its mana to the pool at once. `F != 0` (a resolving DB$ Mana's RestrictValid$ Spell.<spec> over Produced$ Combo, CR 106.6; gorge effMana) adds each pick as restricted mana through `addManaRestr` (State.rb; `genPrep.restrF` registers F, `anyMultiR` lets the colours differ; StallRestrSrc past the batches the pool holds); Produced$ Any with F stays refused by kgen. Chandra, Hope's Beacon; Desolation of Smaug."},
	{"ext:LibSweep", "OpExt ExtLibSweep (F)", "Every battlefield permanent matching F (as the resolving controller; Teferi uses ...TargetedPlayerCtrl) leaves for its owner's library: seat 0's battlefield, then seat 1's, one departure batch; each owner's cards that reached the library sit on top in move order (gorge libraryOrderPlacement), then each owner that received a card, a token included, in order of first placement, shuffles its library (gorge effChangeZoneAll Shuffle$ True, changeZoneAllShuffleLibraries); nothing moved, nothing shuffles. Teferi, Temporal Pilgrim."},
	{"ext:TokenPT", "OpExt ExtTokenPT (C)", "Right BEFORE an Ex-form CreateToken: reads override C's P/T (its PA/TA) first, runs that CreateToken in place, then sets the one token it minted (the last mint) to those values as a permanent layer-7b set stamped at the mint (gorge effects/token.go TokenPower$/TokenToughness$, CR 111.4, 613.4b). No mint does nothing; more than one (a token doubler) stalls StallTokenPT. Unwilling Vessel, The Skullspore Nexus, Tumbleweed Rising, Dance of the Tumbleweeds, Abzan Monument."},
	{"ext:CopyNamed", "OpExt ExtCopyNamed (B.N named card's CardID, C CopyFlags byte | exception override+1 << 8)", "CopyPermanent DefinedName$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go: the source is a card of the compiled card universe named by the ability, not an object): the resolving controller creates one token that is a copy of that card (its printed face, CR 707.2), through the CreateToken replacements and entry as an object's copy is. B.N is the table token the named card rides as (kgen's copy-by-name key; the matchup remaps it to its CardID), C packs the CopyFlags byte (TokenTapped$ is CpTapped; the AtEOT$ and RememberTokens$ riders are the same flags; no PumpKeywords$) with the copy exceptions' override index+1 (at most 255) in the byte above, read as OpCopyAsTokenEx reads them. The source names no object, so the copy has no template (no face-down copy, no copy of a copy). No copy count, target, Choices$ or counters (kgen refuses them beside DefinedName$); a name gorge's universe does not hold makes gorge copy nothing, so kgen emits no instruction for it. An Aura, an as-enters choice or a clone election stalls rather than ask. A matchup holding a card-name chooser beside the copier is refused (the chooser narrows gorge's name universe). Mutable Explorer's tapped Mutavault."},
	{"ext:CopyPicked", "OpExt ExtCopyPicked (Obj the picked card, B.N CopyFlags | CopyAttacking, C copy exceptions)", "CopyPermanent Choices$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go, the supportsChoice arm): the resolving controller creates one token copy of the object the preceding OpChooseCard picked (RefChosen), read as OpCopyAsTokenEx reads Obj, B.N and C. kgen lowers the mandatory one-pick over the battlefield filter as that OpChooseCard (one KChoose posed even for a single candidate, none for no candidate) and refuses a copy exception, copy count, pump, remember, target, Defined$ or counters beside it. CopyAttacking (B.N bit 14, TokenAttacking$ True in the controller's own attack trigger): the token enters attacking the opponent (gorge copyAttackRider: players only, so no planeswalker or battle defender and no ask); CpTapped enters it tapped. Nothing picked makes no copy, but the AtEOT$ rider's delayed trigger is still registered (CpSacAtEndDly, CpExileAtEnd; gorge scheduleAtEOTNone, CR 603.7) and does nothing at the end step. An Aura, an as-enters choice or a clone election stalls rather than ask. Calamity, Galloping Inferno."},
	{"ext:CopyTokenCtr", "OpExt ExtCopyTokenCtr (Obj source, B amount, C counter kind)", "CopyPermanent WithCountersType$ / WithCountersAmount$ (gorge effects/copypermanent.go, entryWithCounters): the token copy of Obj enters with B counters of kind C, put through the counter replacements as part of the token's own entry (CR 122.6, 614.1c), not after it; counters are not copiable (CR 707.2), so the source's own are never copied. The amount is read once for the resolution (CR 608.2h: Ochre Jelly's TriggerRemembered$CardCounters.P1P1/HalfDown reads the dead Jelly's last known counters, the delayed program's LKI); B <= 0 is a plain copy, and a token doubler's extra copies each get the counters. No copy exceptions, CopyFlags or NumCopies$ (kgen refuses them beside the rider); an Aura, an as-enters choice or a clone election stalls rather than dropping the counters. Ochre Jelly, A-Ochre Jelly, Littjara Mirrorlake."},
	{"ext:Recruit", "OpExt ExtRecruit", "The Hobbit's Recruit action (gorge effRecruit, DB$ Recruit): the resolving controller draws a card, then discards a card (one pick in hand order, ChRecruitDiscard, CanonKind discard; no ask when the hand holds one card, nothing when empty), then creates one 1/1 white Human Soldier token only if a nonland card was discarded. Touches no remembered set. Esgaroth Garrison, Great Gilded Boat, Lake-town Lookout, Long Lake Nuisance, Patient Instructor, Sound the Trumpets, The Mountain-king's Return, The Queen of Dale."},
	{"ext:Cumulative", "OpExt ExtCumulative (C the instructions to skip when the source is gone)", "The head of a cumulative upkeep trigger's body (CR 702.24a; Mystic Remora): the source, if it is still the permanent that triggered on the battlefield, gets an age counter through the ordinary counter placement (an AddCounter replacement applies, as gorge's CounterChange emit); if it is gone the next C instructions (the payment and the sacrifice) are skipped. The UnlessPaid after it charges its generic cost once per age counter now on the source, as the trigger's own pay-or-decline ask (gorge cumulative_pay / cumulative_sac, canonically trigger_cost_pay / trigger_cost_decline), and the Sacrifice of the source behind it runs on a decline. Only a plain generic cost lowers; any other cumulative upkeep cost refuses. dirac/trig_cumulative.go."},
	{"ext:NumTimes", "OpExt ExtNumTimes (A unit generic, B packed unit pips, C max, Skip the decline jump)", "A printed trigger's own \"pay {unit} up to N times\" announcement (gorge triggeredCostNumTimesAsk): the controller announces 0..m, m the most repetitions (up to AnnounceMax$ N) whose total the potential mana covers, kept as the resolution's X; 0 declines and skips the rest of the body. The IfPaid that follows charges the unit X times. With no repetition payable nothing is asked and the IfPaid poses its decline-only ask. Tranquil Frillback."},
	{"ext:ChooseName", "OpExt ExtChooseName", "An as-enters nonland card-name choice, the first instruction of an enters program (CR 614.12, 201.4; gorge's ETB NameCard, Defined$ You, ValidCards$ Card.nonLand): the entering permanent's controller chooses the name of one real nonland card of the matchup (a ChGenName decision, mode = the card's CardID, Table.NameCards ascending, gorge's sorted name list over the same cards), asked as the colour choice is, and the answer is kept in the permanent's chosen byte as that CardID (a permanent that left holds nothing, CR 400.7). A matchup holding a multi-face card beside a name chooser is refused when it is built, and the pool table plays the chooser inert when it holds a multi-face card or a nonland card with a CardID of 255 or more. An activation is matched on the source's printed name, so a copy of a named card or a face-down source would differ from gorge, which reads the current name. Read by a Tf4NamedCast SpellCast line. Kai Winn, Faithless Leader. B = 3 offers only the nonland names among the hands of the seats still in the game but the chooser (Alhammarret, High Arbiter: ETB RevealHand Player.Opponent | RememberRevealed, NameCard ChooseFromDefinedCards$ Remembered, Cleanup; the reveal is public and poses no decision), and poses no ask at all when no nonland card was shown, as gorge poses none for an empty set; the CantBeCast B&CantCastNamed read compares the cast card with the answer."},
	{"ext:EachDamage", "OpExt ExtEachDamage (F, B, C)", "Every battlefield permanent matching F (seat 0 first, entry order; read once) -- or, with damager target slots in C's high byte (a bit per slot), the objects of those slots legal as the resolution started, in pick order, still on the battlefield and matching F when set -- deals B damage to the object in Ref C's low byte (a target, or Self), B = 0 meaning each damager's own power (Count$CardPower), in one damage batch whose hits name their own sources: replacement, prevention, deathtouch and lifelink per source, lifelink gained once per source, damage triggers after (gorge effEachDamage, DefinedDamagers$ Valid <filter>, ParentTarget or a one-slot Targeted). A Targeted union over two or more slots, EachToItself$, ToEachOther$, ValidCards$ and player recipients refuse. Case of the Gateway Express, Moonlight Hunt; Common Goal, Band Together."},
	{"ext:DmgMark", "OpExt ExtDmgMark (Obj the damaged player)", "An Effect's `Event$ DamageDone | ValidSource$ Card,Emblem | ValidTarget$ Player.IsRemembered,Permanent.ControlledBy Player.IsRemembered` replacement whose body doubles the damage (`ReplaceCount$DamageAmount/Twice`), Duration$ UntilYourNextTurn, RememberObjects$ TriggeredTarget (gorge replacement_damage.go reads the captured players): the resolving controller marks the player in Obj, one genState.dmk bit per (controller, player), and every damage event to that player or a permanent they control is doubled once per live mark; the controller's marks end at the cleanup before their next turn. The same controller marking the same player again while it is live stalls (StallDmgMark); an event the mark and another damage replacement both match stalls (StallDmgMarkOrder: gorge asks the CR 616.1 order, which the mark has no object candidate for). Lightning, Army of One."},
	{"ext:PreventDamageScope", "OpExt ExtPreventDamageScope", "All damage that would be dealt this turn to the resolving controller and/or the creatures they control (C bits kop.PrevScope*), optionally only by creature sources on the battlefield, combat and noncombat (gorge effEffect's bodyless DamageDone Prevent$ replacement in the Command zone): one more genState.prevCol record per resolution, each its own CR 616.1 order candidate (three a turn; a fourth stalls StallPrevCol). A high op (kop/ops.go). Eerie Interference, The Needs of the Many, Summon: Alexander."},
	{"ext:TurnRepl", "OpExt ExtTurnRepl (C kop.TurnReplExileOpp or TurnReplPlusCreatureCtr)", "An Effect's until-end-of-turn replacement over a player's side of the board. C=TurnReplExileOpp: `DB$ Effect | ReplacementEffects$` with one `Event$ Moved | ValidLKI$ Creature.OppCtrl | Origin$ Battlefield | Destination$ Graveyard` body `DB$ ChangeZone | Defined$ ReplacedCard | Origin$ Battlefield | Destination$ Exile` -- every creature an opponent of the controller controls that would die this turn is exiled instead, one that enters after the Effect resolved included (a scope record in the kernel's exile-instead table, read by dieZone beside the per-object marks; competing with another exile-instead effect it stalls StallReplLeave). C=TurnReplPlusCreatureCtr: one `Event$ AddCounter | ValidCard$ Creature.YouCtrl+inZoneBattlefield | ValidCounterType$ P1P1` body `DB$ ReplaceCounter | ValidCounterType$ P1P1 | ChooseCounter$ True | Amount$ Y` with `Y: ReplaceCount$CounterNum/Plus.1` -- one more +1/+1 counter on a creature the controller controls, a per-player count apart from ExtCounterPlusEOT's (it is one more plus candidate in the CR 616.1 order ask beside Boimler's and a doubler's). Both end at cleanup. Malicious Eclipse, Prairie Dog."},
	{"ext:CounterPlusEOT", "OpExt ExtCounterPlusEOT", "Until end of turn, if one or more counters would be put on a permanent the resolving controller controls, that many plus one of each of those kinds are put on it instead (Brad Boimler, Eager Ensign's tap-triggered `DB$ Effect | ReplacementEffects$` with one `Event$ AddCounter | ActiveZones$ Battlefield | ValidCard$ Permanent.YouCtrl+inZoneBattlefield` body whose `DB$ ReplaceCounter | ChooseCounter$ True | Amount$ X` has `X: ReplaceCount$CounterNum/Plus.1`; gorge effEffect's AddCounter replacement with no ValidCounterType$, so every kind matches, rules/replacement_match.go). A per-player count in genState.plusCtr, one per activation, set by the resolution and cleared at cleanup; it applies through the ordinary counter-replacement path, so it is its own CR 616.1 order candidate against a doubler (both stall StallReplCtr) and the effect's ActiveZones$ gate is not consulted after it resolves, even if the source leaves. Only the exact shape lowers; every other Effect+AddCounter shape keeps its named refusal. Brad Boimler, Eager Ensign."},
	{"ext:PreventColor", "OpExt ExtPreventColor", "The resolving controller chooses a colour (ChGenColor, all five); all damage sources of that colour would deal this turn is prevented, combat and noncombat (gorge effChooseColor, then effEffect's bodyless DamageDone Prevent$ replacement over ValidSource$ Card.ChosenColor): a genState.prevCol record per resolution (three a turn; a fourth stalls StallPrevCol), each its own CR 616.1 order candidate, the same card resolving again moving its records to the new colour (gorge reads the card's live ChosenColor). A high op (kop/ops.go). Prismatic Strands."},
	{"op:Goad", "OpGoad (Obj, or F with Obj RefNone)", "The battlefield permanent Obj, or every battlefield permanent matching F (Defined$ Valid, seat 0 first), is goaded by the resolving controller until that player's next turn (CR 701.15; gorge effGoad, the default UntilYourNextTurn duration): genState.goad[p] slot bits, cleared as p's turn begins (gorge TurnChange expireTurnGoads) and when it leaves. A goaded creature attacks each combat if able, and only the defending player (its planeswalkers and battles satisfy no goad, gorge attackOffers' CR 508.1d filter). A high op (kop/ops.go). Goblin Racketeer, Taunting Kobold, Disrupt Decorum."},
	{"op:Saddle", "OpSaddle (Obj, or a target/trigger object)", "The battlefield permanent Obj becomes saddled (CR 702.171b; gorge effAlterAttribute Saddled: Object.SaddledTurn): perm.cseen bit cseenSaddled, cleared as the next turn begins (gorge TurnChange) and gone when it leaves (a new permanent). Read by F2Saddled. Obj is any object ref the op takes: the source (the Saddle expansion's AB$ AlterAttribute Defined$ Self Attributes$ Saddled SorcerySpeed$ True), a target (Guidelight Matrix's ValidTgts$ Mount.YouCtrl, Alacrian Armory's up-to-one Mount/Vehicle), or the trigger object (Kolodin, Triumph Caster's Defined$ TriggeredCard); a target no longer legal at resolution does nothing. C = 1 is a Case's Solved designation (AlterAttribute Solved, read by PredSolved; never cleared as a turn begins)."},
	{"op:Monstrosity", "OpMonstrosity (A n)", "The permanent becomes monstrous (CR 701.37; gorge effPutCounter's MonstrositySet arm): if it is not already monstrous, n +1/+1 counters through OpPutCounter's path (the counter replacements and CounterAddedOnce), then the monstrous designation, then TrigBecomeMonstrous with amount n. n <= 0 places no counters and never marks; an already-monstrous permanent does nothing. Keepsake Gorgon, Polukranos, World Eater."},
	{"op:Support", "OpSupport (A n, C counter kind | 0x100 other)", "The resolving controller supports n (CR 701.41a; gorge putCounterSupport): one counter of the kind on each of up to n creatures of any controller (other than the source for a permanent's ability, any creature for an instant or sorcery), an any-number pick (ChGenBolster, gorge's counter_pick, closed by Done or the n-th pick; a 17th pick stalls StallProlif); nothing when n <= 0 or no creature is eligible. Expedition Raptor, Shoulder to Shoulder. Remove form (C&0x200; RemoveCounter Choices$, gorge removeCounterChoose): the same pick over the battlefield permanents matching F (either controller; no Other rule), each pick losing one counter of the kind (none removed from a pick holding none); C&0x400 exact (A picks, Done withheld, no ask when eligible <= A: every eligible one loses a counter), otherwise an any-number pick (A = 16); C&0x800 RememberAmount$: the removed total joins the remembered count (RememberedCount). Dyadrine, Synthesis Amalgam; Garnet, Princess of Alexandria."},
	{"op:Incubate", "OpIncubate (Obj player, A n, B times, C token)", "Player Obj incubates A (CR 701.53a-b; gorge effIncubate): B times (min 1) create the Incubator token C under Obj -- token doublers apply, each mint its own TokenCreate -- and put A +1/+1 counters on every mint through the counter-replacement path (CounterAddedOnce); A < 0 creates nothing, A = 0 still mints with no counter event. The counters go after entry, as gorge (CR 701.53a says the token enters with them; noted in crcoverage 701.53a-b). Obj is the controller unless Defined$ TargetedController (Excise the Imperfect). Bloated Processor, Chrome Host Seedshark, Glissa, Herald of Predation, Glistening Dawn, Ichor Drinker."},
	{"op:Manifest", "OpManifest (Obj player, A n, B.N flags)", "Player Obj manifests n cards from the top of their library (CR 701.40a; gorge effManifest): each is the real card moved face down (not a token) and marked manifested, so it is a 2/2 colourless creature with no name or abilities and dies as itself; a full battlefield stalls. The manifested card turns face up for its mana cost when it is a creature card (CR 701.40b) and for its printed Morph/Megamorph/Disguise cost as an alternative (CR 701.40c-d). n <= 0 or an empty library does nothing. B.N = CfManifestRemembered (Defined$ Remembered: manifest each card of the remembered set from where it sits, under the resolving controller, in set order; a battlefield card is skipped; Obj/A unused; Write into Being). Cloudform, Reality Shift, Whisperwood Elemental, Soul Summons, Lightform, Rageform."},
	{"op:Cloak", "OpCloak (Obj player, A n, B.N flags)", "Player Obj cloaks n cards from the top of their library (CR 701.58a; gorge effCloak): face down with ward {2} and marked cloaked, so the same turn-face-up procedures apply (CR 701.58b-d). B.N = CfTapped (enter tapped, the MoveZone-then-Tap pair), CfShuffle (gorge's pile shuffle: a no-op, no library shuffle and no RNG draw), CfRemember (RememberCloaked$: each cloaked card joins the remembered set), CfChosen (cloak the preceding OpChooseCard pick from where it sits, under the resolving controller -- the Choices$ hand shape, gorge's face_down_choice pick), CfCloakCtrl (Obj names only the library's owner; the cards enter under the resolving controller -- the ValidLibrary Card.TopLibrary+OwnedBy shape, gorge's cloak(t.Obj, c.Controller), CR 110.2a), CfCloakRemembered (Defined$ Remembered: cloak each card of the remembered set from where it sits, under the resolving controller, in set order; a battlefield card is skipped; Obj/A unused; Expose the Culprit, Sleuth Instructor). Cryptic Coat, Vannifar Evolved Enigma, Etrata Deadly Fugitive."},
	{"op:ManifestDread", "OpManifestDread (Obj player, A n, B.N flags)", "Player Obj manifests dread n times (CR 701.62a; gorge effManifestDread): look at the top two cards, manifest one (the player's ask; one card left manifests without one) and put the other into its owner's graveyard. B.N&CfRemember: RememberManifested$ True, each manifested card joins the remembered set. Zimone Mystery Unraveler, Unwanted Remake, Killer's Mask, Valgavoth's Onslaught, Moldering Gym."},
	{"op:PumpAllEach", "OpPumpAllEach (F filter, A/B amounts, C keywords, Obj bits)", "Each creature matching F gets +A/+B until end of turn and the keywords C (gorge effPump over a multi-object Defined$ Valid <filter>: the set read once at resolution, CR 611.2c, seat 0 first). Obj&PumpEachPower (NumAtt$ Double): A is each creature's OWN derived power, Obj&PumpEachTough (NumDef$ Double): B its own toughness (gorge numForObjectText; CR 701.10a-c). An amount outside the end-of-turn pump's int8 range stalls (StallPT) rather than wrapping. Roar of Endless Song, Unnatural Growth, Double Trouble, Voltstorm Angel (A)."},
	{"op:DoubleCountersAll", "OpDoubleCountersAll (F filter, C kind)", "OpDoubleCounters (CR 701.10e; gorge effMultiplyCounter) on each battlefield permanent matching F in battlefield order, seat 0 first; C is the counter kind, 255 every kind. Bristly Bill, Spine Sower; Kalonian Hydra (A)."},
	{"op:MayShuffleMove", "OpMayShuffleMove (Obj player, C slot, A may)", "The player Obj (the effect's controller; RefNone when A.N=0) may (A.N=1, gorge objectPathMayShuffle) or must (A.N=0) put the legal chosen cards of target slot C on top of their owners' libraries in pick order (the first chosen ends on top, gorge libraryOrderPlacementAt), then shuffles each distinct owner's library once in referent order (gorge objectPathShuffleOwners); a slot with no chosen card does nothing and asks nothing. Cards chosen but illegal are not moved and the shuffle still happens (CR 701.24c). Krosan Reclamation, Oracle of Tragedy, Put Away, Cathartic Parting, Wand of Vertebrae."},
	{"op:Transform", "OpTransform (Obj)", "Obj turns to its card's next face (CardDef.Faces[(Face+1)%n]; gorge effSetState Mode$ Transform: FlipFace to (FaceIdx+1)%faces): the same object, counters, damage, attachments, tapped state and summoning sickness stay; its subscriptions, statics and grants follow the new face. A transforming-DFC token (FaceTransform, the Incubator token) also restamps the layer timestamp on the battlefield (CR 613.7g); a modal layout does not. CR 701.27a: only a permanent transforms, so a source removed in response is left untouched in its graveyard or exile (gorge added the same zone gate; Forge SetStateEffect and XMage skip a non-battlefield object). kgen lowers Mode$ Transform with Defined$ Self (or no Defined$ and no ValidTgts$, gorge's Self fallback) on a modal layout or a transforming-DFC token: Monica Rambeau and the Incubator token are the lifted cards; the other SPM Modal transformers are refused on their back faces and non-token transforming DFCs stay the faces class."},
	{"f2:Saddled", "F2Saddled", "A battlefield permanent that is saddled (gorge IsSaddled: SaddledTurn == the turn); never off the battlefield. 'Whenever this creature attacks while saddled'."},
	{"f2:Sneaked", "F2Sneaked", "The spell was cast for its sneak cost (CR 702.190a; gorge filter.go 'sneaked' reads CastFlags&FlagSneaked). Read on a SpellCast self trigger's stack filter (selfCastFilterOK), as Count$ValidStack Card.Self+sneaked (ExSneaked), and on a battlefield permanent through the arena's mechSneaked mark (kw_sneak.go); any other zone is refused."},
	{"f2:Unblocked", "F2Unblocked", "An attacking permanent with no blocker recorded (CR 509.1h; gorge filter.go 'unblocked': IsAttacking and no BlockedBy, a blocker that left still counting). Battlefield reads only (flags2Perm); every card-zone matcher fails closed. K:Ninjutsu's Return<1/Creature.YouCtrl+attacking+unblocked> cost."},
	{"f2:TgtPlayerCtrl", "F2TgtPlayerCtrl", "A battlefield permanent whose controller is a player target of the current stack entry, the resolving one or the one being built (CR 115.10; gorge TargetedPlayerCtrl, matchTargetedPlayerCtrl: no bound player target is false). On the battlefield it reads the controller; off it (a card matcher) the same bit reads the card's OWNER, kgen's `OwnedBy Targeted` alias (Cruel Calculations' Count$ThisTurnEntered_Graveyard_from_Library_Card.OwnedBy Targeted; never on the battlefield or stack). Villainous Wrath's Count$Valid Creature.TargetedPlayerCtrl."},
	{"f2:DefendingCtrl", "F2DefendingCtrl", "A battlefield permanent the defending player controls: two-player, any player but the active one; past two seats, the attack event's defending seat bound as the trigger is queued (or checked, for an IsPresent$), stalling (StallDefenderPW) with none (CR 506.2, 508.5; gorge ControlledBy TriggeredDefendingPlayer, the Attacks trigger's DefendingPlayer). kgen lowers it only in an Attacks trigger's body; on the battlefield it reads the controller, off it the card's OWNER (`OwnedBy TriggeredDefendingPlayer`, Chorale of the Void's graveyard target). Spring Splasher, Thunder Lasso, Captain America's Shield."},
	{"cost:TapHost", "CostTapHost", "Tap the permanent that granted this ability (Fishing Pole's granted ability: '{1}, {T}, tap Fishing Pole')."},
	// --- fields ---
	{"filter:Owner", "Filter.Owner", "Owner relative to the controller, on the battlefield (off it, Ctrl already means owner)."},
	{"filter:Sub", "Filter.Sub / NotSub", "Must / must not have subtype index Sub-1 of the matchup table (NoSubtype = 255: a subtype nothing in the matchup has: Sub never matches, NotSub always passes)."},
	{"filter:Or", "Filter.Or", "Alternatives: matches if this filter OR Filters[Or] matches (chains point to earlier filters)."},
	{"filter:PredV", "Filter.PredV", "The bound of a *V predicate."},
	{"cond:Promised", "CondPromised", "The gift was promised (CR 702.174): the resolving or building entry's sfPromised flag, or, read by an enter trigger with no entry, the spell putting the source onto the battlefield. Gorge: ConditionPresent$ Card.Self+PromisedGift with ConditionZone$ Stack, and a self enter trigger's ValidCard$ Card.Self+PromisedGift (checked only when it triggers)."},
	{"f2:Kicked", "F2Kicked", "The object was kicked (Goblin Bushwhacker, Sun-Blessed Healer ETB)."},
	{"f2:CastByYou", "F2CastByYou", "The permanent was cast by its controller (Nine-Lives Familiar)."},
	{"f2:EnteredThisTurn", "F2EnteredThisTurn", "Put into its current zone this turn (Abyssal Harvester: a creature card put into a graveyard this turn)."},
	{"f2:ChosenType", "F2ChosenType", "Has the source's chosen creature type (Banner of Kinship)."},
	{"f2:ChosenColor", "F2ChosenColor", "Is the source's chosen colour (Heraldic Banner)."},
	{"f2:Remembered", "F2Remembered / F2NotRemembered", "In / not in the remembered set."},
	{"f2:ChosenCard", "F2ChosenCard / F2NotChosenCard", "Is / isn't a chosen card."},
	{"f2:AttachedToT0", "F2AttachedToT0", "Attached to target 0's object (Fiery Annihilation's Equipment); `AttachedTo Targeted` is the same referent (gorge attachedToReferentCodes; Light of Judgment)."},
	{"f2:TargetedBy", "F2TargetedBy", "Targeted by the resolving ability."},
	{"f2:SameNameAsSource", "F2SameNameAsSource", "Retired: kgen no longer emits it. Every named<X>, the source's own printed name included (Hare Apparent), lowers to Pred = PredNamed, PredN = X's pool entry, -1 = no such object here."},
	{"f2:WithFlying", "F2WithFlying / F2WithoutFlying", "Has / lacks flying (current keywords)."},
	{"f2:Emblem", "F2Emblem", "An emblem (damage sources: Niv-Mizzet's 'source you control')."},
	{"f2:Basic", "F2Basic", "Has the basic supertype (land searches)."},
	{"f2:Legendary", "F2Legendary", "Has the legendary supertype, with a type head (Creature.Legendary)."},
	{"f2:WasDamaged", "F2WasDamaged", "An object dealt positive damage this turn (State.g.dmgTurn). Gorge `wasDealtDamageThisTurn` (Object.WasDealtDamageThisTurn, reset at TurnChange and on a battlefield entry, CR 400.7): the kernel records the hit on dmgPerm/dmgCounters/infectCounters, so it survives a zone change and a regeneration like gorge's. Sold Out's SkipIf on the exiled target reads it off the battlefield; Downwind Ambusher."},
	{"f2:NotTriggerObj", "F2NotTriggerObj", "Is not the resolving (or building) ability's triggering object; an unbound referent fails closed. Gorge `NotDefinedTriggeredCard` (also `NotDefinedTriggeredAttacker`, in an Attacks trigger's body: Saw) (effects/filter.go notDefinedTriggerReferent). Jackdaw Savior."},
	{"f2:SharesColorRem", "F2SharesColorRem", "Shares a colour with another object in the remembered set, both read from their printed faces; colourless shares nothing; fails closed on the battlefield. Gorge: `SharesColorWithOther Remembered` (effects/filter_attachment.go sharesColorWithOther), Sphinx's Tutelage's repeat gate over the milled cards."},
	{"tgt:MinMax", "TargetSpec.Min/Max", "The slot takes Min..Max distinct objects (all matching Filter); ops on RefTargetN act on each. Decision: one pick per object, stop allowed once Min reached."},
	{"tgt:Kicked", "TargetSpec.MinKicked/MaxKicked + TgfKickedRange", "When the spell is kicked the slot takes MinKicked..MaxKicked objects (255 = any number) instead (Divine Resilience)."},
	{"tgt:Gift", "TargetSpec.Min/Max/MinKicked/MaxKicked + TgfGiftRange", "Gift: the slot takes Min..Max objects, or MinKicked..MaxKicked when the gift was promised, both literal (0..0: no target; Wear Down one or two, Long River's Pull's creature-spell or any-spell slot). The cast is offered when every mandatory slot can be announced under either election; an election whose count can't be met reverses the cast (gorge: 'cast aborted: no legal target'). With TgfAtResolution the slot is chosen as the spell resolves, only under the election that gives it one object (Into the Flood Maw)."},
	{"tgf:Distinct", "TgfDistinct", "The slot's objects must differ from every earlier slot's (Drakuseth's 'other targets')."},
	{"tgf:SameController", "TgfSameController", "All of the slot's objects share a controller (graveyard cards: an owner — 'from a single graveyard', Soul-Shackled Zombie)."},
	{"tgf:DiffController", "TgfDiffController", "The slot's objects have different controllers (Run Away Together)."},
	{"tgf:SharedCrType", "TgfSharedCrType", "All of the slot's objects share a creature type (a changeling has every one); a mandatory 2-object slot offers a first pick only with a partner, and the slot's maximum is capped at the most candidates holding one type. At resolution the objects that no longer share one with the kept ones are dropped (CR 608.2b). Gorge `TargetsWithSameCreatureType$` (effects/params/targets.go, decision.SetPropAdmits, rules/setprops.go narrowSetProps). Unbury (graveyard); the battlefield form is Secret Tunnel."},
	{"tgf:DistinctNames", "TgfDistinctNames", "No two of the slot's objects share a name; the maximum is capped at the distinct names among the candidates. Gorge `TargetsWithDifferentNames$` (decision.SetPropDistinct, SetPropCapacity). Behold the Sinister Six!."},
	{"tgf:MaxTotalMV", "TgfMaxTotalMV + TargetSpec.MaxMV", "The slot's graveyard cards have a total mana value of at most MaxMV (a literal; the slot's minimum is 0). Gorge `MaxTotalTargetCMC$` (rules/target_modes.go totalCMCCappedCandidates, Decision.MaxSum). Scout for Survivors, Joshua, Phoenix's Dominant."},
	{"tgf:Decl", "TgfDecl", "A spell's copy target declaration: the slot is declared by the spell's root node or a chosen charm mode's head (gorge rules/target_modes.go copyTargetDeclarations). Read only for a spell copy whose controller may choose new targets (OpCopySpell C&1)."},
	{"tgf:DeclSub", "TgfDeclSub", "A spell's copy target declaration declared by a SubAbility$ link (not the root): a copy whose controller may choose new targets (OpCopySpell C&1) asks it after the root's declaration, one ask per link in chain order, offering the link's own cast-time targets first (CR 707.10c; gorge rules/target_modes.go copyChainDeclarations)."},
	{"tgf:BoundsV", "TgfBoundsV + TargetSpec.MinV/MaxV", "The slot's bounds are values, evaluated as the slot is announced (gorge rules/target_legal.go resolvedTargetBoundsWithGift): MinV is literal 0 (the slot is optional), MaxV a ValueRef (X paid, a count of permanents, the trigger amount; Rabid Attack, Divergent Equation, Heroic Feast, Prismabasher, Coveted Falcon). A resolved 0 asks nothing; a maximum above the candidates ends in the done-only ask a constant slot has. A copy re-evaluates them (copyBounds). Zero-pick answers to a copy's declaration keep the inherited targets (gorge finishCopyTargets)."},
	{"tgt:Divide", "TargetSpec.Divide", "The total damage divided at targeting (OpDealDamageDivided)."},
	{"tgt:StackObjTrig", "TgtStackObjTrig", "A spell matching Filter, or a TRIGGERED ability on the stack (never an activated one): Counter's TargetType$ Instant,Sorcery,Triggered (gorge state.StackKindTokenOf, an OR over the tokens, rechecked at resolution). A spell is named by its object, an ability as TgtStackObj names one (StackTarget0 + its stack index). Spider-Sense."},
	{"tgt:SpellTgting", "TgtSpellTgting", "A spell other than the source whose own chosen object targets (tgt and its extra multi-object targets) include a battlefield permanent matching Filter for the chooser: Counter's TargetValidTargeting$ (gorge filterTargetValidTargeting, the OFFER only). At resolution the target rechecks as a plain spell target (still a spell on the stack): gorge does not reread the targeting clause. Fugitive Droid."},
	{"op:CounterRemMV", "OpCounter B&1 (kop.CtrRemMV)", "RememberCounteredCMC$ True: when the countered spell actually leaves the stack (not an ability, not an uncounterable spell) its mana value, announced X included (CR 202.3e), is added to the resolution's sum resCtx.remLK, which Count$RememberedNumber reads as ExRemLKIPT (N 2, beside the Sacrifice sums N 0 and 1; kgen keeps the two writers out of one program; gorge effCounter, count_body_paid.go RememberedNumber). Hurl into History. B&2 (kop.CtrRemember, RememberChanged$ True on ChangeZone Origin$ Stack Destination$ Exile with C = CtrDestExile|CtrDestMove, under an OpMayAsk MayGuardStackSpell) adds the moved spell to the resolution's remembered set just before it leaves the stack; a later gate on nothing remembered (ConditionDefined$ Remembered, ConditionCompare$ EQ0) then holds only when the controller declined. Brazen Bluff."},
	{"af:Latent", "AfLatent", "The ability is not active on the card: a delayed/reflexive program, a granted ability (Override.Grant, Static.Grant) or an emblem's ability."},
	{"af:ManaDynamic", "AfManaDynamic + ManaV", "The mana ability produces ManaV mana (Elvish Archdruid: one G per Elf you control)."},
	{"af:ManaChosen", "AfManaChosen", "Produces one mana of the source's chosen colour (Heraldic Banner)."},
	{"af:ResolveCount", "AfResolveCount", "A triggered ability whose resolutions this turn are counted (one once-per-turn record per resolution, keyed by source object and ver) for ExResolvedThisTurn. Harvestrite Host."},
	{"af:ManaChoice", "AfManaChoice", "The mana ability's colour is a choice among ManaColors (Produced$ Combo ...), not simultaneous production (the FDN gain lands, Ruby Daring Tracker)."},
	{"af:Gift", "AfGift", "A permanent's gift trigger (CR 702.174c): a self enter trigger with CondPromised (and AfCheckOnTrigger), queued after the card's own enter triggers; the gift is given (TrigGiveGift) as it is put on the stack (gorge rules/altcast.go altCostEnter, trigger_queue.go)."},
	{"af:Ninjutsu", "AfNinjutsu (ActZone hand, CostReturn, OpNinjutsu)", "The K:Ninjutsu ability (CR 702.49; gorge cards/kw_ninjutsu.go): offered from the hand only in the declare-blockers, combat-damage and end-of-combat steps (gorge ActivationPhases$; gorge's one Combat Damage step is the kernel's two), its Return<1/Creature.YouCtrl+attacking+unblocked> pick capturing the returned attacker's defender on the entry. Ninja of the Deep Hours."},
	{"af:Station", "AfStation", "The Station ability (CR 702.184a; gorge rules/station.go): an activated ability with CostSorcery and CostTapX N=1 over another untapped creature you control, canonicalised as gorge's priority special action \"station\". Its tap pick is posed before the push (gorge asks before minting the ability), always, even with one candidate (ChStation, gorge's KChoose \"station\" Min=Max=1); the picked creature is the entry's trigger object, and the program puts max(0, its power at resolution) CHARGE counters on the source (gorge stationAmount: in its new zone if it left). The stack projection's Ability is 255 (gorge's minted body has no face index)."},
	{"ab:Gate", "Ability.Gate (Ctr, N, Eq)", "A threshold gate: with `Ctr != 0` the ability exists only while the source permanent's count of `Ctr` is >= `N` (== `N` when `Eq`). A Class's level-N trigger is `Gate{CtrLevel, N-1}`, enumerated only while it holds and rechecked on resolution (unless AfCheckOnTrigger; gorge ANDs ClassBand$ into the intervening-if walk); its level-N activator is `Gate{CtrLevel, N-2, Eq}` with CostSorcery, offered only while it holds (gorge kwClass: IsPresent$ Card.Self+classLevel_EQ<N-1>). Only a printed battlefield trigger or activated ability carries one; a gated static or replacement is refused. The kernel reads it only behind prep.anyGate."},
	{"trig:GiveGift", "TrigGiveGift", "Whenever a player (Whose) gives a gift (Jolly Gerbils). No slot subscription: a gift scans the battlefield."},
	{"card:Gift", "CardDef.Gift", "K:Gift (CR 702.174a): after the push and the either-or additional cost, before every other cost and target choice, the caster may promise the opponent a gift (DkChoose/ChGenGift, gorge giftAsk); the answer is the entry's sfPromised flag."},
	{"card:Casualty", "CardDef.Casualty", "K:Casualty:<N> (CR 702.153a, fixed N >= 1; Casualty:X is refused): a second cast option (AkCastCasualty) beside the plain cast, offered while the caster controls a creature with power >= N. It asks which one to sacrifice (ChGenCasualty, before X and targets; the sacrifice settles at payment with the other costs). Paid, a trigger goes on the stack above the spell and copies it on resolution (OpCopySpell, new targets allowed)."},
	{"card:Bargain", "CardDef.Bargain", "K:Bargain (CR 702.166): the optional artifact/enchantment/token sacrifice is Casualty\u2019s sibling cast row (AkCastCasualty), offered while the caster controls an artifact or enchantment and the pool pays the plain cast; the election asks ChGenBargain (gorge\u2019s \"bargain\") and the pick settles at payment with the other costs. A completed bargained cast sets the stack entry\u2019s sfKicked (gorge FlagBargained); it queues no copy trigger. The permanent\u2019s kicked mark (g.kicked) and the resolving entry feed Count$Bargained/Count$Bargain, Card.Self+bargained and Condition$ Bargain; a spell copy clears it (CR 707.10)."},
	{"card:OptCost", "CardDef.OptCost, OptBehold", "S:Mode$ OptionalCost (CR 601.2b) with a Blight<N> or Behold<1/Type> part: the optional cast is the kicked cast (AkCast mode 1, gorge\u2019s \"optionalcost\" option), offered beside the plain cast while the part is payable and the floating pool pays it (gorge\u2019s planner prices no OptionalCost card, plain cast included); it folds the part into the cost-pick stage (behold, then blight) and sets the stack entry\u2019s sfKicked (gorge FlagOptionalCostPaid), read by Count$OptionalGenericCostPaid.<a>.<b> and Condition$ OptionalCost. Instants and sorceries only, except a CollectEvidence<N> part on a permanent spell (Crimestopper Sprite, Vitu-Ghazi Inspector): the paid flag moves to the permanent\u2019s kicked mark and the card\u2019s own self-ETB trigger reads it as Card.Self+kicked (CastSA>Collected; false once the source has left, as in gorge)."},
	{"card:Offspring", "CardDef.Offspring", "K:Offspring:<cost> (CR 702.175a): the optional additional cost is gorge's \"(offspring)\" cast option (base + offspring), the kernel's kicked cast with the cost in CardDef.Kicker (no KwKicker); paid, the entry's sfKicked moves to the permanent's kicked mark, which the expansion's enter trigger counts (Count$Valid Card.Self+kicked) to mint one CpOneOne copy."},
	{"af:CheckOnTrigger", "AfCheckOnTrigger", "The trigger's Cond is checked only when the event happens, not again on resolution (gorge NoResolvingCheck$; Courageous Goblin, Ruby)."},
	{"ab:ModeRestrict", "Ability.ModeRestrict", "A charm's ChoiceRestriction$ scope (gorge CharmEligibleModes, \"choose one that hasn't been chosen this turn / this game\"): 1 ThisTurn, 2 ThisGame; 0 none. Single-pick charms on a printed battlefield trigger or activated ability, one per card. The kernel logs each announced mode on the source slot (State.g.chPick, behind prep.anyCharmPick), drops a barred mode from the offer (build step, offer gate), removes a trigger with every mode barred (gorge removeModelessTrigger), ends the ThisTurn picks at the turn change and every pick when the slot is next entered (CR 400.7). Monument to Endurance, Breeches Eager Pillager, The Vision, Lita Little Orphan Amphibian (ThisTurn); Three Bowls of Porridge (ThisGame);."},
	{"ab:RepMax", "Ability.RepMax / RepCost / RepBudget", "A charm that may choose a mode more than once (CanRepeatModes$): RepMax[m] is the most times mode m can be chosen (CharmNum$, or the pawprint budget over the mode's price), and a nonzero entry makes stackEntry.mode a count per mode in bits.Len8(RepMax[m]) bits above the earlier modes' (kop.RepeatLayout; the byte holds eight). RepCost[m] and RepBudget are the Pawprint$ price of each mode and the charm's budget (0 = none; CR 700.2i, 107.18). Spell charms of at most four modes with 1..1 targets; the template and extra-instance target slots must fit kop.MaxTargets. The kernel asks the modes as single picks of every mode the pick count and budget still admit, plus Done at the minimum (dirac/modal_charmrepeat.go); gorge's decision is Repeatable with MaxSum over the modes' Option.Value. Cosmium Confluence, Moment of Reckoning, Season of Loss."},
	{"ab:ManaRestrict", "Ability.ManaRestrict", "The mana may be spent only on spells matching the filter (Giada: Angel spells)."},
	{"ab:CantCopy", "Ability.CantCopy", "An ability that can't be copied (CantCopy$ True; gorge SpellCopyAllowed): ExtCopyAbility naming its stack entry makes no copy, the target staying legal and the resolution going on. A table byte, not State (AbilityFlags has no free bit). Gogo, Master of Mimicry."},
	{"ab:Exhaust", "Ability.Exhaust", "An exhaust ability (CR 702.177a, Exhaust$ True; beside CostOncePerGame): the class test of trig:AbilityCast ValidSA$ Activated.Exhaust. A table byte, not State (AbilityFlags has no free bit)."},
	{"ab:Evidence", "Ability.Evidence", "CollectEvidence<N> in an activated battlefield ability's cost (CR 701.59a, 602.2b; gorge cast_targets.go evidenceAsk): N, 0 = none. After the targets and the division, before the payment, the activator picks graveyard cards (ChCostEvidence, any number; Done once the picked total mana value reaches N, all picked ends it); a graveyard that cannot reach N reverses the activation (CR 733.1, gorge offers it regardless). The picked cards are exiled at payment. A table byte, not State (CostFlags has no free bit). The same cost as a trigger's own cost is OpIfPaid with PayKind PayManaX and B.N PayBSubEvidence (the nibble is full; gorge evidenceStage: a short graveyard declines; a graveyard the threshold needs whole is exiled unasked). Forensic Researcher, Polygraph Orb (activated); Izoni, Center of the Web, Sample Collector (trigger's own)."},
	{"ab:ActZone", "Ability.ActZone", "Activate from this zone instead of the battlefield (Reassembling Skeleton from the graveyard)."},
	{"trig:Filter2", "Trigger.Filter2", "DamageDone: the damaged object must match; AttackersDeclared: the attackers counted."},
	{"trig:Cond", "Trigger.Cond", "Intervening if (CR 603.4): checked when the event happens and again on resolution (unless AfCheckOnTrigger)."},
	{"trig:Zone", "Trigger.Zone", "The source must be in this zone (Graveyard: Flamewake Phoenix; Command: emblems)."},
	{"trig:N", "Trigger.N", "AttackersDeclared: at least N attackers (Armasaur Guide: 3); CounterAddedOnce: the counter kind; SpellCast: ValidSA$ / ValidSAonCard$ `Spell.ManaSpent <op><n|X>` (CR 601.2h, 603.2), a kop.DmgGate over the cast's pool mana spent (0xff = X, the spell's PRINTED mana value, ValidSAonCard$ only) -- a fire-time filter with no resolution recheck (gorge trigmatch.spellCastMatches, ValidSAMatches case 2, spellValidSAonCardMatches over ManaSpentForCast; kernel State.spentGateOK). SpellCast reads N only under Tf2NthSpell, which the lowering refuses beside the gate."},
	{"tf3:ConvergeBound", "Tf3ConvergeBound", "ETB of the card itself: the body's Count$Converge is the entering spell's colours spent, copied into the pending trigger's x as it triggers (0 for an object that entered uncast) and read while the source is still that object on the battlefield (gorge reads c.Source live, effects/count_body_paid.go). Never with Tf2XBound or Tf2SpentBound. Sundering Archaic, Transcendent Archaic."},
	{"tf3:CastConverge", "Tf3CastConverge", "SpellCast (a battlefield listener, not the spell itself, not OrCopy): the trigger amount (ExTriggerAmount) is the triggering spell's colours spent as the trigger fires (gorge TriggerConverge, TriggeredCard$Converge). Never with Tf2CastSpent or Tf2CastSnapshot. A table holding one turns on gfSpendRd: gorge's planner prices no cast while it is on a battlefield. Magmablood Archaic."},
	{"tf3:ManaFromTreasure", "Tf3ManaFromTreasure", "SpellCast (a battlefield listener, not the spell itself, not OrCopy): the cast's payment spent mana a Treasure produced (ValidSA$ Spell.ManaFromTreasure; gorge ValidSAMatches via CastProvenanceAdmits, state.TypedTreasure). Read while the cast's build is live (a stack copy never matches); a table holding one turns on castTapOn and marks the Treasure cards. Smaug, Wicked Worm."},
	{"tf3:OrTargets", "Tf3OrTargets", "SpellCast (a battlefield listener, not the spell itself, not OrCopy, not Tf2TargetsFilter2): the cast spell matches Filter OR some target of it matches Filter2 (ValidSA$ \"Spell.X,Spell.IsTargeting Valid Y\"; gorge validSATargetingList / spellIsTargetingMatchesPtr: any object target, in any zone, read against the trigger's controller; a player target never matches). Danitha, Sword of Hope."},
	{"tf3:Static", "Tf3Static", "A SpellCast trigger whose line carries Static$ True: resolved off the stack by the trigger drain, before the CR 603.3b ordering ask (gorge engine/rules/static_trigger.go resolveStaticTriggers; kernel trig_mayplaystatic.go placeStaticTriggers) — no priority pass, no order choice. Only a body kgen proves ask-free carries the flag (no targets, no Charm, no Optional/Unless/Cost rider; the exact rider Effect shapes). Intrepid Paleontologist, Leonardo Sewer Samurai, Osteomancer Adept, Undead Sprinter, Mikey & Don."},
	{"tf3:MayPlaySrc", "Tf3MayPlaySrc", "A SpellCast trigger's ValidSA$ Spell.MayPlaySource: the cast went through a may-play permission, read off the spell's stack entry as the trigger fires (gorge ValidSAMatches reads the cast's FlagMayPlay — the flag-only approximation of Forge's host-specific MayPlaySource; a stack copy never carries it; kernel mayPlaySpell, trig_mayplaystatic.go). Mikey & Don, Party Planners; Undead Sprinter."},
	{"trigflag4", "TrigFlags4", "Trigger.Flags4 appends the single-target trigger qualifiers and Tf4NthFiltered (bit 3): a Tf2NthSpell line whose ValidCard$ turns some spells away counts the caster's cast-ring pushes that match Filter (gorge activatorCastCount). Tf4SingleTarget (bit 0): a SpellCast trigger whose cast spell's ROOT target list has exactly one target (IsSingleTarget$ True; gorge trigmatch.TargetShapeMatches reads obj.Targets, not a chained SubAbility$ link's SubTargets, and a multi-pick root slot counts every pick; kernel singleTargetOK). Tf4SingleCauseTarget (bit 1): a DamageDone trigger whose cause is the resolving spell, carrying exactly one target in total (Targets plus SubTargets) that includes the damaged creature (ValidCause$ Spell.numTargets EQ1 + TargetRelativeToCause$ Creature.targetedBy; gorge damageCauseMatches/stackCauseAdmits/targetCountAdmits; kernel singleCauseOK). Leyline of Resonance; Imodane, the Pyrohammer. Tf4CounterCell (bit 2): a CounterAddedOnce line lowered from Mode$ CounterPlayerAddedAll fires once per put action per recipient (gorge counterBatch latch); OpPutCounter and OpPutCounterAll carry B = kop.PutCtrCellFirst/PutCtrCellNext across one action's kinds. Tf4NamedCast (bit 4): a SpellCast line lowered from Mode$ SpellAbilityCast with ValidCard$ Card.NamedCard, ValidSA$ Spell,Activated and ValidActivatingPlayer$ Opponent over the source's as-enters chosen card name (ExtChooseName): it fires when an opponent casts a spell whose card is the source's chosen name (castTrigGen, castNamedOK) and when an opponent activates an ability of a source with that name (fireAbilityCast, namedActivation; a mana ability never reaches it, as in gorge); a copy of a spell is not cast and does not fire it. Kai Winn, Faithless Leader. Tf4OptTrigPlayer (bit 5): with TfOptional, a Phase trigger's OptionalDecider$ TriggeredPlayer: the CR 603.5 resolution ask goes to the trigger's player (the active player, State entry trigPl), not the controller, as gorge's deciderFromSpecTriggeredPlayer does; only the every-player's-turn shape (no ValidPlayer$) lowers. Peace in Our Time, whose body draws for that player, gives their creatures a this-turn CantAttack emblem (a second identical one for the player stands for both) and puts a peace counter on the enchantment."},
	{"tf2:FirstTime", "Tf2FirstTime", "Only the first such event each turn (first life gain: Cat Collector, Vanguard Seraph)."},
	{"tf2:YourTurn", "Tf2YourTurn", "Only during the controller's turn."},
	{"tf2:OppTurn", "Tf2OppTurn", "Only during an opponent's turn (Brineborn Cutthroat)."},
	{"tf2:NonCombat", "Tf2NonCombat", "DamageDone: noncombat damage only (Niv-Mizzet)."},
	{"tf2:ToOpponent", "Tf2ToOpponent", "DamageDone with TfToPlayer: to an opponent only."},
	{"tf2:SelfOrFilter", "Tf2SelfOrFilter", "The event object is the source itself OR matches Filter (Arahbo, Vengeful Bloodwitch)."},
	{"tf2:NthSpell", "Tf2NthSpell + Trigger.N", "SpellCast: the caster's spell count this turn, the triggering one included, against N (gorge ActivatorThisTurnCast$ <op>N: CompareIntCount over pay.SpellsCastThisTurn). A bare N is ==; N >= 256 packs the operator as a kop.DmgGate (NE, GE, LE, GT, LT) over the literal in the low byte (kernel trigCmpOK). Hearthborn Battler, Ledger Shredder, Geralf, the Fleshwright (GT1)."},
	{"trig:ManaExpend", "TrigManaExpend + Trigger.N", "Whenever you expend N (CR 700.14): the cast whose mana takes the controller's total spent on spells this turn from below N to N or more (gorge trigmatch.ManaExpendMatches; fired after the payment, before the SpellCast triggers). The BLB expend cards."},
	{"tf2:Alone", "Tf2Alone", "Attacks: the trigger fires only when exactly one creature was declared as an attacker (gorge Alone$ True, trigmatch.AttacksMatches' declaredAttackerCount; the Exalted expansion). Akrasan Squire."},
	{"tf2:Batch", "Tf2Batch", "A \"one or more\" line queued once per simultaneous batch, at its first matching member (gorge trigger_match.go's zone and damage batch latches): ChangesZoneAll as ETB/Dies/Leaves (an entry batch, leaveAll, an effect's sacrifice; every other move is its own batch), DamageDoneOnce as DamageDone with Tf2PerReferent (once per damaged referent per damage batch), SacrificedOnce as Sacrificed (an effect's sacrifice, or one cost payment's sacrifices: gorge emitSacrifices). Valley Questcaller, Dour Port-Mage, Kastral, Camellia."},
	{"tf2:ToYou", "Tf2ToYou (with TfToPlayer)", "DamageDone: only damage to the listener's controller (gorge ValidTarget$ You; the recipient player is read from the event, not assumed to be the opponent of the source's controller). Risona, Asari Commander."},
	{"tf2:PerReferent", "Tf2PerReferent (with Tf2Batch) + Trigger.N", "DamageDone lowered from Mode$ DamageDoneOnce: queued once per damaged referent (a permanent, or a player) per damage batch, at the referent's first matching event, with the batch total of the matching events to that referent as the trigger amount (gorge trigger_match.go damageBatchKey; a combat damage step is one batch, every other damage event a batch of one). ValidSource$ is Filter, ValidTarget$ is Filter2 (objects only) or TfToPlayer / Tf2ToOpponent / Tf2ToYou (players only), CombatDamage$ is TfCombat / Tf2NonCombat. Trigger.N, when nonzero, is the DamageAmount$ gate on the batch total (kop.DmgGate: comparator << 8 | literal). The trigger object is the recipient (trigger player its controller) for an object referent, the first source (trigger player the damaged player) for a player one. A granted line (Animate Triggers$) is not latched: gorge queues it per event. Feldon, Innocent Bystander, Venus, Sleep Magic, The Thing, Spinneret and Spiderling, Strength of Will."},
	{"tf2:SrcInPlay", "Tf2SrcInPlay", "DamageDone / DamageDealtOnce: the line's ValidSource$ carries inZoneBattlefield (gorge wordInZone, a live zone test), so damage whose source is not a permanent (a spell, or an ability whose source left play: a sacrificed Fanatical Firebrand's ping) never fires it; fireDamageSrc skips the listener. A comma list with the word on only some alternatives is refused. No Mercy, Dread, Aurification, Dissipation Field."},
	{"tf2:Filter2Recipient", "Trigger.Filter2 on DamageDone / DamageDealtOnce", "The damaged permanent must match Filter2 (a player never does): every damage site passes the recipient, and damageBatch fires once per recipient for these lines (Nested Ghoul, Giant's Skewer, Rona's back face)."},
	{"tf:NotToGrave", "TfNotToGrave (always with Tf2Batch)", "Leaves: only to a zone other than a graveyard (ChangesZoneAll's \"leave without dying\": Dour Port-Mage)."},
	{"tf2:Cycled", "Tf2Cycled", "Discarded: a cycle, not a discard. Zone graveyard + TfSelf: \"when you cycle this card\" -- fired for the card itself, from the graveyard, when a cycling ability (AfCycling) discards it as its cost (fireCycled). Battlefield: \"whenever you / a player cycle(s) a card\" matched against the cycled card and its owner, walked with the discard triggers in one pass (cycleDiscard); a plain discard never fires it. Gorge: Mode$ Cycled (rules/trigmatch/cards.go cycledMatches, trigger_zone_gate.go). Other / FirstTime$ shapes are refused."},
	{"tf2:PerPair", "Tf2PerPair", "BecomesBlocked: the trigger fires once per declared (attacker, blocker) pair in declaration order whose attacker matches Filter and whose blocker matches Filter2 (one of them the listener itself); the trigger object is the pair's other member. Gorge: Mode$ AttackerBlockedByCreature (rules/trigger_blocks.go attackerBlockedByPairCandidates, queueAttackerBlockedTrigger). Ashmouth Hound."},
	{"tf2:BlockedBySelf", "Tf2BlockedBySelf", "BecomesBlocked: the trigger fires only for an attacker this permanent blocks (\"whenever this blocks a creature\"; gorge Mode$ AttackerBlocked ValidBlocker$ Card.Self, rules/trigger_blocks.go attackerBlockedCandidates). Wall of Frost."},
	{"tf2:AtkYou", "Tf2AtkYou", "Attacks with Attacked$: the attacked defender may be the trigger's controller (gorge attackedDefenderMatches). With Tf2DefPlayer (an AttackersDeclared line, AttackedTarget$ You) the group's defender must be the controller (kernel fireDefPlayer)."},
	{"tf2:AtkYourPW", "Tf2AtkYourPW", "Attacks with Attacked$: ... or a planeswalker the trigger's controller controls."},
	{"tf2:AtkOpp", "Tf2AtkOpp", "Attacks with Attacked$: ... or an opponent player."},
	{"tf2:TargetsFilter2", "Tf2TargetsFilter2 + Trigger.Filter2", "SpellCast: the spell has a target and some target of its chain matches Filter2 (gorge TargetsValid$, trigmatch.TargetShapeMatches): a battlefield object as a permanent; a Filter2 chain entry with FPlayer (with FSelf and FOther, so no permanent matches it) is a You or Opponent player alternative, matched by Ctrl against the trigger's controller (kernel castTargetsPlayer, Reparations); a chain entry carrying kop.ZoneAny is a zone-free object alternative (a type read in any zone, Danitha, Spear of Agony's Creature.OppCtrl), so an off-battlefield target matches through the card matcher with its stack entry's controller for a spell and its owner otherwise (kernel castTargetsAll). Heroic."},
	{"op:ChangeSpeed", "OpChangeSpeed (Obj players, C 1 increase|2 decrease, B.N flags)", "Each player in Obj changes speed by one (CR 702.179): C=1 increases, starting from 0 and stopping at 4; C=2 decreases, stopping at 1. B.N bit 0 restricts the change to a speed-less player (an increase from zero); bit 1 restricts it to a player whose speed exceeds every other player's. The bounds and the comparison read the folded speed (genState.speed). Gorge: api:ChangeSpeed (engine/effects/change_speed.go). Spikeshell Harrier."},
	{"op:Earthbend", "OpEarthbend (Obj land target, A n, C override)", "Earthbend n (CR 701.66; gorge effEarthbend): a target land you control still on the battlefield becomes a 0/0 Creature with haste for as long as it stays (the override, DurPermanent), gets n +1/+1 counters through OpPutCounter's path (n <= 0: none), and gets one leave-keyed delayed record (State.dly, delayed.when = dlyLeave). The implicit Land.YouCtrl target is gorge's parse step (normalizeImplicitTarget). A target gone from the battlefield does nothing. Badgermole, Earthbending Lesson, Rockalanche and the other TLA earthbenders."},
	{"op:EarthbendReturn", "OpEarthbendReturn (internal)", "The earthbend return trigger, queued by fireLeave when a land with a leave-keyed record goes to a graveyard or exile (matched by object id only, as gorge: no incarnation tracking, never expires; one trigger per record, after the dies/leaves triggers). On resolution the card in a graveyard or exile returns to the battlefield tapped under its OWNER's control (gorge deviates from CR 701.66a the same way); a card elsewhere does nothing. Never in a Prog."},
	{"op:WarpExile", "OpWarpExile (Obj)", "The delayed warp trigger (CR 702.185a): exile battlefield permanent Obj, no LKI rider (the card's own ChangeZone). When the card reached exile this way its owner gets a DurWarp may-play record (normal mana cost, only on a later turn) that dirac/kw_warp.go offers; the record goes stale when the card leaves exile. Gorge: engine/cards/link.go __kwWarpExile and rules/altcast.go warpRecastAvailable. Haliya, Guided by Light."},
	{"tf2:CastSnapshot", "Tf2CastSnapshot", "SpellCast: the trigger amount (ExTriggerAmount) is the number of instant and sorcery spells the controller cast this turn, the triggering one included, counted when the trigger fires; a spell cast in response does not change it and a copy is never counted. Gorge: `TriggerObjectsCurrentCastSpells$Valid Sorcery.YouCtrl,Instant.YouCtrl` (effects/count_triggercastspells.go). Thousand-Year Storm (with /Minus.1)."},
	{"tf2:CastSpent", "Tf2CastSpent", "SpellCast: the trigger amount (ExTriggerAmount) is the triggering spell's pool mana spent (X included; convoke picks, life and free casts not), recorded at payment and snapshotted when the trigger fires, so it survives the spell leaving the stack. Only a battlefield listener that is not the spell itself. Gorge: `TriggeredCard$CastTotalManaSpent` (effects/count_ref_property.go, TriggerManaSpent). Opus-family cast payoffs (Aberrant Manawurm, Deluge Virtuoso, Tellah)."},
	{"tf2:Increment", "Tf2Increment", "SpellCast: Increment (CR 702.xx, Secrets of Strixhaven, the bare `K:Increment`) -- the trigger fires only when the source is a creature and the cast's pool mana spent is greater than its current power or toughness, the layer output, read as it triggers (gorge trigmatch.IncrementHolds over ManaSpentForCast; kernel State.incrementAdmits, the spell entry's recorded spend). The condition is an intervening \"if\" (CR 603.4): as the trigger resolves it is checked again (gorge rules.triggerResolvingCheckHolds, the spend captured in TriggerContext.TriggerIncrementSpent; kernel State.incrementResolves, the spend captured on the trigger entry). Bit 24 shared with Tf2ToYou, read on disjoint events."},
	{"st:Cond2", "Static.Cond2", "The static applies only while the condition holds (threshold, your turn, life vs starting life, ...)."},
	{"st:Dynamic", "StDynamic + Static.VA/VB", "The static's amounts are values recomputed continuously (Blanchwood Armor, Banner of Kinship, Fiend Artisan, cost reductions by count)."},
	{"st:EmbNum", "StEmbNum (Static.A stays 0, no VA)", "ReduceCost on an emblem Effect whose Amount$ was Count$ChosenNumber: the reduction is the emblem's frozen chosen number from `State.g.embN`, not a value. adjustCostGen reads it through embNumAt; an emblem with no frozen number reduces by 0. gorge effects/effect.go evaluates SetChosenNumber$ once as the Effect resolves and the registered static carries that frozen state.ContinuousEffect.ChosenNumber, so life lost or gained later in the turn does not raise the discount (Rowan, Scion of War; Will, Scion of Peace; kernel static_emblemnumber.go; DebugEmbNumLive is the mutation that re-reads the source live)."},
	{"st:AddSub", "Static.AddSub", "Affected objects also have these subtypes (Skyknight Squire: Knight)."},
	{"st:Grant", "Static.Grant", "Affected objects have the source card's ability Grant-1 (Fishing Pole)."},
	{"st:ProtFrom", "Static.ProtFrom", "A Continuous static's granted protection from a quality (AddKeyword$ Protection:<spec>, CR 702.16): the affected objects can't be damaged (prevented), blocked, targeted, enchanted or equipped by a source matching this filter (plain type and colour terms; gorge sourceHasQuality). The filter reads the source as CardDef.ProtFrom does. A layer-6 grant: it does not survive a later loss of the recipient's abilities. Sword of Wealth and Power."},
	{"st:RaiseYou", "StRaiseYou", "IncreaseCost (kgen RaiseCost, gorge costModifiersCompose's raise group): only the static's controller's spells (Activator$ You); with StRaiseOpp only its opponents'; neither: every caster's. Generic mana A (or VA with StDynamic) is added before the reductions' floor at zero; Zone ZoneCommand is the card's own \"costs more\". Dovin, Hand of Control."},
	{"st:Zone", "Static.Zone", "ReduceCost: ZoneCommand = the static works on the card itself in hand/any zone ('this spell costs less'); MayPlayFrom: the zone played from."},
	{"st:YouHexproof", "StYouHexproof", "Continuous: the static's controller has hexproof too (Affected$ You,...; read by playerHexproof under Cond2). Captain America, Super-Soldier; Shalai, Voice of Plenty."},
	{"st:PanhETB", "StPanhETB + Static.Filter2", "Panharmonicon lowered from ValidMode$ ChangesZone,ChangesZoneAll | ValidCause$ | Destination$ Battlefield: besides the ValidCard$ match on the trigger's source, only a trigger caused by a permanent (or token) entering the battlefield echoes, and the entering object must match Filter2 (relative to the static's controller). The cause is the triggering object of a TrigETB placement (gorge panharmoniconModes maps a TokenCreate/CardToken mint to ChangesZone with the battlefield as destination); a TrigTokenCreated placement is a Mode$ TokenCreatedOnce trigger, which ValidMode$ ChangesZone does not name, and is not echoed. A graveyard-leave trigger caused by the same move is not echoed (deviation, GORGE-FINDINGS.md). Starfield Vocalist, Virtue of Knowledge, Traveling Chocobo."},
	{"st:RaiseLife", "StRaiseLife (= StPanhETB, on a StatIncreaseCost)", "IncreaseCost whose Static.A is LIFE the matching spell's caster pays on top of its cost, not generic mana (RaiseCost Cost$ PayLife<N>; gorge composeRaiseCost RaiseLife, CR 601.2f/h, 119.4). With StTargetsFilter2 (ValidTarget$, read relative to the static's source) the life is owed once a chosen target matches: that target is dropped from the menu when the caster has less life than the total owed, the life is paid with the cast's other life. Terror of the Peaks."},
	{"st:RaisePerTarget", "StRaisePerTarget (= StOncePerTurn, on a StatIncreaseCost)", "The spell's own IncreaseCost charged once per target beyond the first (RaiseCost Cost$ <pips> | Amount$ TargetedObjects$Amount/Minus.1 | Relative$ True; gorge composeRaiseCost): Static.A generic and Static.B coloured pips (packed as StReduceColor) per charge, the charge count read from the cast in progress (0 targets or 1: nothing). The pips join the cost before the reductions take theirs. Officious Interrogation; Fireball is the Cost$-less form, one generic per charge."},
	{"st:ReduceAny", "StReduceAny (= StRaiseOpp, on a StatReduceCost)", "ReduceCost with no Activator$: the reduction applies to either player's spells, not the controller's alone (gorge costStaticApplies reads Activator$ only when present; Forge StaticAbilityCostChange). Helm of Awakening."},
	{"st:TargetsFilter2", "StTargetsFilter2", "ReduceCost applies only if the spell targets an object matching Filter2 (Luminous Rebuke)."},
	{"st:Bargained", "StBargained", "A self ReduceCost that prices only the bargained cast (ValidSpell$ Spell.Bargain: Hamlet Glutton, Ice Out, Johann's Stopgap; gorge spellConstraintMatchesBargain reads the cast mode): the plain cast pays the full cost, the bargained cast (AkCastCasualty of a Bargain card) the discounted one, at the offer and at the charge."},
	{"st:MayPayLife", "StMayPayLife (= StReduceColor, on a StatMayPlayFrom)", "A library-top play permission whose cast pays life equal to the card's mana value in place of its mana cost (Effect MayPlayAltManaCost$ PayLife<ConvertedManaCost> beside MayPlay$ over Card.TopLibrary: Gwenom, Remorseless; gorge prices the cast through the grant's alternative only, CR 118.9). The offer is free of mana when the caster has the life (CR 119.4); the cast pays the mana value in life beside its other costs; a land is played for nothing. The Effect's MayLookAt$ look is information only and lowers to nothing."},
	{"st:ReduceColor", "StReduceColor (Static.A generic, Static.B coloured counts)", "ReduceCost whose Color$ names coloured pips (Brush Off, Color$ 1 U | Amount$ 1): A is the generic part, B packs a count per colour (two bits each, W U B R G C from bit 0). The coloured pips come off first and the shortfall spills to generic, never below 0 (gorge pay CostMods.ApplyTo)."},
	{"repl:Cond", "Repl.Cond / Repl.Filter", "The replacement applies only while the condition holds; Filter: the other objects it applies to."},
	{"card:WardLife", "CardDef.WardLife", "Ward—pay N life (KwWard with WardN 0; Sire of Seven Deaths, Zul Ashur)."},
	{"card:WardEvidence", "CardDef.WardEvidence", "Ward—collect evidence N (KwWard with WardN 0): pay or not, then 1..all of the payer's graveyard cards, short of N mana value countering (gorge kw_ward.go; Axebane Ferox)."},
	{"card:TypedMana", "CardDef.TypedMana", "The printed face is a Cave or a Desert: its mana is typed in gorge's pool (state.Game TypedMana), which ends gorge's planned resolution-time payment (pay.PlanPoolOK): the rest is paid through the manual window (kernel payReplanned). Hidden Nursery."},
	{"card:Engines", "CardDef.Engines", "Printed Start your engines! (CR 702.179a; gorge engine/rules/speed.go checkSpeedStart): a seat with no speed that controls a permanent carrying it gets speed 1, scanned after every battlefield entry (spell, token, copy, return) and every control change (genState.speed; the control-change scan is what an entry-only hook misses). Not when the permanent has lost its abilities. A table with it or an OpChangeSpeed also queues the active player's source-less speed trigger when an opponent loses life on their turn (once a turn, speed 1..3; ab.Gate CtrMaxSpeed abilities exist only at speed 4)."},
	{"card:Wither", "CardDef.Wither", "Printed wither (CR 702.80): its damage to a creature is dealt as -1/-1 counters (infect's creature half: the infect paths with genPrep.anyInfect); to a player or planeswalker it is ordinary damage. Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: effects/damage.go emitObjectDamage's wither tag. Boggart Ram-Gang. A GRANTED wither (Pump KW$ Wither, a static AddKeyword$ Wither, an override AddKw) is the keyword bit kop.KwWither (kgen kwBits; never set for a printed K:Wither) and is read through the same paths (kernel witherKw / srcWither: genPrep.anyWitherGrant sets anyInfect); a source that left the battlefield reads its LKI keywords (gorge lki.Wither). Barbed Bloodletter."},
	{"card:AloneAtk", "CardDef.AloneAtk", "Printed \"CARDNAME can't attack alone.\" (CR 506.5): the creature is offered as an attacker only while another creature could join it, and Done is withheld while it is the lone attacker; a must-attack requirement on it binds only while a partner can attack (CR 508.1d). Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: combat.DeclaresAlone, decision Option.AloneRestricted, requiredCore. Pet Sehlat."},
	{"card:AloneBlk", "CardDef.AloneBlk", "Printed \"CARDNAME can't block alone.\" and the block half of \"CARDNAME can't attack or block alone.\" (CR 506.5): a block pair is offered only when another block is declared or can still join it, and Done is withheld while the one declared blocker carries the restriction. Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: combat.DeclaresAlone over the blocker option and Done, decision Option.AloneRestricted. Craven Hulk, Bonded Horncrest."},
	{"card:Daybound", "CardDef.Daybound / Nightbound", "K:Daybound / K:Nightbound (CR 702.145, CR 731; gorge rules/daynight.go, cr-daybound-nightbound and -transform): with neither designation a daybound permanent makes it day, else a nightbound one night (an SBA); the untap step turns day to night when the last turn's active player cast no spells and night to day after two or more; each change transforms every face-up daybound front / nightbound back the designation contradicts (Transformed triggers fire); a daybound front entering at night enters back face up; nothing else transforms them. genState.dayNight. Brutal Cathar, Graveyard Trespasser."},
	{"card:WardDiscard", "CardDef.WardDiscard", "Ward—Discard a card (gorge kw_ward.go's Discard arm): pay or not, then a ward_discard pick of one hand card (posed even with one card); an empty hand counters (Graveyard Trespasser)."},
	{"card:WardSac", "CardDef.WardSac", "Ward—Sacrifice a <filter> (gorge kw_ward.go's Sac arm, N = 1): pay or not (both offered always), then a ward_sac pick of one permanent the payer controls matching WardSac, evaluated on the live layers (Ygra makes creatures Food); none matching counters at once. The pick leaves for the graveyard without fireSac: gorge's \"sacrificed for ward\" MoveZone is not events.IsSacrifice, so no Sacrificed trigger or tally (GORGE-FINDINGS.md; Vein Ripper, Ygra)."},
	{"card:WardWaterbend", "CardDef.WardWaterbend", "Ward—Waterbend {N} (gorge ward.go's Waterbend arm): pay or not (both offered always), then the taps owed past the floating pool: none pays from the pool unasked, fewer candidates than owed counters, else one ward_waterbend pick of that many untapped artifacts and creatures, asked even when exactly that many exist (The Unagi of Kyoshi Island)."},
	{"card:WardPoison", "CardDef.WardPoison", "Ward—AddCounterYou<N/POISON> (gorge ward.go's AddCounterYou arm): pay or not (both offered always), paying gives the ward's payer N poison counters through the kernel's addPoison, a decline countering the warded spell or ability (The Serpent Society)."},
	{"card:WardDiscOrN", "CardDef.WardDiscOrN", "Ward—Discard a card or pay {N} (gorge ward.go's \">:\" arm): pay or not (both offered always), then one ward_alt pick of a hand card to discard (hand order) or {N} (offered while the pool pays it or the payer controls an untapped mana source), the {N} charged as the plain {N} ward's through its mana window; no option counters at once (Titania, Rugged Rumbler)."},
	{"card:WardLifePower", "CardDef.WardLifePower", "Ward—Pay life equal to its power (gorge kw_ward.go's PayLife<X/…> arm): the ward permanent's power read when the ward resolves, floored at 0, then the pay-N-life ask (a pump in response changes the life paid; Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo)."},
	{"card:Lure", "CardDef.Lure", "The all-must-block keyword: every able creature blocks it (CR 509.1c; gorge kw:AllMustBlock, cr-lure-all-must-block): while it attacks, a creature able to block a lure attacker is offered only its lure blocks, and the declaration completes only when every such creature blocks one. Not when it has lost its abilities. Prized Unicorn."},
	{"card:MustBeBlocked", "CardDef.MustBeBlocked", "The must-be-blocked keyword (CR 509.1c; gorge hidden keyword MustBlock, read layer-derived per attacker): an attacker requirement that one blocker satisfies. gorge accepts only a declaration obeying the most requirements (decision.blockRequiredQuota: one unit per must-be-blocked attacker with a block, one per lure duty blocker blocking a lure attacker); the kernel offers a pair only while that maximum stays reachable and Done only once met (blockerOptionsReq: a bounded search over the free blockers, StallMustBlock past its node budget). An attacker no creature could block is no requirement. Not when it has lost its abilities. Fear of Being Hunted, Vinebred Brawler, Raphael Ninja Destroyer."},
	{"card:Madness", "CardDef.HasMadness + MadnessCost", "Printed madness (CR 702.35a-b; gorge rules/altcast.go): a discard of the card puts it into exile instead (every discard path: effect, cost, cleanup), and queues a kernel-native keyword trigger (ab 251) that the owner may answer as it resolves by casting the card from exile for MadnessCost (offered only when castable; paid through gorge's mana window) or else puts it into the graveyard. X, hybrid and granted madness refuse. Fiery Temper."},
	{"card:Miracle", "CardDef.HasMiracle + MiracleCost", "Printed miracle (CR 702.94a; gorge rules/miracle.go): the first card its owner draws in a turn (never the opening deal) queues a kernel-native keyword trigger (ab 249). Placing it asks the owner whether to reveal (a no drops it), a yes puts it on the stack so both players get priority, and as it resolves the owner may cast the card from hand for MiracleCost (offered only when castable; paid through gorge's mana window) or keep it. X, hybrid and granted miracle refuse. Reforge the Soul."},
	{"card:MinBlockers", "CardDef.MinBlockers", "A printed S:Mode$ MinMaxBlocker | ValidCard$ Creature.Self | Min$ N (CR 509.1b): the creature can't be blocked except by N or more creatures, menace's floor generalised (an attacker that fewer could block is not offered; a pick that leaves the declaration uncompletable is not offered). Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/restrictions.go MinMaxBlockerBounds. Troll of Khazad-dum."},
	{"card:ExtraBlocks", "CardDef.ExtraBlocks", "A printed S:Mode$ Continuous | AffectedDefined$ Self | CanBlockAmount$ 1 (CR 509.1a): the creature can block one additional attacker each combat, so it is declared against at most two, and its controller divides its combat damage between them (CR 510.1d; one more blocker of each attacker, blocked pairs in declaration order). Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/extrablock.go BlockCapacity. Ghastbark Twins."},
	{"card:Evasion", "CardDef.Evasion", "Printed blocking-restriction keywords without a keyword bit (kop.Ev*): horsemanship (CR 702.31b, blocked only by a creature with horsemanship) and intimidate (CR 702.13a, blocked only by an artifact creature or one sharing a colour). Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/block.go CanBlock. Shu Cavalry, Kraken of the Straits."},
	{"card:Infect", "CardDef.Infect", "Printed infect (CR 702.90): its damage is dealt to a player as poison counters (no life loss) and to a creature as -1/-1 counters (no marked damage). Not when it has lost its abilities. A table with infect and a damage-replacement order ask, a counter-added trigger or proliferate stalls (StallInfect). Gorge: effects/damage.go emitObjectDamage, rules/infect.go convertInfectDamage. Glistener Elf."},
	{"card:Cascade", "CardDef.Cascade", "Printed K:Cascade instances (CR 702.85a/c): casting the spell queues that many kernel-native triggers; each exiles from the library top to the first nonland card of strictly lower mana value (spell MV + X), offers its free cast, and bottoms the rest in a random order drawn from the engine rng (gorge's seeded Fisher-Yates, effCascadeResidue). Gorge: effects/cascade.go effCascade. Bloodbraid Elf."},
	{"card:Toxic", "CardDef.Toxic", "Printed toxic N, instances summed (CR 702.164): a player it deals combat damage to also gets N poison counters. Gorge: rules/combat.go runCombatAssignments, ToxicValue. Bilious Skulldweller."},
	{"card:HexColors", "CardDef.HexColors", "Printed hexproof from a colour (CR 702.11d): a spell or ability of that colour an opponent controls can't target it. Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/protection.go hexproofBlocksTarget. Knight of Grace."},
	{"card:ProtColors", "CardDef.ProtColors", "Printed protection from a colour (CR 702.16; \"each color\" is all five): a source of one of those colours can't damage (prevented), block, target or enchant it. Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/protection.go protectedFrom. White Knight."},
	{"st:Landwalk", "Static.Landwalk", "A Continuous static's granted landwalk (AddKeyword$ Landwalk:<land spec>, CR 702.14): the affected creatures can't be blocked while the defending player controls a land matching this battlefield filter (as CardDef.Landwalk reads it). A layer-6 grant: it does not survive a later loss of the recipient's abilities. Only a global grant lowers (not an Equipment's or Aura's). Gorge: rules/combat/block.go LandwalkEvades over the derived keywords. Goblin King, Lord of Atlantis."},
	{"card:ProtFrom", "CardDef.ProtFrom", "Printed K:Protection:<spec> (CR 702.16): a source matching this filter (types, subtypes, colours) can't damage (prevented), block, target or enchant it. Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/protection.go sourceHasQuality. Tel-Jilad Chosen."},
	{"card:Landwalk", "CardDef.Landwalk", "The printed landwalk keyword (CR 702.14): the creature can't be blocked while the defending player controls a land matching this battlefield filter (its printed or granted subtypes). Not when it has lost its abilities. Gorge: rules/combat/block.go LandwalkEvades. Bog Raiders."},
	{"card:SelfFlash", "CardDef.SelfFlash", "A CastWithFlash EffectZone$ All self grant (\"you may cast this spell as though it had flash if you control a Faerie\"): the card's own StatCastWithFlash ability, gated by IsPresent$ read for the caster with no battlefield source, lets it be cast at instant speed from any zone it is cast from, never granting other spells flash. Gorge: rules/statics_cast.go withSelfStatics + castWithFlashTargets. Illusion Spinners, Bard's Company, Serpent of the Pass."},
	{"card:Leyline", "CardDef.Leyline", "May begin the game on the battlefield from the opening hand (after mulligans; a decision per such card)."},
	{"card:SpellCost", "CardDef.SpellCost", "A permanent spell's additional cost (Arbiter of Woe: sacrifice a creature). Instants/sorceries carry theirs on the AbSpell ability's Cost."},
	{"card:BeamMeUp", "CardDef.BeamMeUp (AltCost the mana, FbCost the return)", "Printed beam me up: a graveyard cast for AltCost that also returns a creature you control to its owner's hand, then exiles the spell."},
	{"card:FbCost", "CardDef.FbCost (with KwFlashback; AltCost the mana part)", "A printed flashback cost's non-mana part (CR 702.34a; gorge flashbackCost parses the keyword parameter as a whole cost): one Sac<N/Spec> or tapXType<N/Spec>, paid through the flashback cast's sacrifice / tap-creatures picks in place of the spell's additional cost, and its census gates the graveyard offer. Dread Return, Lava Dart."},
	{"card:CombatHitRec", "CardDef.CombatHitRec (genPrep.cdRec)", "The card reads the filter word ControlledBy Player.wasDealtCombatDamageThisTurnBySource against itself (Filter.Ctrl = CtrlHitBySrc): a landed combat hit on a player by one of its objects is recorded in genState.cdh (up to four sources a turn, a fifth stalls StallCombatHit), keyed by the source's Obj so the record outlives the source leaving and returning (gorge dealtCombatDamageBySource matches the hit's ObjID). A card without it records nothing. Steel Hellkite."},
	{"card:ExiledWith", "CardDef.ExiledWith (genPrep.exwRec)", "The card reads the exiled-with source link (pred:ExiledWith or ex:ExiledWithN): its resolutions record each card they exile (genState.exw: the source's ver, the reverse and forward bits), so a later resolution of the same source finds them. A card without it records nothing. Ghost Vacuum, Northampton Farm."},
	{"card:RemPersist", "CardDef.RemPersist (gen.links)", "The card's enters trigger remembers what its leaves trigger reads (gorge's Remembered persists on the source): the enters resolution's remembered objects are kept in the exile links keyed by the source's battlefield incarnation when it ends with the source still that incarnation, and that incarnation's leaves trigger resolves with them as its remembered set (a source gone before its enters trigger resolved leaves the card where it went). Journey to Nowhere, Mesmeric Fiend; the dies form (the leaves trigger is Destination$ Graveyard, both triggers optional) is Hoarding Dragon."},
	{"card:SpendRead", "CardDef.SpendRead", "An SVar body reads Count$CastTotalManaSpent: gorge's cast planner prices no cast of the card (faceWantsCastSpend, \"shape:mana_spent_reader\"), so it is offered only when the floating pool pays it. Memory Deluge."},
	{"tf2:CastFromHand", "Tf2CastFromHand", "ValidCard$ ...+wasCastFromYourHandByYou: SpellCast, the spell was cast from its owner's hand by the trigger's controller; a TfSelf ETB, the source entered as the resolving spell its controller cast from their hand (stackEntry.prov). Soulhunter Rakshasa."},
	{"tf2:Convoked", "Tf2Convoked", "A TfSelf ETB whose amount (ExTriggerAmount) is the creatures that convoked the source's spell, bound as it triggers (gorge Convoked$Amount; stackEntry.prov). Knight-Errant of Eos."},
	{"f2:Warped", "F2Warped", "CastSa Spell.Warp on a battlefield permanent: cast for its warp cost, its warp exile still pending (the delayed record, its queued trigger or that trigger on the stack). Full Bore."},
	{"card:AltAddCost", "CardDef.AltAddCost + HasAltAdd", "AlternateAdditionalCost: when casting, pay either the spell's additional cost (AbSpell Cost) or this one (Eaten Alive: sacrifice a creature or pay {3}{B}). Decision at cast."},
	{"card:Improvise", "CardDef.Improvise", "K:Improvise (CR 702.126a): the cast may tap untapped artifacts, each paying {1} of the generic part (dirac/kw_convoke.go, mode-6 picks). A granted Improvise (stat:StackKw A=1) reads the same paths (kernel isImprovise); every printed {X} carrier and printed Convoke+Improvise card is refused; a grant on such a spell poses the mixed or pre-X announcement (kernel convokeOptions), and only a Harmonize or alternative-cost route stalls unmodelled (StallStackKwGrant)."},
	{"card:Convoke", "CardDef.Convoke", "K:Convoke (CR 702.51a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the cast may tap untapped creatures for its mana cost (dirac/kw_convoke.go). A Convoke grant (stat:StackKw A=7) reads the same paths (kernel hasConvoke); a printed {X} carrier or printed Convoke+Improvise card is refused; a grant on such a spell poses the mixed or pre-X announcement (kernel convokeOptions), and only a Harmonize or alternative-cost route stalls unmodelled (StallStackKwGrant)."},
	{"card:Delve", "CardDef.Delve", "K:Delve (CR 702.66a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the cast is offered on its graveyard credit, min(generic, graveyard size), and announces graveyard cards to exile after X, one pick at a time (dirac/kw_delve.go); the cards move to exile once the mana is paid. A granted Delve (stat:StackKw A=9) reads the same paths (kernel hasCastDelve)."},
	{"card:Battle", "CardDef.Defense + kop.CtrDefense + DurDefeated", "A transforming double-faced Siege (CR 310, 712; gorge faces.IsBattle): it enters with Defense CtrDefense counters through the counter replacements (CR 310.4) and records its sole opponent as the protector in perm.chosen (0xF0|seat; gorge applySiegeProtector, no ask in two players). The active player may attack any battle whose protector is the opponent; combat and spell damage to it removes that many defense counters and is not marked (gorge foldDamage); a battle with no defense is exiled by the state-based action (gorge battleZeroDefense) and queues the owner's transformed free cast (DurDefeated, ChDefeatCast; gorge startDefeatedCast's defeat_cast_yes/no). Refused unless a 2-face DoubleFaced card with a Battle front, a non-Battle back, a plain numeric Defense 1..127 and no enters replacement; tokens stay refused.."},
	{"card:Impending", "CardDef.Impending + ImpendingCost", "K:Impending:<N>:<cost> (CR 702.176a): the hand offers the impended cast at ImpendingCost (gorge's \"impended\" cast option, FlagImpending); cast that way the permanent enters with N time counters (CtrTime) and is not a creature while it has one; the end-step removal is a synthesized trigger (gorge's granted __kwImpendingTick line). Refused beside another cast route; any other card putting time counters is refused (the kernel reads the counter, not the cast provenance). Overlord of the Mistmoors."},
	{"card:Warp", "CardDef.HasWarp + WarpCost", "K:Warp:<cost> (CR 702.185a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the hand offers the warp cast at WarpCost (gorge's \"warped\" cast option, FlagWarped), and a permanent spell cast that way is exiled at the beginning of the next end step by OpWarpExile with a recast from exile on a later turn at its normal mana cost (gorge \"warp_recast\"). An {X} in the warp cost is announced like a printed one (Broodguard Elite); a warp cost with a non-mana part is refused (Timeline Culler). Haliya, Guided by Light."},
	{"card:Paradigm", "CardDef.Paradigm", "K:Paradigm (SOS; gorge rules/paradigm.go): 1 + the table's Paradigm-name index (at most 8 names; a ninth refuses). A resolved spell goes to exile instead of the graveyard (a countered or fizzled one does not) and sets its owner's genState.parad bit for the name; in its owner's first main phase the exiled card is offered as a free cast unless it was put on the stack this turn (the ring). gorge casts the card itself, not a copy. Only a single-face instant/sorcery lowers. Decorum Dissertation, Germination Practicum, Restoration Seminar."},
	{"card:Plot", "CardDef.HasPlot + PlotCost", "K:Plot:<cost> (CR 702.170a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the hand offers the plot special action at PlotCost at sorcery speed (gorge \"plot\" cast option), exiling the card with the plotted designation; on a later turn its owner may cast it from exile without paying its mana cost at sorcery speed (gorge \"plot_cast\"). X, hybrid and non-mana plot costs are refused, as is plot beside an alternative or additional cost, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Slickshot Show-Off."},
	{"card:Foretell", "CardDef.HasForetell + ForetellCost", "K:Foretell:<cost> (CR 702.143a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): during its controller's turn, whenever they have priority, the hand offers the foretell special action (kernel AkPlot mode 1, gorge \"foretell\" cast option) at {2} (never the keyword cost; no cost static of the spell scope reaches it), exiling the card with a DurForetell record; on a later turn its owner may cast it from exile (AkCast mode 0, target 5, gorge \"foretell_cast\") for ForetellCost with the card's own timing and targets, when the floating pool pays it. X, hybrid and non-mana foretell costs are refused, as is foretell beside an alternative or additional cost, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Behold the Multiverse, Ravenform."},
	{"card:Sneak", "CardDef.HasSneak + SneakCost", "K:Sneak:<cost> (CR 702.190; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): in its controller's declare-blockers step the hand offers the sneak cast (kernel AkSneak, gorge Mode \"sneak\") at SneakCost plus returning an unblocked attacker they control to its owner's hand (the ChCostReturn pick, always asked); a permanent spell cast that way enters tapped and attacking that attacker's defender (CR 702.190b). Offered when the floating pool pays or a scripted activation (filter land) can fund it, as gorge's planner prices a sneak play through the same prefix search. X, hybrid, CardManaCost, rider and non-mana sneak costs are refused, as is sneak beside an alternative or additional cost, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Splinter, Hamato Yoshi."},
	{"card:Evoke", "CardDef.HasEvoke + EvokeCost", "K:Evoke:<cost> (CR 702.74a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the hand offers the evoked cast at EvokeCost (gorge's \"evoked\" cast option, FlagEvoked; hybrid pips are announced as for any cost); the permanent that cast produces queues a mandatory \"sacrifice it\" trigger as it enters, after the card's own enters triggers (gorge altCostEnter). Provenance is bit 10 of the spell entry's spc. Refused beside another cast cost route, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Catharsis, Deceit, Emptiness, Vibrance, Wistfulness."},
	{"card:Dash", "CardDef.HasDash + DashCost", "K:Dash:<cost> (CR 702.109a; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the hand offers the dashed cast at DashCost (gorge's \"dashed\" cast option, FlagDashed; hybrid pips are announced as for any cost); the permanent that cast produces gains haste until end of turn and, at the beginning of the next end step, returns to its owner's hand if it is still that permanent (a kernel-internal delayed act, ordered with the other end-step triggers even when stale, gorge __kwDashReturn). Provenance is the entry's impending mode bit, read only on a card with printed dash. Refused beside another cast cost route, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer."},
	{"card:WebSling", "CardDef.HasWebSling + WebSlingCost", "K:Web-slinging:<cost> (CR 702.188; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): under the plain cast's timing the hand offers the web-slinging cast (kernel AkWebSling, gorge Mode \"web-slinging\") at WebSlingCost plus returning a tapped creature its caster controls to its owner's hand (the ChCostReturn pick, always asked). Offered only when the floating pool pays, as gorge's planner prices no web-slinging play. X, hybrid, CardManaCost, rider and non-mana costs are refused, as is web-slinging beside another cast cost route, on an {X} spell or on a multi-face card. Spider-Man, Web-Slinger."},
	{"card:Bestow", "CardDef.HasBestow + BestowCost + BestowTgt", "K:Bestow:<cost> (CR 702.103; no free KwMask bit, so its own field): the hand offers the bestowed cast (kernel AkBestow, gorge Mode \"bestowed\") at BestowCost, one {X} allowed; the spell is an Aura with enchant creature (BestowTgt) from payment on (gorge FlagBestowed), resolves attached, or as a creature spell when its target is illegal (CR 702.103e); while attached the permanent is an Aura, not a creature, and it detaches and stays when its host is gone, not a creature or protected from it (CR 702.103f). Hybrid, rider and non-mana bestow costs are refused. Nyxborn Hydra."},
	{"cost:DiscardFiltered", "CostDiscardFiltered (N, Filter)", "Discard `N` hand cards matching Filter (CR 118.3, 601.2h; gorge pay.DiscardCandidates over MatchesSpecFrom): a Discard<N/Spec> cost whose spec is beyond Card/Random/Hand (Solitary Cell's Card.Legendary, grandeur's Card.named<self>, CR 702.36). The candidates are the hand cards matching Filter, the source excluded while it is a hand card; the payable gate (canActivate / pickCostPayable) and the payment picks (pkDiscard) count them, else the cost is unpayable. Alone among the counted parts (Cost.N / Cost.Filter), a battlefield activated ability's own cost only; kgen refuses the rest. A named<face> clause is the source's own name and lowers to Pred = PredNamed, PredN = the card's id (Page, Loose Leaf). A named clause may also name another card: PredNamed, PredN = the pool entry with that printed name, -1 = no such object in this matchup (matches nothing, gorge sharesName)."},
}

// opsUsage records, per doc label, the pool cards using it.
func opsUsage(pt *poolTables, all []*lCard, bs []built) map[string]map[string]bool {
	use := map[string]map[string]bool{}
	add := func(l, card string) {
		if use[l] == nil {
			use[l] = map[string]bool{}
		}
		use[l][card] = true
	}
	kOp := map[kop.Op]string{}
	for _, d := range opsEntries {
		if strings.HasPrefix(d.label, "op:") {
			for o := kop.Op(0); o < kop.OpHighEnd; o++ {
				if o.Known() && "op:"+o.String() == d.label {
					kOp[o] = d.label
				}
			}
		}
	}
	exNames := map[kop.ExprKind]string{kop.ExCountGraveyard: "CountGraveyard", kop.ExSumPower: "SumPower", kop.ExDistinctCMC: "DistinctCMC",
		kop.ExKicked: "Kicked", kop.ExMorbid: "Morbid", kop.ExCommittedCrime: "CommittedCrimeThisTurn", kop.ExAttackedThisTurn: "AttackedThisTurn", kop.ExPowerOf: "PowerOf",
		kop.ExToughnessOf: "ToughnessOf", kop.ExLifeOf: "LifeOf", kop.ExLibrarySizeOf: "LibrarySizeOf", kop.ExStartingLife: "StartingLife",
		kop.ExTriggerAmount: "TriggerAmount", kop.ExLifeGainedThisTurn: "LifeGainedThisTurn", kop.ExOppLifeLostThisTurn: "OppLifeLostThisTurn",
		kop.ExCountersOn: "CountersOn", kop.ExCreaturesDied: "CreaturesDied", kop.ExRememberedCount: "RememberedCount",
		kop.ExExcessDamage: "ExcessDamage", kop.ExLastLifeLost: "LastLifeLost", kop.ExTokensCreated: "TokensCreated", kop.ExLifeLostThisTurn: "LifeLostThisTurn", kop.ExSum: "Sum", kop.ExCount: "Count", kop.ExX: "X",
		kop.ExHandSizeOf: "HandSizeOf", kop.ExCountExile: "CountExile", kop.ExOppsLostLife: "OppsLostLife", kop.ExAttackedTurn: "AttackedTurn", kop.ExMVOf: "MVOf", kop.ExTriggerSpellMVLKI: "TriggerSpellMVLKI", kop.ExCountAtLeast: "CountAtLeast", kop.ExThisTurnCastSpec: "ThisTurnCastSpec", kop.ExPromisedGift: "PromisedGift", kop.ExResolvedThisTurn: "ResolvedThisTurn", kop.ExRollResult: "RollResult", kop.ExCastManaSpent: "CastManaSpent", kop.ExTgtSpent: "TgtSpent", kop.ExConverge: "Converge", kop.ExHighestOppPoison: "HighestOppPoison", kop.ExSelfPrepared: "SelfPrepared", kop.ExThisTurnActGrave: "ThisTurnActGrave", kop.ExSneaked: "Sneaked", kop.ExPoisonOf: "PoisonOf", kop.ExProduct: "Product", kop.ExAttackersAll: "AttackersAll", kop.ExRefCount: "RefCount", kop.ExYourTurns: "YourTurns", kop.ExYourExtraTurns: "YourExtraTurns", kop.ExLowestLife: "LowestLife", kop.ExRedNCDmg: "RedNCDmg", kop.ExVoid: "Void", kop.ExRevolt: "Revolt", kop.ExLeftZone: "LeftZone", kop.ExCastFromGrave: "CastFromGrave", kop.ExCtrAdded: "CtrAdded", kop.ExExiledWithN: "ExiledWithN", kop.ExNumColorsOf: "NumColorsOf", kop.ExRemLKIPT: "RemLKIPT", kop.ExUnlockedDoors: "UnlockedDoors", kop.ExNotOwnLibMV: "NotOwnLibMV", kop.ExChosenMode: "ChosenMode", kop.ExChosenNumber: "ChosenNumber", kop.ExMod: "Mod", kop.ExPhaseCount: "PhaseCount", kop.ExStepIn: "StepIn", kop.ExAdamant: "Adamant", kop.ExCounterKinds: "CounterKinds", kop.ExTargetPlayers: "TargetPlayers", kop.ExIfCastOwnMain: "IfCastOwnMain", kop.ExOppExtreme: "OppExtreme", kop.ExActivations: "Activations", kop.ExDmgAmountReceived: "DmgAmountReceived"}
	condNamesK := map[kop.CondKind]string{kop.CondPresent: "Present", kop.CondValue: "Value", kop.CondThreshold: "Threshold",
		kop.CondYourTurn: "YourTurn", kop.CondRefMatches: "RefMatches", kop.CondPromised: "Promised", kop.CondAnd: "And"}
	refNamesK := map[kop.Ref]string{kop.RefRemembered: "Remembered", kop.RefDelayedRemembered: "DelayedRemembered", kop.RefReplaced: "Replaced",
		kop.RefTriggerSource: "TriggerSource", kop.RefSacrificed: "Sacrificed", kop.RefHost: "Host",
		kop.RefTargets01: "Targets01", kop.RefTargets012: "Targets012", kop.RefTargets12: "Targets12", kop.RefTargets0123: "Targets0123", kop.RefRememberedController: "RememberedController", kop.RefDiscarded: "Discarded", kop.RefOppNonRemCtrl: "OppNonRemCtrl", kop.RefSrcOwner: "SrcOwner", kop.RefPromised: "Promised", kop.RefTriggerAttackers: "TriggerAttackers", kop.RefRememberedOwner: "RememberedOwner"}
	f2Names := []struct {
		b kop.FilterFlags2
		l string
	}{{kop.F2Kicked, "Kicked"}, {kop.F2CastByYou, "CastByYou"}, {kop.F2EnteredThisTurn, "EnteredThisTurn"}, {kop.F2ChosenType, "ChosenType"},
		{kop.F2ChosenColor, "ChosenColor"}, {kop.F2Remembered | kop.F2NotRemembered, "Remembered"}, {kop.F2ChosenCard | kop.F2NotChosenCard, "ChosenCard"},
		{kop.F2AttachedToT0, "AttachedToT0"}, {kop.F2TargetedBy, "TargetedBy"}, {kop.F2SameNameAsSource, "SameNameAsSource"},
		{kop.F2WithFlying | kop.F2WithoutFlying, "WithFlying"}, {kop.F2Emblem, "Emblem"}, {kop.F2Basic, "Basic"}, {kop.F2Legendary, "Legendary"}, {kop.F2SharesColorRem, "SharesColorRem"},
		{kop.F2NotTriggerObj, "NotTriggerObj"}, {kop.F2WasDamaged, "WasDamaged"}, {kop.F2Saddled, "Saddled"}, {kop.F2Sneaked, "Sneaked"}, {kop.F2Unblocked, "Unblocked"},
		{kop.F2TgtPlayerCtrl, "TgtPlayerCtrl"}, {kop.F2DefendingCtrl, "DefendingCtrl"}, {kop.F2CrewedSrc, "CrewedSrc"}}
	kwNames := []struct {
		b kop.KwMask
		l string
	}{{kop.KwHexproofFromInstants, "HexproofFromInstants"}, {kop.KwProtBlack, "ProtBlack"}, {kop.KwProtRed, "ProtRed"},
		{kop.KwPreventCombatDamageTo, "PreventCombatDamageTo"}, {kop.KwFlashbackOwnCost, "FlashbackOwnCost"},
		{kop.KwPreventCombatDamageFrom, "PreventCombatDamageFrom"},
		{kop.KwUnblockable, "Unblockable"}, {kop.KwCantBlock, "CantBlock"}}
	for ci, c := range all {
		if len(c.Refusals) > 0 {
			continue
		}
		name := c.Name
		d := &bs[ci].def
		seenF := map[kop.FilterID]bool{}
		var filt func(id kop.FilterID)
		var val func(v kop.ValueRef)
		kw := func(m kop.KwMask) {
			for _, k := range kwNames {
				if m&k.b != 0 {
					add("kw:"+k.l, name)
				}
			}
		}
		filt = func(id kop.FilterID) {
			for id != 0 && !seenF[id] {
				seenF[id] = true
				f := pt.filters[id]
				if f.Owner != 0 {
					add("filter:Owner", name)
				}
				if f.Sub != 0 || f.NotSub != 0 {
					add("filter:Sub", name)
				}
				if f.Or != 0 {
					add("filter:Or", name)
				}
				if f.PredV != (kop.ValueRef{}) {
					add("filter:PredV", name)
				}
				switch f.Pred {
				case kop.PredCMCEQ:
					add("pred:CMCEQ", name)
				case kop.PredCMCLEV:
					add("pred:CMCLEV", name)
				case kop.PredCountersGE:
					add("pred:CountersGE", name)
				case kop.PredToughnessGE:
					add("pred:ToughnessGE", name)
				case kop.PredHasXCost:
					add("pred:HasXCost", name)
				case kop.PredPowerLTToughness:
					add("pred:PowerLTToughness", name)
				case kop.PredMultiColor:
					add("pred:MultiColor", name)
				case kop.PredHistoric:
					add("pred:Historic", name)
				case kop.PredEquipped:
					add("pred:Equipped", name)
				case kop.PredTypesAll:
					add("pred:TypesAll", name)
				case kop.PredTypesAllCMCLE:
					add("pred:TypesAllCMCLE", name)
				case kop.PredModified:
					add("pred:Modified", name)
				case kop.PredHasCounters:
					add("pred:HasCounters", name)
				case kop.PredMonstrous:
					add("pred:Monstrous", name)
				case kop.PredNoCounters:
					add("pred:NoCounters", name)
				case kop.PredLacksKeyword:
					add("pred:LacksKeyword", name)
				case kop.PredOutlaw:
					add("pred:Outlaw", name)
				case kop.PredMonoColor:
					add("pred:MonoColor", name)
				case kop.PredSameNameT0:
					add("pred:SameNameT0", name)
				case kop.PredCountersLT:
					add("pred:CountersLT", name)
				case kop.PredToughnessLEV:
					add("pred:ToughnessLEV", name)
				case kop.PredTotalPT:
					add("pred:TotalPT", name)
				case kop.PredBlocked:
					add("pred:Blocked", name)
				case kop.PredSolved:
					add("pred:Solved", name)
				case kop.PredAdventureCard:
					add("pred:AdventureCard", name)
				case kop.PredSuspected:
					add("pred:Suspected", name)
				case kop.PredTrigPlayerCtrl:
					add("pred:TrigPlayerCtrl", name)
				case kop.PredExiledWith:
					add("pred:ExiledWith", name)
				case kop.PredTriggerObj:
					add("pred:TriggerObj", name)
				case kop.PredWasCastEnter:
					add("pred:WasCastEnter", name)
				case kop.PredWasCastSpell:
					add("pred:WasCastSpell", name)
				case kop.PredNotF2:
					add("pred:NotF2", name)
				case kop.PredFaceDown:
					add("pred:FaceDown", name)
				case kop.PredWord7:
					add("pred:Word7", name)
				case kop.PredPowerGTBase:
					add("pred:PowerGTBase", name)
				case kop.PredPermMark:
					add("pred:PermMark", name)
				}
				for _, x := range f2Names {
					if f.Flags2&x.b != 0 {
						add("f2:"+x.l, name)
					}
				}
				val(f.PredV)
				id = f.Or
			}
		}
		val = func(v kop.ValueRef) {
			switch v.K {
			case kop.VCountFilter:
				filt(kop.FilterID(v.N))
			case kop.VExpr:
				add("v:Expr", name)
				e := pt.exprs[v.N]
				if n, ok := exNames[e.Kind]; ok {
					add("ex:"+n, name)
				}
				if n, ok := refNamesK[e.Ref]; ok {
					add("ref:"+n, name)
				}
				if n := ctrDocKey(e.Ctr); n != "" {
					add(n, name)
				}
				filt(e.F)
				val(e.Sub[0])
				val(e.Sub[1])
			}
		}
		var cond func(id kop.CondID)
		cond = func(id kop.CondID) {
			if id == 0 {
				return
			}
			k := pt.conds[id]
			if n, ok := condNamesK[k.Kind]; ok {
				add("cond:"+n, name)
			}
			if n, ok := refNamesK[k.Ref]; ok {
				add("ref:"+n, name)
			}
			if k.Kind == kop.CondAnd {
				cond(k.Sub[0])
				cond(k.Sub[1])
			}
			filt(k.F)
			val(k.A)
			val(k.B)
		}
		var abil func(ab *kop.Ability)
		abil = func(ab *kop.Ability) {
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostTapHost != 0 {
				add("cost:TapHost", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostTapPower != 0 {
				add("cost:TapPower", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostPayEnergy != 0 {
				add("cost:PayEnergy", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostReturnSelf != 0 {
				add("cost:ReturnSelf", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostReturn != 0 {
				add("cost:Return", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostExileSelf != 0 {
				add("cost:ExileSelf", name)
			}
			usagePutLib(ab.Cost, name, add)
			if ab.Cost.ExileHand {
				add("cost:ExileHand", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.ExileBf {
				add("cost:ExileBf", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Host == kop.CostHostExile {
				add("cost:HostExile", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.DiscardHand {
				add("cost:DiscardHand", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostOncePerTurn != 0 {
				add("cost:OncePerTurn", name)
			}
			if ab.Cost.Flags&kop.CostSubAmong != 0 {
				add("cost:SubAmong", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigAttacks && ab.Trig.N == kop.TrigNTraining {
				add("trig:Training", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigTaps && ab.Trig.N == kop.TrigNTeamworkTap {
				add("trig:TeamworkTap", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Flags3&kop.Tf3GameOnce != 0 {
				add("trig:GameOnce", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Flags3&kop.Tf3FirstAttack != 0 {
				add("trig:FirstAttack", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Flags4 != 0 {
				add("trigflag4", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbActivated && ab.Trig.Cond != 0 {
				add("ab:ActCond", name)
			}
			if n := ctrDocKey(ab.Cost.Ctr); n != "" {
				add(n, name)
			}
			filt(ab.Cost.Filter)
			for i := 0; i < int(ab.NTargets); i++ {
				t := ab.Targets[i]
				filt(t.Filter)
				if t.Min != 0 || t.Max != 0 {
					add("tgt:MinMax", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfKickedRange != 0 {
					add("tgt:Kicked", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfGiftRange != 0 {
					add("tgt:Gift", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfDistinct != 0 {
					add("tgf:Distinct", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfSameController != 0 {
					add("tgf:SameController", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfDiffController != 0 {
					add("tgf:DiffController", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfDecl != 0 {
					add("tgf:Decl", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfDeclSub != 0 {
					add("tgf:DeclSub", name)
				}
				if t.TFlags&kop.TgfSingleTgt != 0 {
					add("tgf:SingleTgt", name)
				}
				if t.Divide != 0 {
					add("tgt:Divide", name)
				}
				switch t.Kind {
				case kop.TgtStackObjTrig:
					add("tgt:StackObjTrig", name)
				case kop.TgtSpellTgting:
					add("tgt:SpellTgting", name)
				}
			}
			if ab.NModes > 0 {
				add("op:Charm", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfLatent != 0 {
				add("af:Latent", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfManaDynamic != 0 {
				add("af:ManaDynamic", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfManaChosen != 0 {
				add("af:ManaChosen", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfManaChoice != 0 {
				add("af:ManaChoice", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfResolveCount != 0 {
				add("af:ResolveCount", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfCheckOnTrigger != 0 {
				add("af:CheckOnTrigger", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfNinjutsu != 0 {
				add("af:Ninjutsu", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfStation != 0 {
				add("af:Station", name)
			}
			if ab.AFlags&kop.AfGift != 0 {
				add("af:Gift", name)
			}
			if ab.Gate.Ctr != 0 {
				add("ab:Gate", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigGiveGift {
				add("trig:GiveGift", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigFacesDilemma {
				add("trig:FacesDilemma", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigProliferate {
				add("trig:Proliferate", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigTokenCreated {
				add("trig:TokenCreated", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigBecomeMonstrous {
				add("trig:BecomeMonstrous", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigTurnFaceUp {
				add("trig:TurnFaceUp", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigAbilityCast {
				add("trig:AbilityCast", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigCommitCrime {
				add("trig:CommitCrime", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigManifestDread {
				add("trig:ManifestDread", name)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbTriggered && ab.Trig.Event == kop.TrigTransformed {
				add("trig:Transformed", name)
			}
			if ab.ManaRestrict != 0 {
				add("ab:ManaRestrict", name)
				filt(ab.ManaRestrict)
			}
			filt(ab.ManaRestrictAb)
			if ab.ActZone != 0 {
				add("ab:ActZone", name)
			}
			if ab.Exhaust {
				add("ab:Exhaust", name)
			}
			if ab.CantCopy {
				add("ab:CantCopy", name)
			}
			if ab.Evidence != 0 {
				add("ab:Evidence", name)
			}
			val(ab.ManaV)
			tr := ab.Trig
			filt(tr.Filter)
			if tr.Filter2 != 0 {
				add("trig:Filter2", name)
				filt(tr.Filter2)
			}
			if tr.Cond != 0 {
				add("trig:Cond", name)
				cond(tr.Cond)
			}
			if tr.Zone != 0 {
				add("trig:Zone", name)
			}
			if tr.N != 0 {
				add("trig:N", name)
			}
			for _, x := range []struct {
				b kop.TrigFlags2
				l string
			}{{kop.Tf2FirstTime, "FirstTime"}, {kop.Tf2YourTurn, "YourTurn"}, {kop.Tf2OppTurn, "OppTurn"}, {kop.Tf2NonCombat, "NonCombat"},
				{kop.Tf2ToOpponent, "ToOpponent"}, {kop.Tf2SelfOrFilter, "SelfOrFilter"}, {kop.Tf2CastSnapshot, "CastSnapshot"}, {kop.Tf2CastSpent, "CastSpent"}, {kop.Tf2NthSpell, "NthSpell"}, {kop.Tf2BlockedBySelf, "BlockedBySelf"}, {kop.Tf2TargetsFilter2, "TargetsFilter2"}, {kop.Tf2Alone, "Alone"}, {kop.Tf2AtkYou, "AtkYou"}, {kop.Tf2AtkYourPW, "AtkYourPW"}, {kop.Tf2AtkOpp, "AtkOpp"}, {kop.Tf2Batch, "Batch"}, {kop.Tf2PerPair, "PerPair"}, {kop.Tf2Cycled, "Cycled"}, {kop.Tf2CastFromHand, "CastFromHand"}, {kop.Tf2Convoked, "Convoked"}, {kop.Tf2Increment, "Increment"}} {
				if tr.Flags2&x.b != 0 {
					add("tf2:"+x.l, name)
				}
			}
			st := ab.Static
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbStatic {
				switch st.Kind {
				case kop.StatCDAPT:
					add("stat:CDAPT", name)
				case kop.StatNoMaxHandSize:
					add("stat:NoMaxHandSize", name)
				case kop.StatCombatDmgToughness:
					add("stat:CombatDmgToughness", name)
				case kop.StatExtraLandPlay:
					add("stat:ExtraLandPlay", name)
				case kop.StatUntapOther:
					add("stat:UntapOther", name)
				case kop.StatGoad:
					add("stat:Goad", name)
				case kop.StatCantTarget:
					add("stat:CantTarget", name)
				case kop.StatMayPlayFrom:
					add("stat:MayPlayFrom", name)
				case kop.StatOverride:
					add("stat:Override", name)
				case kop.StatPlayerHexproof:
					add("stat:PlayerHexproof", name)
				case kop.StatCantBeBeamedUp:
					add("stat:CantBeBeamedUp", name)
				case kop.StatBeamGrant:
					add("stat:BeamGrant", name)
				case kop.StatFbGrant:
					add("stat:FbGrant", name)
				case kop.StatWarpGrant:
					add("stat:WarpGrant", name)
				case kop.StatCantBeCast:
					add("stat:CantBeCast", name)
				case kop.StatCantGainLife:
					add("stat:CantGainLife", name)
				case kop.StatAnyTypeCreatures:
					add("stat:AnyTypeCreatures", name)
				case kop.StatCantDraw:
					add("stat:CantDraw", name)
				case kop.StatCantPreventDamage:
					add("stat:CantPreventDamage", name)
				case kop.StatCantPutCounter:
					add("stat:CantPutCounter", name)
				case kop.StatCantSacrifice:
					add("stat:CantSacrifice", name)
				case kop.StatCantPhaseIn:
					add("stat:CantPhaseIn", name)
				case kop.StatControl:
					add("stat:Control", name)
				case kop.StatPanharmonicon:
					add("stat:Panharmonicon", name)
				case kop.StatHexproofOwnColors:
					add("stat:HexproofOwnColors", name)
				case kop.StatCanAttackDefender:
					add("stat:CanAttackDefender", name)
				case kop.StatStackKw:
					add("stat:StackKw", name)
				case kop.StatAsIfHaste:
					add("stat:AsIfHaste", name)
				case kop.StatCantBeSuspected:
					add("stat:CantBeSuspected", name)
				}
				if st.Cond2 != 0 {
					add("st:Cond2", name)
					cond(st.Cond2)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StDynamic != 0 {
					add("st:Dynamic", name)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StEmbNum != 0 {
					add("st:EmbNum", name)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StTargetsFilter2 != 0 {
					add("st:TargetsFilter2", name)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StBargained != 0 {
					add("st:Bargained", name)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StReduceColor != 0 {
					if st.Kind == kop.StatMayPlayFrom {
						add("st:MayPayLife", name) // StMayPayLife aliases StReduceColor
					} else {
						add("st:ReduceColor", name)
					}
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StYouHexproof != 0 {
					add("st:YouHexproof", name)
				}
				if st.StFlags&kop.StPanhETB != 0 {
					if st.Kind == kop.StatIncreaseCost {
						add("st:RaiseLife", name) // StRaiseLife aliases StPanhETB
					} else {
						add("st:PanhETB", name)
					}
				}
				if st.Kind == kop.StatIncreaseCost && st.StFlags&kop.StRaisePerTarget != 0 {
					add("st:RaisePerTarget", name) // aliases StOncePerTurn
				}
				if st.StFlags&(kop.StRaiseYou|kop.StRaiseOpp) != 0 {
					add("st:RaiseYou", name)
				}
				if st.Grant != 0 {
					add("st:Grant", name)
				}
				if st.ProtFrom != 0 {
					add("st:ProtFrom", name)
				}
				if st.Landwalk != 0 {
					add("st:Landwalk", name)
				}
				if st.Zone != 0 {
					add("st:Zone", name)
				}
				kw(st.Kw)
				filt(st.Filter)
				filt(st.Filter2)
				filt(st.ProtFrom)
				filt(st.Landwalk)
				val(st.VA)
				val(st.VB)
			}
			if ab.Kind == kop.AbReplacement {
				switch ab.Repl.Kind {
				case kop.ReplEntersProgram:
					add("repl:EntersProgram", name)
				case kop.ReplOthersEnterProgram:
					add("repl:OthersEnterProgram", name)
				case kop.ReplCantLoseGame:
					add("repl:CantLoseGame", name)
				case kop.ReplOppsCantWinGame:
					add("repl:OppsCantWinGame", name)
				case kop.ReplDoubleDamageToOpps:
					add("repl:DoubleDamageToOpps", name)
				case kop.ReplDamagePlus:
					add("repl:DamagePlus", name)
				case kop.ReplPreventNoncombatToOthers:
					add("repl:PreventNoncombatToOthers", name)
				case kop.ReplPreventMillOpps:
					add("repl:PreventMillOpps", name)
				case kop.ReplPreventDamageCounters:
					add("repl:PreventDamageCounters", name)
				case kop.ReplDamageHealFirst:
					add("repl:DamageHealFirst", name)
				case kop.ReplDoubleTokens:
					add("repl:DoubleTokens", name)
				case kop.ReplCopyFirstToken:
					add("repl:CopyFirstToken", name)
				case kop.ReplAddToken:
					add("repl:AddToken", name)
				case kop.ReplDoubleCounters:
					add("repl:DoubleCounters", name)
				case kop.ReplGraveToLibrary:
					add("repl:GraveToLibrary", name)
				case kop.ReplDiscardOppToBattlefield:
					add("repl:DiscardOppToBattlefield", name)
				case kop.ReplPayBeforeETB:
					add("repl:PayBeforeETB", name)
				case kop.ReplExileOnLeave:
					add("repl:ExileOnLeave", name)
				case kop.ReplDoubleCountersOn:
					add("repl:DoubleCountersOn", name)
				case kop.ReplAddCountersOn:
					add("repl:AddCountersOn", name)
				case kop.ReplOnePoison:
					add("repl:OnePoison", name)
				case kop.ReplDoubleCountersYou:
					add("repl:DoubleCountersYou", name)
				case kop.ReplTurnUpProgram:
					add("repl:TurnUpProgram", name)
				case kop.ReplCantTurnUp:
					add("repl:CantTurnUp", name)
				case kop.ReplSpellsCantBeCountered:
					add("repl:SpellsCantBeCountered", name)
				}
				if ab.Repl.Cond != 0 || ab.Repl.Filter != 0 {
					add("repl:Cond", name)
				}
				cond(ab.Repl.Cond)
				filt(ab.Repl.Filter)
			}
			for _, in := range ab.Prog {
				if l, ok := kOp[in.Op]; ok {
					add(l, name)
				}
				if in.Op == kop.OpExt {
					add("ext:"+in.Ext().String(), name) // kop/ext.go sub-ops
				}
				if n, ok := refNamesK[in.Obj]; ok {
					add("ref:"+n, name)
				}
				filt(in.F)
				val(in.A)
				val(in.B)
				switch in.Op {
				case kop.OpSkipUnless:
					cond(kop.CondID(in.C))
				case kop.OpGrantKeyword:
					kw(kop.KwMask(uint16(in.C)) | kop.KwMask(uint16(in.B.N))<<16)
				case kop.OpPutCounter, kop.OpRemoveCounter, kop.OpRemoveCounterRem, kop.OpEnterWithCounters, kop.OpDoubleCounters:
					if n := ctrDocKey(kop.CounterKind(in.C)); in.C != 255 && n != "" {
						add(n, name)
					}
				case kop.OpCounter:
					if in.B.N&kop.CtrRemMV != 0 {
						add("op:CounterRemMV", name)
					}
				case kop.OpOverride:
					kw(pt.overrides[in.C].AddKw)
				case kop.OpCreateEmblem:
					for i := range pt.emblems[in.C].Abilities {
						abil(&pt.emblems[in.C].Abilities[i])
					}
				}
			}
		}
		kw(d.Keywords)
		filt(d.Enchant.Filter)
		filt(d.BestowTgt.Filter)
		filt(d.BeholdF)
		filt(d.WardSac)
		if d.WardLife != 0 {
			add("card:WardLife", name)
		}
		if d.WardEvidence != 0 {
			add("card:WardEvidence", name)
		}
		if d.BeholdN != 0 {
			add("cost:Behold", name)
		}
		if d.WardDiscard != 0 {
			add("card:WardDiscard", name)
		}
		if d.WardSac != 0 {
			add("card:WardSac", name)
		}
		if d.WardWaterbend != 0 {
			add("card:WardWaterbend", name)
		}
		if d.WardPoison != 0 {
			add("card:WardPoison", name)
		}
		if d.WardDiscOrN != 0 {
			add("card:WardDiscOrN", name)
		}
		if d.WardLifePower {
			add("card:WardLifePower", name)
		}
		if d.Daybound || d.Nightbound {
			add("card:Daybound", name)
		}
		if d.Leyline {
			add("card:Leyline", name)
		}
		if d.SelfFlash {
			add("card:SelfFlash", name)
		}
		if d.Landwalk != 0 {
			add("card:Landwalk", name)
		}
		filt(d.Landwalk)
		if d.HexColors != 0 {
			add("card:HexColors", name)
		}
		if d.ProtColors != 0 {
			add("card:ProtColors", name)
		}
		if d.Evasion != 0 {
			add("card:Evasion", name)
		}
		if d.MinBlockers != 0 {
			add("card:MinBlockers", name)
		}
		if d.ExtraBlocks != 0 {
			add("card:ExtraBlocks", name)
		}
		if d.HasMadness {
			add("card:Madness", name)
		}
		if d.HasMiracle {
			add("card:Miracle", name)
		}
		if d.Wither {
			add("card:Wither", name)
		}
		if d.AloneAtk {
			add("card:AloneAtk", name)
		}
		if d.AloneBlk {
			add("card:AloneBlk", name)
		}
		if d.Engines {
			add("card:Engines", name)
		}
		if d.TypedMana {
			add("card:TypedMana", name)
		}
		if d.Infect {
			add("card:Infect", name)
		}
		if d.Toxic != 0 {
			add("card:Toxic", name)
		}
		if d.Cascade != 0 {
			add("card:Cascade", name)
		}
		if d.ProtFrom != 0 {
			add("card:ProtFrom", name)
		}
		filt(d.ProtFrom)
		if d.SpellCost != (kop.Cost{}) {
			add("card:SpellCost", name)
		}
		if d.HasAltAdd {
			add("card:AltAddCost", name)
		}
		if d.RemPersist {
			add("card:RemPersist", name)
		}
		if d.ExiledWith {
			add("card:ExiledWith", name)
		}
		if d.CombatHitRec {
			add("card:CombatHitRec", name)
		}
		if d.SpendRead {
			add("card:SpendRead", name)
		}
		if d.BeamMeUp {
			add("card:BeamMeUp", name)
		}
		if d.FbCost.Flags != 0 {
			add("card:FbCost", name)
		}
		if d.Gift {
			add("card:Gift", name)
		}
		if d.Offspring {
			add("card:Offspring", name)
		}
		if d.Convoke {
			add("card:Convoke", name)
		}
		if d.Improvise {
			add("card:Improvise", name)
		}
		if d.Delve {
			add("card:Delve", name)
		}
		if d.Casualty != 0 {
			add("card:Casualty", name)
		}
		if d.Bargain {
			add("card:Bargain", name)
		}
		if d.Paradigm != 0 {
			add("card:Paradigm", name)
		}
		if d.OptCost.Flags != 0 || d.OptBehold || d.OptEvidence != 0 {
			add("card:OptCost", name)
		}
		for i := range d.Abilities {
			abil(&d.Abilities[i])
		}
	}
	return use
}

// writeOpsDoc renders OPS.md.
func writeOpsDoc(p *pool, pt *poolTables, all []*lCard, bs []built) []byte {
	use := opsUsage(pt, all, bs)
	deckUse := func(cs map[string]bool) int {
		n := 0
		for _, d := range p.decks {
			for _, c := range d {
				if cs[c] {
					n++
					break
				}
			}
		}
		return n
	}
	type row struct {
		e     opsDoc
		decks int
		cards []string
	}
	var rows []row
	for _, e := range opsEntries {
		cs := use[e.label]
		var names []string
		for c := range cs {
			names = append(names, c)
		}
		sort.Slice(names, func(i, j int) bool {
			a, b := p.nDecks[names[i]], p.nDecks[names[j]]
			if a != b {
				return a > b
			}
			return names[i] < names[j]
		})
		rows = append(rows, row{e, deckUse(cs), names})
	}
	sort.SliceStable(rows, func(i, j int) bool { return rows[i].decks > rows[j].decks })
	var b bytes.Buffer
	b.WriteString("# kop additions: interpreter contract\n\n")
	b.WriteString("The dirac interpreter's contract for the generated card tables.\n\n")
	b.WriteString("Generated by `go run ./dirac/cmd/kgen` (the usage columns come from this table; the semantics from\n")
	b.WriteString("dirac/kgen/opsdoc.go); do not edit. Every op, enum value and field dirac/kgen appended to\n")
	b.WriteString("dirac/kop, with the exact interpreter semantics, the decisions it implies and the cards that\n")
	b.WriteString("use it, ordered by the number of decks that need it (of " + fmt.Sprint(len(p.decks)) + "). Packed operand constants\n")
	b.WriteString("(PayKind, DamageFlags, MoveFlags, SearchFlags, DigFlags, DigUntilFlags, CopyFlags, TokenFlags,\n")
	b.WriteString("Duration) are in dirac/kop/table.go. \"Gorge\" names the gorge parameter or rule mirrored;\n")
	b.WriteString("where this says \"mirror gorge\" the oracle is the arbiter. An item with 0 decks is defined for a\n")
	b.WriteString("refused or token-only use and may be implemented last.\n\n")
	for _, r := range rows {
		fmt.Fprintf(&b, "## %s\n\n%s\n\n", r.e.title, r.e.text)
		if len(r.cards) == 0 {
			b.WriteString("Used by: no supported pool card.\n\n")
			continue
		}
		var cs []string
		for _, c := range r.cards {
			cs = append(cs, fmt.Sprintf("%s (%d)", c, p.nDecks[c]))
		}
		fmt.Fprintf(&b, "Decks: %d. Cards: %s.\n\n", r.decks, strings.Join(cs, ", "))
	}
	return b.Bytes()
}

// ctrDocKey is the ops-doc key of counter kind c: "ctr:New" for the
// appended featurized kinds, "ctr:Unfeat" for the kinds above CtrLevel.
func ctrDocKey(c kop.CounterKind) string {
	switch {
	case c == kop.CtrShield:
		return "ctr:Shield"
	case c >= kop.CtrCharge:
		return "ctr:Unfeat"
	case c >= kop.NumCounterKinds:
		return "ctr:New"
	}
	return ""
}

// usagePutLib records the PutCardToLibFromGrave self cost (a Cost byte, not a
// CostFlags bit).
func usagePutLib(c kop.Cost, name string, add func(label, card string)) {
	if c.PutLibSelf {
		add("cost:PutLibSelf", name)
	}
	if c.ExileGSelf {
		add("cost:ExileGSelf", name)
	}
}
